\par\par \b \uc2 LADYS Options on BIT Exchange paves new retail trading highway for meme coins\b0\par\par\uc2 Crypto Daily \par \uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 July 2023\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2023, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 DUBAI, DUBAI, July 6th, 2023, Chainwire\par \par \uc2 The options trading market gets another boost thanks to yet another collaboration between the cryptocurrency derivatives exchange BIT and the duo of Darley Technologies and DWF Labs.\par \par \uc2 Just recently, BIT rolled out options tied to Cardano's \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  token in collaboration with strategic partner Darley Technologies and market maker DWF Labs. Today, LADYS Options marks a significant milestone in the industry as the world's first Meme-coin Options brought to the market for both institutional and retail traders.\par \par \uc2 Options might be seen as an intimidating instrument for new traders or existing spot traders. This type of derivative gives the trader the right to buy or sell an underlying asset at a certain price on or before a specific date. The core functionalities of options are binary: the right to buy the asset is a call option, and the right to sell it is a put option.\par \par \uc2 "Our intention is to simplify access to options trading for all traders, providing an interface that is simple to understand and instruments that are in line with what communities are passionate about. Meme-coins are an excellent way to engage people to learn options trading" said Andrei Grachev, the Managing Partner of DWF Labs."We are proud to announce the listing of LADYS options as the world's first meme-coin options, made possible through the support of our esteemed partners, Darley Technologies and DWF Labs." Said Justin Buitendan, the Global Head of Institutional Sales of BIT, "Meme coins have experienced rapid growth, and we are thrilled to provide our clients with an additional avenue to enhance their trading strategies. LADYS options mark the starting point of an exciting journey, and there are more exciting opportunities on the horizon."\par \par \uc2 The incredible popularity of the LADYS token, as well as the sudden sprout of related projects, made it the perfect candidate for the first Meme-coin Option to be traded, thanks to the alliance between BIT, DWF Labs, and Darley Technologies.\par \par \uc2 About BIT\par \par \uc2 BIT is a full-featured cryptocurrency exchange that is designed for use by professionals, with advanced risk management and fund efficiency supported by Portfolio Margin and Unified Margin.\par \par \uc2 BIT was launched in August 2020 as an affiliate to Matrixport, a prominent crypto financial service company. BIT is one of the top crypto options trading platforms which offer innovative USD-margined trading pairs.\par \par \uc2 About Darley Technologies\par \par \uc2 Darley Technologies is a pioneering liquidity provider for options trading in the cryptocurrency space, with a mission to provide deep and reliable liquidity at competitive prices. Based in Zug, Switzerland, the heart of Europe\u8217\'20\'19s blockchain ecosystem, Darley Technologies brings together teams of highly experienced scientists, developers and traders to design and engineer the most advanced network infrastructures, technology and trading algorithms, enabling it to successfully execute its mission across multiple venues worldwide.\par \par \uc2 About DWF Labs\par \par \uc2 DWF Labs is a global \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  market maker and multi-stage web3 investment firm, providing support from token listing to market making to OTC trading solutions. DWF Labs seeks to invest and support bold founders who want to build the future of Web3.\par \par \uc2 DWF Labs is present in Singapore, Switzerland, South Korea, the BVI, and the UAE and trades almost 2,000 pairs with a daily volume that places DWF Labs among the top 5 ranking entities trading on the world\u8217\'20\'19s top 40 exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Website | Portfolio | \uc2 Linkedin\uc2  | \uc2 Twitter\uc2  | Telegram | Medium\par \par \uc2 ContactManaging Partner DWF LabsAndrei Grachevmedia@dwf-labs.com\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020230706ej76000gp\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 7/5: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , LTC, MATIC, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,723 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 July 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to resume the up move in Bitcoin and select altcoins indicates that bears remain active at higher levels.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin continues to trade near $31,000, making it an important resistance level to watch out for in the short term. Some analysts believe the current consolidation {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-analyst-32-5-k-launchpad-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could result in an upside breakout in Bitcoin}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The institutional investors also seem to be positive about the prospects of a further rally in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ). \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  head of research James Butterfill said in a recent report that 98% of all the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-primary-focus-investors-amid-year-highs-coinshares"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inflows of $334 million}}}\uc2  went into Bitcoin-related products.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/8ed30133-fa43-4d41-8637-18d81e8cde43.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-traders-hope-buy-dip-btc-price-toward-30k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 short-term price action on Bitcoin}}}\uc2  and select altcoins looks positive, market participants should stay cautious due to the uncertainty regarding macroeconomic issues. The crypto markets are likely to be influenced by the United States inflation figures and the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s monetary action over the next few weeks.\par \par \uc2 What are the important near-term support levels on Bitcoin and altcoins that need to hold for the recovery to continue? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin broke and closed above the $31,000 level on July 3, but the bulls could not build upon this strength. This suggests that the bears have not yet given up.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/1d20574d-94ce-4cf2-9454-3f6a618e924b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $29,673 is the important level to watch out for on the downside. If the price rebounds off this level, it will suggest that the bulls are buying the dips.\par \par \uc2 That will enhance the prospects of a break above the $31,000 to $31,432 overhead zone. The BTC/USDT pair may then rise to $32,400, where the bears may again pose a strong challenge.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will be negated in the near term if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day EMA. That could sink the pair to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of $27,849.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance at $2,000, indicating that the bears are actively guarding the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/a5d6b867-e783-4bda-ba63-0761f628938e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will have to sink and sustain the price below the moving averages to indicate that the ETH/USDT pair may continue its consolidation between $2,000 and $1,626 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the 20-day EMA ($1,876), it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying the dips. That will enhance the prospects of a break above $2,000. The pair may then soar to the $2,142 to $2,200 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers tried to stretch BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) recovery above the 20-day EMA ($245) on July 3, but the bears aggressively sold near the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $252.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/a1899a1f-df03-4ad1-95a7-4b18f156b8a6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price skidded back below the 20-day EMA on July 4, indicating that the bears remain active at higher levels. The flattish 20-day EMA and the relative strength index (RSI) in the negative territory indicate that the BNB/USDT pair may continue to oscillate between $257 and $220 for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above $257, it will suggest that the sentiment is gradually turning positive and the bulls are buying the dips. The positive momentum could pick up after buyers thrust the price above the $257 to $265 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears have held off the attempts by the bulls to drive and sustain XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) above the moving averages, indicating that higher levels continue to attract sellers.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/76550d5d-3a29-4f93-96cd-421adee68cab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to strengthen their position further by pulling the price below the immediate support at $0.44. If they can pull it off, the selling may intensify and the XRP/USDT pair could plunge to the strong support at $0.41.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the moving averages. That could open the doors for a potential rally to the $0.56 to $0.59 resistance zone, where the bears are expected to mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 The narrow range trading in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) resolved to the downside on July 5. This suggests that the short-term bulls have given up and are booking profits.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/7001bbfc-28a3-45cd-a72e-64131bdae952.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA ($0.29), the bears will try to sink the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair to $0.26. Such a move will suggest that the pair may remain stuck inside the $0.30 to $0.24 range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns up from the current level and breaks above $0.30, it will suggest the start of a sustained recovery. There might be a minor pit stop at the 50-day SMA ($0.32), but it is likely to be crossed. Above this level, the pair could surge toward $0.38.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls again tried to push and sustain Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance of $0.07 on July 4, but the bears held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/a477a239-e3aa-4c77-a8f6-8034498daf39.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($0.07) has started to turn up gradually, but the RSI has dipped to the midpoint, indicating that the positive momentum may be weakening. If the price breaks and sustains below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the DOGE/USDT pair may spend some more time inside the range between $0.06 and $0.07.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to gain the upper hand, they will have to propel and sustain the price above $0.07. That could start a recovery in the pair that could reach $0.08 and then $0.10.\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Solana\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) July 4 candlestick shows that the bears are strongly protecting the level. A minor positive in favor of the bulls is that they have not allowed the price to dip back below the immediate support at $18.70.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/9a59ca16-dd8f-4555-bd09-da576a840d9b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($17.87) has started to turn up and the RSI is in positive territory, indicating that buyers have the upper hand. The bulls will again try to overcome the barrier at the downtrend line. If they succeed, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair may jump to $22 and then to $24.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price continues lower and breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest the start of a deeper correction. The pair may then slump to the strong support zone between $16.18 and $15.28.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-2017-like-rally-again-dollar"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Can Bitcoin repeat a 2017-like rally as dollar correlation reverses?}}}\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down sharply from the overhead resistance of $115 and slipped below the breakout level of $106. This suggests the start of a corrective phase.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/fd257a1c-79ba-452f-814b-36f108af925e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 50% Fibonacci retracement level of $98 is an important support level to watch out for. A strong bounce off this level will be a positive sign, as it will show that traders are buying on dips. That will increase the likelihood of a retest of $115. If this resistance gives way, the LTC/USDT pair may resume its uptrend toward $136.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price breaks below $98, it will suggest that short-term traders may be booking profits. The pair may then dump to the 20-day EMA ($94). A deeper correction is likely to delay the resumption of the up move.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers pushed Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance of $0.69 on July 3, which completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  ascending triangle pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/be12dac0-0cc4-4b5b-95c1-d45bc028879e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls could not sustain the higher levels as the bears pulled the price back below the breakout level of $0.69.\par \par \uc2 If the price bounces off the current level and rises above $0.72, it will suggest the start of a new up move. The MATIC/USDT pair could then climb to the pattern target of $0.88. The 50-day SMA ($0.75) may act as a hurdle, but it is likely to be crossed.\par \par \uc2 The important support to watch on the downside is the uptrend line. A break below it may sink the pair to $0.56.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the overhead resistance of $5.56 on July 3, indicating that the bears are fiercely defending the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/153a7ec2-56e4-4d00-ab5a-21bb795ed1df.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The DOT/USDT pair has slipped to the immediate support at $5.15, which is an important level to keep an eye on. The moving averages are placed just below this support; hence, the bulls will try to start a recovery.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds sharply off $5.15, the pair may form an inverse head-and-shoulders pattern, which will complete on a break and close above $5.56. That could start a strong up move to the downtrend line and later to the pattern target of $6.90.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate in the near term if the price plummets below the moving averages. That could pull the pair to $4.74.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-07/3d17b9bd-eb5c-45ce-a9bb-9b249dd569c6.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230705ej75000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
