\par\par \b \uc2 Gemini\uc2  Eyes APAC Expansion, Crypto Daily TV 21/6/2023\b0\par\par\uc2 Amara Khatri \par \uc2 635 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 June 2023\par \uc2 CryptoDaily\par \uc2 CRPTOD\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 2023, CryptoDaily, All rights Reserved - Provided by SyndiGate Media Inc. \par \par \uc2 In Todays Headline TV CryptoDaily News:\par \par \uc2 Gemini\uc2  to expand in APAC\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchange \uc2 Gemini\uc2  plans to expand in Asia-Pacific, a region it sees as driving the \u8220\'20\'1Cnext wave of growth for crypto.\u8221\'20\'1D The expansion comes as \uc2 Gemini\uc2  tries to establish itself outside of the U.S., which this year has seen increased regulatory actions against crypto exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Cardano labeled a "security" by SEC\par \par \uc2 Cardano, one of the largest competitors of the Ethereum network, was recently labeled a \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity\u8221\'20\'1D by the \uc2 US Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 . The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown resulted in a steep decline in \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  price, and the altcoin has been struggling to wipe out its losses since June 5.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2 , SEC strike deal to keep US customer assets in country\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2 , the world's biggest cryptocurrency exchange, and Binance.US have entered into an agreement with the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  to ensure that U.S. customer assets remain in the United States until a sweeping lawsuit filed this month by the regulatory agency is resolved.\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD exploded 4.7% in the last session.\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin-Dollar pair rose 4.7% in the last session after gaining as much as 5.1% during the session. The ROC is giving a negative signal. Support is at 25975.3333 and resistance at 27501.3333.\par \par \uc2 The ROC is giving a negative signal.\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD exploded 2.7% in the last session.\par \par \uc2 The Ethereum-Dollar pair exploded 2.7% in the last session. The Ultimate Oscillator is giving a positive signal. Support is at 1688.841 and resistance at 1772.141.\par \par \uc2 The Ultimate Oscillator is currently in positive territory.\par \par \uc2 XRP/USD saw a minor dip of 0.2% in the last session.\par \par \uc2 The Ripple-Dollar pair corrected downwards in the last session, falling 0.2%. The Stochastic indicator is giving a negative signal. Support is at 0.4739 and resistance at 0.5078.\par \par \uc2 The Stochastic indicator is giving a negative signal.\par \par \uc2 LTC/USD exploded 3.5% in the last session.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Litecoin\uc2 -Dollar pair skyrocketed 3.5% in the last session. The Ultimate Oscillator is giving a positive signal. Support is at 75.631 and resistance at 78.671.\par \par \uc2 The Ultimate Oscillator is giving a positive signal.\par \par \uc2 Daily Economic Calendar:\par \par \uc2 UK Consumer Price Index\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Price Index is a measure of price movements made by comparing the retail prices of a representative shopping basket of goods and services. The UK's Consumer Price Index will be released at 06:00 GMT, the US Redbook Index at 12:55 GMT, the Belgian Consumer Confidence Index at 09:00 GMT.\par \par \uc2 US Redbook Index\par \par \uc2 The Johnson Redbook Index measures the year-over-year same-store sales growth from a sample of large general merchandise retailers.\par \par \uc2 BE Consumer Confidence Index\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Confidence captures the sentiment that individuals have regarding economic activity. A high level of consumer confidence indicates a stronger economy.\par \par \uc2 NL Consumer Confidence Adj\par \par \uc2 The Consumer Confidence is a leading index that measures the level of consumer confidence in economic activity. A high level of consumer sentiment is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the overall economy. The Dutch Consumer Confidence Adj will be released at 04:30 GMT, Japan's Foreign Investment in Japan Stocks at 23:50 GMT, Japan's Foreign Bond Investment at 23:50 GMT.\par \par \uc2 JP Foreign Investment in Japanese Stocks\par \par \uc2 Securities investment referrers to bonds issued in a domestic market by a foreign entity in the domestic market\u8217\'20\'19s currency.\par \par \uc2 JP Foreign Bond Investment\par \par \uc2 The Foreign Bond Investment refers to bonds issued in a domestic market by a foreign entity in the domestic market\u8217\'20\'19s currency.\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer: This article is provided for informational purposes only. It is not offered or intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, financial, or other advice.\par \par \uc2 Document CRPTOD0020230621ej6l000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/19: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , LTC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,731 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin is trying to stabilize near $26,500, and that may trigger buying in select altcoins.\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index (SPX) has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/06/15/stock-market-today-live-updates.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gained}}}\uc2  for five consecutive weeks, the first such instance since November 2021. In comparison, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is trading well below its local high of $31,000, made on April 14. This shows a clear divergence between the performance of the two asset classes.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts expect Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s range-bound action to continue for some more time. Cryptocurrency traders will be looking for some positive triggers that could push the price above the range. One such rumor floating in the markets is that after \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  filed for a Bitcoin spot exchange-traded fund, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-this-week-fear-26k-key-5-things"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fidelity Investments may also follow suit}}}\uc2 . If that happens, it will be a positive sign for the markets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/47e632f4-304d-48ea-8308-f5eaf2f528ae.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Another positive for the cryptocurrency markets has been that the U.S. Dollar Index (DXY) softened in the past week. Historically, the dollar and Bitcoin have an inverse correlation, which may help limit the downside in Bitcoin and launch a relief rally.\par \par \uc2 Let\u8217\'20\'19s look at the important resistance levels that need to be crossed to start a sustained recovery in Bitcoin and the major altcoins.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index is in a short-term uptrend. The rally of the past few days pushed the relative strength index (RSI) into the overbought territory, indicating that a minor correction or consolidation is possible.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/9ca161b2-a9ef-453a-8cf5-3ff9c76aaf3e.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The index could turn down and retest the breakout level of 4,325. If the price rebounds off this level, it will suggest that buyers have flipped 4,325 into support. That will enhance the prospects of a rally to 4,500 and thereafter to 4,650.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and breaks below the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of 4,283, it will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum is weakening. That could pull the index to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of 4,180. Below this level, the advantage may tilt in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The failure of the bulls to sustain the U.S. Dollar Index back above the 20-day EMA (103) on June 12 accelerated selling. That pulled the index back below the 50-day SMA (102) on June 15.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/3000f6d6-2878-4c80-8323-52b4642daae4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has started to turn down and the RSI is in negative territory, indicating that bears have the upper hand. Sellers will try to sink the price to the crucial support at 100.82. A break and close below this level will signal the resumption of the downtrend.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if buyers quickly push the price back above the moving averages, it will suggest that the index could rise to the downtrend line. Buyers will have to drive the price above this level to open the gates for a possible rally to 106.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been correcting inside the descending channel pattern for the past several weeks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/22cd7768-6dfa-413c-ba21-b4119c0bd8c3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA ($26,389) is flattening out and the RSI has climbed to the midpoint, indicating that the selling pressure could be reducing. Buyers will try to push the price to the resistance line of the channel. This is an important level for the bears to defend because a break and close above it could start a new up move.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down sharply from the current level, it will suggest that bears continue to sell on rallies. The BTC/USDT pair could then retest the strong support zone between $25,250 and $24,800.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) attempt to start a recovery is facing selling at the 20-day EMA ($1,766), but a minor positive is that the bulls have not allowed the price to slip back below $1,700.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/bb245a2c-778a-4c40-9111-01f30f1e3606.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from $1,700, the ETH/USDT pair will again attempt to rally above the 20-day EMA. If that happens, it will suggest that the short-term corrective phase may be over. The pair may first rise to $1,928 and subsequently to $2,000.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $1,700, it will indicate that bears remain in command. There is minor support at $1,600, but if this level gets taken out, the pair may plunge to $1,352.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) relief rally is facing selling at the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $252.50, but a positive sign is that the bulls have not given up much ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/17bc2097-65a1-4fae-b422-03019b4bbeb9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will again try to thrust the price above the overhead resistance zone between $252.50 and the 20-day EMA ($259). If they can pull it off, the BNB/USDT pair may climb to the 61.8% retracement level of $272.50. The bears are expected to fiercely protect this level.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance, it will suggest that the bears are not ready to give up their hold. The pair could then once again drop to the critical support at $220.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears repeatedly pulled XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) below the 50-day SMA ($0.47) between June 14 and 17, but they could not sustain the lower levels. This suggests buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/48713ecf-1566-437e-bf88-685a6b501b44.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are trying to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.49). If they achieve that, it will indicate that the XRP/USDT pair may swing between the 50-day SMA and $0.56 for some more time. The flattening 20-day EMA and the RSI near 50 also point to a possible consolidation in the short term.\par \par \uc2 If bears want to remain on top, they will have to quickly tug the price below $0.45. That could accelerate selling and sink the pair to $0.41.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to start a relief rally in Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) even though the RSI is at deeply oversold levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/4108fce2-2ac4-4a1e-8d2e-ca6c78d4267c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to sink the price to the vital support at $0.24. This is important support to keep an eye on because if it cracks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may skid to $0.22 and then extend the decline to $0.20.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are likely to have other plans. They will try to guard the zone between $0.24 and $0.22 with vigor. If the price turns up from this zone, it will suggest that the pair may consolidate between $0.24 and $0.30 for a while. The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA ($0.30).\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-cardano-price-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is Cardano price down today?}}}\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been trading inside a tight range between the 20-day EMA ($0.06) and the horizontal support at $0.06 for the past few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/511e17b4-8073-412e-8764-2c25ed22ab0a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The failure of the DOGE/USDT pair to rise above the 20-day EMA suggests that the sentiment remains negative and the bears are selling on every minor rally. That increases the risk of a break below the vital support at $0.06. If this level gives way, the pair may collapse to $0.05.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the 20-day EMA remains the key hurdle for the bulls to cross. If they sustain the price above this resistance, the pair could rally to $0.08. This level may pose a strong challenge to the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) is witnessing a tough battle near the $15.28 level. Buyers pushed the price above this level, but they have not been able to overcome the barrier at $16.18.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/eedb177e-403f-4008-bc19-575373c1043c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to sink the price below $15.28. If they do that, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could slide to $14.06 and later to the support at $12.80. This is an important level to watch out for because if it breaks down, the pair may tumble to $10.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break above the zone between $16.18 and the 20-day EMA ($17.03). That could clear the path for a potential retest of the breakdown level of $18.70. This level is likely to attract strong selling by the bears.\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls are trying to keep \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) above the immediate support at $75, which suggests that lower levels are being bought.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/a93650e7-232d-47c8-96e1-8dfe1c494066.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price to the overhead resistance at the 20-day EMA ($81). This level is likely to witness strong selling by the bears, as they will try to maintain their control. If the price turns down from the current level or the 20-day EMA, it will open the doors for a possible retest of the support zone between $75 and $70.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if bulls shove the price above the 20-day EMA, it will indicate that the bears may be losing their grip. The LTC/USDT pair could then rally to $90.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/9bfdc25d-9ae4-4b61-92ba-10eeae499c01.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230619ej6j000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Cryptocurrencies\par \b \uc2 Crypto investment products experience outflows for 9th consecutive week\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Judith BannermanQuist \par \uc2 508 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency investment products witnessed outflows amounting to $5.1 million last week, contributing to a cumulative total of $423 million in outflows over nine weeks.\par \par \uc2 On June 19, European cryptocurrency investment firm \uc2 CoinShares{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://blog.coinshares.com/volume-136-digital-asset-fund-flows-weekly-report-c6e2defdbf01"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 published}}}\uc2  its \u8220\'20\'1C\b \highlight22\uc2 Digital Asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  Fund Flows Report,\u8221\'20\'1D revealing that cryptocurrency investment products experienced outflows totaling $5.1 million last week. The outflows contributed to the continuation of a nine-week streak of outflows, resulting in a cumulative total of $423 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f46706ca-335f-499f-8878-57cedbcfd222.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Weekly crypto asset flows. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 The report noted that despite this downward trend, there was a glimmer of hope toward the end of the week, as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-apply-spot-bitcoin-etf-sec-nasdaq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 news emerged that BlackRock}}}\uc2 , one of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest asset managers, had submitted an application for a Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) exchange-traded product (ETP) in the United States. This development resulted in minor inflows; however, they were not significant enough to offset the earlier outflows observed during the week. As a consequence, the streak of outflows persisted.\par \par \uc2 Examining the regional breakdown, the U.S. and Germany experienced minor inflows of $3.7 million and $2.4 million, respectively. The U.S. maintained its lead in terms of total inflows year-to-date, accumulating $147 million, while Canada struggled with outflows amounting to $277 million. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 report author, James Butterfill, added, \u8220\'20\'1CDespite improving regulatory conditions in Hong Kong, we have not seen any measurable inflows into ETPs year-to-date while total assets under management (AuM) remain low at US$39m.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 , the previous week\u8217\'20\'19s crash in altcoin prices served as a catalyst for investors to increase their positions. Consequently, inflows totaling $2.4 million were observed. Noteworthy cryptocurrencies such as XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) were the focus of these inflows, receiving amounts of $1 million, $0.6 million and $0.2 million, respectively.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) experienced the largest outflows for the week, totaling $5 million. Additionally, both Tron ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tron-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 TRX}}}\uc2  ) and Avalanche ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/avalanche-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AVAX}}}\uc2  ) saw outflows of $0.4 million each. In a similar vein, \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  noted, \u8220\'20\'1CBlockchain equities saw the largest outflows since FTX, totalling $12.3m.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/grayscale-bitcoin-trust-2023-high-blackrock-etf-filing-buyers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Grayscale Bitcoin Trust nears 2023 highs on BlackRock ETF filing as buyers step up}}}\par \par \uc2 On June 15, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  applied for the first Bitcoin spot exchange-traded fund (ETF) in the United States. If approved, the ETF would provide investors with a regulated and accessible way to gain exposure to Bitcoin. Coinbase Custody Trust Company would be the custodian for the fund\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin holdings, while the \uc2 Bank of New York Mellon\uc2  would handle fiat assets. The ETF\u8217\'20\'19s Bitcoin price would be updated every 15 seconds based on the CF Benchmarks index. The approval of \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s application could have significant implications for the wider acceptance and adoption of cryptocurrency investment products in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/gary-genslers-job-at-risk-blackrocks-first-spot-bitcoin-etf-hodlers-digest-june-11-17/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Gary Gensler\u8217\'20\'19s job at risk, BlackRock\u8217\'20\'19s first spot Bitcoin ETF and other news: Hodler\u8217\'20\'19s Digest, June 11\u8211\'20\'1317}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/5077e012-7ab6-4bf7-a415-5511d3c9de87.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230619ej6j000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 cryptocurrency markets\par \b \uc2 Is the cryptocurrency market about to break its 10-week losing streak?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Marcel Pechman \par \uc2 796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph explores whether the crypto market is on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal.\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency total market capitalization fell to $1.02 trillion on June 15, its lowest level in three months. But while the derivatives market\u8217\'20\'19s resilience and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-26k-acceleration-binance-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end-of-week price gains}}}\uc2  amid uncertainty in stablecoins\u8217\'20\'19 reserves provide hope for bulls, it might be too soon to celebrate.\par \par \uc2 Crypto regulatory conditions deteriorate\par \par \uc2 The past few weeks have seen a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend fueled by regulatory uncertainty. Last week, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) saw 2.5% gains, but XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) dropped 5.2%, and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) traded down 0.7%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e327853f-e4f7-4847-a7ac-11a2ec1cdee0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market cap in USD, 1-day. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Notice that the 10-week-long pattern has tested the support level in multiple instances, signaling that bulls will have a hard time breaking from the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend while regulatory conditions have worsened across the globe.\par \par \uc2 For starters, New York-based {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bakkt-delists-cardano-solana-polygon-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derivatives exchange Bakkt is delisting}}}\uc2  Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) due to recent regulatory developments in the United States. The decision follows last week's lawsuits brought by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  against crypto exchanges \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-the-crypto-market-up-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the crypto market up today?}}}\par \par \uc2 More recently, on June 16, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-france-investigation-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance has been the subject of a preliminary investigation}}}\uc2  in France since February 2022. The France-based arm of the crypto exchange reportedly failed to obtain an operating license and illegally offered its services to French customers. Furthermore, the exchange lacked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-kyc-and-why-do-crypto-exchanges-require-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Know Your Customer}}}\uc2  procedures, according to regulators.\par \par \uc2 Also on June 16, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-crypto-exchange-exits-netherlands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance announced its departure from the Netherlands}}}\uc2 , with users being asked to withdraw their funds as soon as possible. The decision to exit the Dutch market occurred after the exchange failed to obtain a virtual asset service provider license.\par \par \uc2 Despite the worsening crypto regulatory environment, two derivatives metrics indicate that bulls are not yet throwing in the towel. Nevertheless, they'll likely have a hard time breaking the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price formation to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Derivatives show balanced demand for BTC, ETH leverage\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  contracts, also known as inverse swaps, have an embedded rate that is usually charged every eight hours.\par \par \uc2 A positive funding rate indicates that longs (buyers) demand more leverage. Still, the opposite situation occurs when shorts (sellers) require additional leverage, causing the funding rate to turn negative.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/0b56bdfc-abdd-4aaf-b2fd-86dcc1dd2f32.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  futures accumulated 7-day funding rate on June 17. Source: Coinglass\par \par \uc2 The seven-day funding rate for BTC and ETH is neutral, indicating balanced demand from leveraged longs (buyers) and shorts (sellers) using perpetual futures contracts.\par \par \uc2 BNB was the only exception, with traders paying up to 1% per week for short bets, which can be explained by the added risks after regulatory scrutiny over the Binance exchange.\par \par \uc2 Tether FUD hurts USDT premium\par \par \uc2 The Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) premium is a good gauge of China-based crypto retail trader demand. It measures the difference between China-based peer-to-peer trades and the United States dollar.\par \par \uc2 Excessive buying demand tends to pressure the indicator above fair value at 100%, and during \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Tether\u8217\'20\'19s market offer is flooded, causing a 2% or higher discount.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/3f00d847-c290-42f5-bfe3-7f826c8ff72c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether (USDT) peer-to-peer vs. USD/CNY. Source: OKX\par \par \uc2 The Tether premium in Asian markets fell to 99.2% after being flat since June 6, indicating moderate discomfort. Reports on June 16 regarding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/usdt-tether-responds-to-chinese-securities-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tether reserves\u8217\'20\'19 exposure to Chinese debt markets}}}\uc2  could have been the cause.\par \par \uc2 Potential market triggers\par \par \uc2 Derivatives metrics displayed resilience considering the strong regulatory activity aimed at crypto exchanges. Consequently, bears are yet to prove their strength if they intend to push crypto below the $1 trillion mark.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-key-ethereum-price-metrics-point-to-growing-resistance-at-1750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3 key Ether price metrics point to growing resistance at the $1,750 level}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite the most recent bounce from the support level, any gains above $1.12 trillion in capitalization (up 10% from the $1.02 trillion low) will likely be short-lived over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, with the Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/160k-halving-btc-price-prediction-model-count-down-new-bitcoin-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halving}}}\uc2  still over 300 days away, the bulls are currently pinning their hopes on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-bitcoin-etf-trust-good-or-bad-for-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin \b  \highlight22ETF approval\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and/or a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-analyst-believes-fed-will-favor-bulls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve rate cut}}}\uc2  as potential bull market catalysts.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b808a860-3b71-4443-8fd7-b4fa8a3ecf18.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230619ej6i00007\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 cryptocurrency markets\par \b \uc2 Is the cryptocurrency market about to break its 10-week losing streak?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Marcel Pechman \par \uc2 796 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph explores whether the crypto market is on the verge of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversal.\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency total market capitalization fell to $1.02 trillion on June 15, its lowest level in three months. But while the derivatives market's resilience and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-26k-acceleration-binance-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 end-of-week price gains}}}\uc2  amid uncertainty in stablecoins' reserves provides hope for bulls, it might be too soon to celebrate.\par \par \uc2 Crypto regulatory conditions deteriorate\par \par \uc2 The past few week have seen a \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend fueled by regulatory uncertainty. Last week, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  saw 2.5% gains, but {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  dropped 5.2%, and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) traded down 0.7%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e327853f-e4f7-4847-a7ac-11a2ec1cdee0.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market cap in USD, 1-day. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Notice that the 10-week long pattern has tested the support level in multiple instances, signaling that bulls will have a hard time breaking from the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend while regulatory conditions have worsened across the globe.\par \par \uc2 For starters, New York-based {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bakkt-delists-cardano-solana-polygon-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 derivatives exchange Bakkt is delisting}}}\uc2  Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) due to recent regulatory developments in the United States. The decision follows last week's lawsuits brought by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) against crypto exchanges Binance and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-the-crypto-market-up-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Why is the crypto market up today?}}}\par \par \uc2 More recently, on June 16, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-france-investigation-report"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance has been the subject of a preliminary investigation}}}\uc2  in France since February 2022. The France-based arm of the crypto exchange reportedly failed to obtain an operating license and illegally offered its services to French customers. Furthermore, the exchange lacked {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-is-kyc-and-why-do-crypto-exchanges-require-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Know-Your-Customer}}}\uc2  procedures, according to regulators.\par \par \uc2 Also on June 16, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-crypto-exchange-exits-netherlands"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance announced its departure from the Netherlands}}}\uc2 , with users being asked to withdraw their funds as soon as possible. The decision to exit the Dutch market occurred after the exchange failed to obtain a virtual asset service provider (VASP) license.\par \par \uc2 Despite the worsening crypto regulatory environment, two derivatives metrics indicate that bulls are not yet throwing in the towel. Nevertheless, they'll likely have a hard time breaking the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price formation to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Derivatives show balanced demand for BTC, ETH leverage\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  contracts, also known as inverse swaps, have an embedded rate that is usually charged every eight hours.\par \par \uc2 A positive funding rate indicates that longs (buyers) demand more leverage. Still, the opposite situation occurs when shorts (sellers) require additional leverage, causing the funding rate to turn negative.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/0b56bdfc-abdd-4aaf-b2fd-86dcc1dd2f32.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  futures accumulated 7-day funding rate on June 17. Source: Coinglass\par \par \uc2 The seven-day funding rate for BTC and ETH is neutral, indicating balanced demand from leveraged longs (buyers) and shorts (sellers) using perpetual futures contracts.\par \par \uc2 BNB was the only exception, with traders paying up to 1% per week for short bets, which can be explained by the added risks after regulatory scrutiny over the Binance exchange.\par \par \uc2 Tether FUD hurts USDT premium\par \par \uc2 The Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) premium is a good gauge of China-based crypto retail trader demand. It measures the difference between China-based peer-to-peer trades and the United States dollar.\par \par \uc2 Excessive buying demand tends to pressure the indicator above fair value at 100%, and during \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Tether\u8217\'20\'19s market offer is flooded, causing a 2% or higher discount.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/3f00d847-c290-42f5-bfe3-7f826c8ff72c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether (USDT) peer-to-peer vs. USD/CNY. Source: OKX\par \par \uc2 The Tether premium in Asian markets fell to 99.2% after being flat since June 6, indicating moderate discomfort. Reports on June 16 on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/usdt-tether-responds-to-chinese-securities-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tether reserves' exposure to Chinese debt markets}}}\uc2  could have been the cause.\par \par \uc2 Potential market triggers\par \par \uc2 Derivatives metrics displayed resilience considering the strong regulatory activity aimed at crypto exchanges. Consequently, bears are yet to prove their strength if they intend to push crypto below the $1 trillion mark.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/3-key-ethereum-price-metrics-point-to-growing-resistance-at-1750"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3 key Ether price metrics point to growing resistance at the $1,750 level}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite the most recent bounce from the support level, any gains above $1.12 trillion in capitalization (up 10% from the $1.02 trillion low) will likely be short-lived over the next few months.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, with the Bitcoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/160k-halving-btc-price-prediction-model-count-down-new-bitcoin-all-time-high"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 halving}}}\uc2  still over 300 days away, the bulls are currently pinning their hopes on a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-bitcoin-etf-trust-good-or-bad-for-btc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin \b  \highlight22ETF approval\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  and/or a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-analyst-believes-fed-will-favor-bulls"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Reserve rate cut}}}\uc2  as potential bull market catalysts.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b808a860-3b71-4443-8fd7-b4fa8a3ecf18.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230618ej6i0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market up today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Yashu Gola \par \uc2 548 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market is up today as traders assess its oversold levels and news \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  is filing for a \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The crypto market is up today, continuing gains from the Friday due to a mix of technical and fundamental factors.\par \par \uc2 Oversold bounce across top crypto market assets\par \par \uc2 On June 17, the crypto market's capitalization grew by over 2% to $1.05 trillion, up nearly 7.5% from the $975.25 billion low seen two days ago.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e474e50a-3b4b-4fb3-b642-8b8eea4434da.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL daily performance chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), which now comprises {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-closer-51-attack-altcoin-cryptocurrency-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nearly 50% of the crypto market}}}\uc2 , rebounded 8.5% from June 15 lows of $24,750.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the second-largest cryptocurrency Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), is up over 9% in the past two days. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-the-crypto-market-down-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Last week's worst performers}}}\uc2 , Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), and Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), also recovered 8-15% in the same period.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b3483aad-6101-45d8-92df-c1d7736e5ca6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Top 15 cryptocurrencies are up sharply in the last 24 hours. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 Interestingly, the crypto market cap started recovering a day after its daily {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/here-s-3-ways-the-relative-strength-index-rsi-can-be-used-as-a-sell-signal"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 relative strength index's (RSI)}}}\uc2  reading fell almost to 30, indicating its nearly "oversold."\par \par \uc2 From a technical perspective, an oversold RSI prompts a price recovery or consolidation, as shown below.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/fc47ed76-313c-49ea-baf3-ee9fd8d37f47.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL daily market performance. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Blackrock\uc2 's \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  buzz\par \par \uc2 In addition to the technical bounce, growing speculations around the first \uc2 Bitcoin \b \highlight22\uc2 ETF\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2  approval\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. helped the crypto market bounce.\par \par \uc2 Notably, \uc2 BlackRock\uc2 , an investment firm managing $9.5 trillion in assets, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/blackrock-apply-spot-bitcoin-etf-sec-nasdaq"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 applied}}}\uc2  to the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) for a \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  on July 16. Throughout its history, the company has applied for 576 ETFs, facing only one rejection.\par \par \uc2 The crypto market has risen 4.5% since the \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  application, with market analyst Lark Davis {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/TheCryptoLark/status/1669751744182779904"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 predicting}}}\uc2  a SEC approval could have the asset manager purchase every single Bitcoin available across crypto exchanges.\par \par \uc2 Excerpts from Davis's statement:\par \par \uc2 "Only about 10% of all Bitcoin [worth $50 billion] is sitting on exchanges. 0.5% of \uc2 BlackRock\uc2  money movings to BTC would buy every single coin available."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-26k-acceleration-binance-fears"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price eyes $26K \u8216\'20\'18acceleration\u8217\'20\'19 zone as Binance fears fade}}}\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the SEC has rejected all \uc2 Bitcoin ETF\uc2  applications, including those from asset managers like \uc2 VanEck\uc2 , Ark Invest, and Bitwise.\par \par \uc2 Crypto market outlook for H2 2023\par \par \uc2 From a technical perspective, the crypto market has ranged inside what appears to be a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-is-a-bull-flag-chart-pattern-and-how-to-spot-it"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bull flag pattern}}}\uc2  since April 2023, which raises its prospects of continuing its recovery trend toward $1.37 trillion into the second half of 2023 \u8212\'20\'14 up 35% from current valuations.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e2f6c448-509a-4b93-8b4e-6d0e36374382.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 TOTAL weekly performance chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Conversely, bears will attempt to push the market cap below the bull flag's lower trendline, risking invalidating the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup altogether.\par \par \uc2 In this \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  scenario, the crypto market would drop toward the next major support at $875.50 billion, an important level from the June-November 2022 and March 2023 sessions.\par \par \uc2 The views and opinions expressed here are solely those of the author and do not necessarily reflect the views of Cointelegraph. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and you should conduct your own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-10/a633230d-3f9a-4749-8bab-017c4b9435a0.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230617ej6h0008d\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 eToro\par \b \uc2 Crypto Biz: Crypto outflows surge, a16z\u8217\'20\'19s UK office, and the silent altcoins ban\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By     Ana Paula Pereira \par \uc2 842 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The combination of escalating interest rates and a tight regulatory environment in the United States forces crypto companies to rethink and adapt their business strategies.\par \par \uc2 A combination of escalating interest rates and a tight regulatory environment in the United States has driven a $417 million outflow from the crypto industry in the past eight weeks, with halts in trading for many altcoins draining liquidity and prolonging the ongoing crypto winter.\par \par \uc2 This environment is forcing crypto companies to rethink and adapt their business strategies.\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchange \uc2 Binance\uc2 , for instance, is moving forward with efforts to diversify its sources of revenue amid legal challenges with regulators. The company is {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-launches-bitcoin-mining-cloud-services-amid-sec-crackdown-in-the-us"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 launching a new subscription-based cloud mining product}}}\uc2  dedicated to Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), allowing users without equipment to purchase Bitcoin hash rates via \uc2 Binance\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s cloud mining service.\par \par \uc2 Also taking a new direction is venture capital firm \uc2 Andreessen Horowitz\uc2  (a16z), opening its first office outside the U.S. in London, United Kingdom. \uc2 Chris Dixon\uc2 , a16z\u8217\'20\'19s managing partner, cited a \u8220\'20\'1Cpredictable business environment\u8221\'20\'1D as one of the main factors behind the decision. U.K. Prime Minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  attributed the expansion to having the \u8220\'20\'1Cright \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and guardrails\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cfoster innovation\u8221\'20\'1D while protecting consumers.\par \par \uc2 According to the Sovereign Wealth Fund Institute, a16z is the largest venture capital firm in the world, with $35.8 billion in assets under management. With this move, the company joins many other crypto businesses setting up operations in more friendly regulatory environments outside the United States.\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s Crypto Biz looks at crypto markets outflows, a16z\u8217\'20\'19s first branch outside the U.S., the ongoing silent ban on altcoins, and the AI models to be first deployed in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 \u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0BCrypto fund outflows reach $417 million over eight weeks as investor caution persists\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 latest weekly report revealed that cryptocurrency investment products {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-fund-outflows-reach-417m-over-8-weeks-as-investor-caution-persists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced outflows of $88 million last week}}}\uc2 . With the substantial drawdown, the outflow streak has reached eight weeks, totaling $417 million. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  analysts attribute this ongoing trend to monetary policy considerations, prompting investors to remain cautious about digital assets. In the past week, Ether products witnessed $36 million of outflows, marking the largest weekly outflows for the asset since the Ethereum Merge in September 2022. Meanwhile, Bitcoin investment products saw outflows totaling $52 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b36f617d-fe9f-4c17-883d-8398072d3316.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products have seen a substantial drawdown over the past two months. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 A16z\uc2  opening London crypto office, citing \u8216\'20\'18predictable\u8217\'20\'19 environment\par \par \uc2 Venture capital firm a16z will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/a16z-open-london-office-international-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open its first office outside of the U.S.}}}\uc2  this year, adding to the backdrop of U.S.-based firms seeking greener pastures outside the country. The decision was finalized after a \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D with the U.K. prime minister and \u8220\'20\'1Cmonths of constructive conversations\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 His Majesty\u8217\'20\'19s Treasury\uc2 , policymakers, and the \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2 . Aside from the new office, a16z has announced its plan to launch a new Crypto Startup School (CSS) program in London in the spring of 2024. The most recent CSS program received more than 8,000 applicants, with 26 companies receiving an investment from a16z.\par \par \uc2 EToro\uc2  halts ALGO, MANA, MATIC and DASH purchases for U.S. customers\par \par \uc2 Trading platform \uc2 eToro\uc2  has halted purchases of Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) for U.S. customers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/etoro-algo-mana-matic-dash-purchases-us-customers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response to the tokens being labeled as securities}}}\uc2  in recent lawsuits from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  in the country. The move came just a few days after competitor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/robinhood-will-end-support-for-3-tokens-named-in-sec-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robinhood also halted support}}}\uc2  for MATIC, along with Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), two other cryptocurrencies deemed as securities by the regulator. Although the assets are officially delisted, eToro US users can still hold and sell these tokens. The firm said it remains a \u8220\'20\'1Csupporter\u8221\'20\'1D of the crypto industry and suggested that the move was purely to avoid any potential regulatory noncompliance.\par \par \uc2 eToro\uc2  has a framework in place which reviews the cryptoassets we offer in light of the rapidly evolving regulatory landscape. Due to recent developments, we will be making some changes to our crypto offering for US customers. (1/5)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 eToro US (@eToroUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eToroUS/status/1668323755435622405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 UK to get \u8220\'20\'1Cearly or priority access\u8221\'20\'1D to AI models from \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 OpenAI\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  recently announced that \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2 , \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and Anthropic \u8212\'20\'14 three tech outfits widely considered the global industry leaders in generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies \u8212\'20\'14 have agreed to provide the U.K. with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uk-to-get-early-or-priority-access-to-ai-models-from-google-and-openai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early access to their AI models}}}\uc2 . Sunak made the announcement during a speech opening London Tech Week, disclosing a three-part plan for AI systems deployment. The prime minister didn\u8217\'20\'19t clarify whether the U.K. would obtain earlier access to production models than the general public or contractors, or if the commitment was simply to offer access to the government and other priority researchers.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Biz is your weekly pulse of the business behind blockchain and crypto, delivered directly to your inbox every Thursday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b97387eb-027f-4c8e-8a73-463af1d26dda.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230617ej6g0002z\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 eT