xpansion to having the \u8220\'20\'1Cright \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and guardrails\u8221\'20\'1D to \u8220\'20\'1Cfoster innovation\u8221\'20\'1D while protecting consumers.\par \par \uc2 According to the Sovereign Wealth Fund Institute, a16z is the largest venture capital firm in the world, with $35.8 billion in assets under management. With this move, the company joins many other crypto businesses setting up operations in more friendly regulatory environments outside the United States.\par \par \uc2 This week\u8217\'20\'19s Crypto Biz looks at crypto markets outflows, a16z\u8217\'20\'19s first branch outside the U.S., the ongoing silent ban on altcoins, and the AI models to be first deployed in the United Kingdom.\par \par \uc2 \u8203\'20\'0B\u8203\'20\'0BCrypto fund outflows reach $417 million over eight weeks as investor caution persists\par \par \uc2 CoinShares\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 latest weekly report revealed that cryptocurrency investment products {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-fund-outflows-reach-417m-over-8-weeks-as-investor-caution-persists"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 experienced outflows of $88 million last week}}}\uc2 . With the substantial drawdown, the outflow streak has reached eight weeks, totaling $417 million. \uc2 CoinShares\uc2  analysts attribute this ongoing trend to monetary policy considerations, prompting investors to remain cautious about digital assets. In the past week, Ether products witnessed $36 million of outflows, marking the largest weekly outflows for the asset since the Ethereum Merge in September 2022. Meanwhile, Bitcoin investment products saw outflows totaling $52 million.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b36f617d-fe9f-4c17-883d-8398072d3316.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products have seen a substantial drawdown over the past 2 months. Source: \uc2 CoinShares\par \par \uc2 A16z\uc2  opening London crypto office, citing \u8216\'20\'18predictable\u8217\'20\'19 environment\par \par \uc2 Venture capital firm a16z will {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/a16z-open-london-office-international-expansion"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 open its first office outside of the U.S.}}}\uc2  this year, adding to the backdrop of U.S.-based firms seeking greener pastures outside the country. The decision was finalized after a \u8220\'20\'1Cproductive dialogue\u8221\'20\'1D with the U.K. prime minister and \u8220\'20\'1Cmonths of constructive conversations\u8221\'20\'1D with \uc2 His Majesty\u8217\'20\'19s Treasury\uc2 , policymakers, and the \uc2 Financial Conduct Authority\uc2 . Aside from the new office, a16z has announced its plan to launch a new Crypto Startup School (CSS) program in London in the spring of 2024. The most recent CSS program received more than 8,000 applicants, with 26 companies receiving an investment from a16z.\par \par \uc2 EToro\uc2  halts ALGO, MANA, MATIC and DASH purchases for U.S. customers\par \par \uc2 Trading platform \uc2 eToro\uc2  has halted purchases of Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) for U.S. customers in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/etoro-algo-mana-matic-dash-purchases-us-customers"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 response to the tokens being labeled as securities}}}\uc2  in recent lawsuits from the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  in the country. The move came just a few days after competitor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/robinhood-will-end-support-for-3-tokens-named-in-sec-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robinhood also halted support}}}\uc2  for MATIC, along with Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), two other cryptocurrencies deemed as securities by the regulator. Although the assets are officially delisted, eToro US users can still hold and sell these tokens. The firm said it remains a \u8220\'20\'1Csupporter\u8221\'20\'1D of the crypto industry and suggested that the move was purely to avoid any potential regulatory noncompliance.\par \par \uc2 eToro\uc2  has a framework in place which reviews the cryptoassets we offer in light of the rapidly evolving regulatory landscape. Due to recent developments, we will be making some changes to our crypto offering for US customers. (1/5)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 eToro US (@eToroUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eToroUS/status/1668323755435622405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 UK to get \u8220\'20\'1Cearly or priority access\u8221\'20\'1D to AI models from \uc2 Google\uc2  and \uc2 OpenAI\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Rishi Sunak\uc2  recently announced that \uc2 Google DeepMind\uc2 , \uc2 OpenAI\uc2  and Anthropic \u8212\'20\'14 three tech outfits widely considered the global industry leaders in generative artificial intelligence (AI) technologies \u8212\'20\'14 have agreed to provide the U.K. with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/uk-to-get-early-or-priority-access-to-ai-models-from-google-and-openai"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 early access to their AI models}}}\uc2 . Sunak made the announcement during a speech opening London Tech Week, disclosing a three-part plan for AI systems deployment. The prime minister didn\u8217\'20\'19t clarify whether the U.K. would obtain earlier access to production models than the general public or contractors, or if the commitment was simply to offer access to the government and other priority researchers.\par \par \uc2 Crypto Biz is your weekly pulse of the business behind blockchain and crypto, delivered directly to your inbox every Thursday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b97387eb-027f-4c8e-8a73-463af1d26dda.jpeg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230616ej6g000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 What happened in crypto\par \b \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Kyle White \par \uc2 902 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 A lot happened in crypto today! Cointelegraph explores the latest events impacting Bitcoin price, altcoins, DeFi, Web3, NFTs and more.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today. The markets continued with volatile movements that decoupled the price action of cryptocurrencies from equities markets. The recent downturn in the crypto market appears connected to the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s June 14 presser where Fed Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  revealed that the central bank would pause rate hikes for June.\par \par \uc2 While this move aligned with investors\u8217\'20\'19 expectations, the crypto market actually reversed course and resumed the sell-off that has been in play for the past three weeks.\par \par \uc2 In the press conference after the June 14 announcement, Powell {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/mediacenter/files/FOMCpresconf20230614.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated}}}\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CNearly all Committee participants view it as likely that some further rate increases will be appropriate this year to bring inflation down to 2 percent over time.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price started June 16, trading above $25,000, but then briefly retracted below $25,000. Analysts correctly predicted that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-bitcoin-resistance-to-retesting-25-k-support-is-futile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop to $25,000}}}\uc2  was inevitable based on the current state of BTC derivatives data. Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dip below $25,000 happened for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-btc-dips-below-25k-first-time-3-months"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 first time in 3-months}}}\uc2  but has since regained the key price level.\par \par \uc2 Following Powell\u8217\'20\'19s interest rate pause, options data on June 15 highlighted potential {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fed-pauses-interest-rates-but-bitcoin-options-data-still-points-to-btc-price-downside"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC price downside}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/a6d4badd-cc71-4e8c-8287-64a9e3b11182.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market performance, 1-day chart. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 The muted crypto price action and lack of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  response to the rate hike pause could be the lingering effect of the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges against Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-coinbase-crypto-industry-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase exchange}}}\uc2  coupled with new Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) drama.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/coldie-snoop-dogg-piece-vitalik-buterin-john-mcafee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Holy shit, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen that!\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Coldie\u8217\'20\'19s Snoop Dogg, Vitalik and McAfee NFTs}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto sector \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still the main threat\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/5-key-highlights-sec-lawsuit-binance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22Regulation\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  has been a constant in the recent cryptocurrency news cycle. While the EU unveiled a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/eu-s-new-crypto-law-how-mica-can-make-europe-a-digital-asset-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22digital asset\b0 \highlight22  framework}}}\uc2 , MiCA, the United States seems intent to regulate through SEC enforcement.\par \par \uc2 On June 5 and June 6, the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  filed civil lawsuits against two of the largest centralized exchanges in crypto, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase}}}\uc2 . The SEC claims that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 61 different cryptocurrencies}}}\uc2 , representing $100 billion in value, are securities.\par \par \uc2 One of the 61 crypto tokens listed was Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), a token that in 2019, Gensler called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/video-of-sec-chair-praising-algorand-resurfaces-after-recently-deeming-it-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great technology}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D which seems to contradict this latest enforcement action.\par \par \uc2 Other top crypto tokens specifically mentioned as securities include \uc2 Binance\uc2  USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ) and COTI.\par \par \uc2 The recent SEC action adds to a long history of disputes, misconceptions or mistrust over the actual use case of digital assets. After the \uc2 FTX\uc2  implosion, some feel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-poked-the-bear-and-the-bear-is-pissed-o-leary-on-the-crypto-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. lawmakers}}}\uc2  are angry with the crypto industry. The most recent battle is centered on how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/centralized-cryptocurrency-exchanges-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centralized exchanges}}}\uc2  can use customer funds.\par \par \uc2 Not all lawmakers are comfortable with Gensler\u8217\'20\'19s actions. United States Rep. Warren Davidson (OH) introduced the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-us-lawmakers-file-sec-stabilization-act-to-fire-gary-gensler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC Stabilization Act}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D into the House of Representatives on June 12. The bill would remove Gensler as Chair and redistribute power amongst a committee.\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has also filed a lawsuit against the SEC to call for clarity on cryptocurrencies. In a response on June 14, the SEC said it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-120-days-respond-coinbase-crypto-clarity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take 120 days}}}\uc2  for the commission to make a recommendation on crypto rulemaking.\par \par \uc2 Crypto investors take shelter in stablecoins\par \par \uc2 The ongoing crypto market \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sent users to seek {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-traders-avoid-risk-and-shelter-in-stablecoins-as-the-market-reaches-a-turning-point"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 shelter in stablecoins}}}\uc2 . Since the start of 2023, over 500,000 wallet addresses have added Tether.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/98610008-bc01-43e4-90b5-bd88df6de6a1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether non-zero addresses. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 Tether\u8217\'20\'19s dominance has led t an all-time high market capitalization of over $83.5 billion on June 15. While the stablecoin issuer has minted $16 billion in USDT in 2023 alone, a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/tether-billion-usdt-mint-on-ethereum-for-chain-swaps"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 single $1 billion}}}\uc2  mint on June 12 led to Tether\u8217\'20\'19s chief technology officer \uc2 Paolo Ardoino\uc2  having to clarify that the mint was for cross-chain swaps.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d220b2d7-1444-4f75-9f50-f2d7e6bc0a48.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether marketcap. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/curve-pool-imbalance-usdt-depeg-concerns-tether-cto-calls-it-fud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tether CTO}}}\uc2  was in the news again on June 15 after USDT slightly de-pegged by 0.3%. The loss of the dollar peg seemed to be triggered by the Curve 3pool imbalance which saw USDT weighted at 73.8% vs USD Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ) and Dai ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dai-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DAI}}}\uc2  ). Despite the de-peg Tether remains convinced that it can redeem any amount required by market participants.\par \par \uc2 Markets are edgy in these days, so it's easy for attackers to capitalize on this general sentiment.\par \par \uc2 But at Tether we're ready as always. Let them come.\par \par \uc2 We're ready to redeem any amount.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Paolo Ardoino\uc2  (@paoloardoino) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/paoloardoino/status/1669223742831042562?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 15, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-metrics-similarities-2020-breakout"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 3 Bitcoin price metrics showing \u8216\'20\'18insane\u8217\'20\'19 similarities to 2020 breakout}}}\par \par \uc2 With heavy macro headwinds, upcoming rate hikes and low volume, it is likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in crypto will remain for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/78d78761-3bd2-4569-96a7-62a97f0a1b0a.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230615ej6f000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin price\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin dips below $25K for the first time in 3 months\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Tom Mitchelhill \par \uc2 538 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The price of Bitcoin plummeted 4% in the hours following the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move to pause interest rates. While the market expected a pause, the Fed hinted at more rate hikes in the near future.\par \par \uc2 The price of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has fallen below the $25,000 mark for the first time since March 17 following a hawkish Fed announcement amid another turbulent week for the crypto industry.\par \par \uc2 Within the span of 30 minutes on June 15, the price of Bitcoin fell 4% from $25,867 to $24,819, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from TradingView. At the time of publication, Bitcoin had regained ground and was holding just above $25,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/13e9265d-9b18-4748-8eb5-418115f16bff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price from June 12 to June 15. Source: TradingView.\par \par \uc2 Over the past week, Bitcoin had been holding around the $26,000 region as the market came to grips with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/binance-coinbase-head-to-court-and-the-sec-labels-67-crypto-securities-hodlers-digest-june-4-10/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\u8217\'20\'19s legal action against}}}\uc2  crypto exchange heavyweights \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2 , as well as increasing macroeconomic uncertainty around interest rate signals from the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sharp drop in price arrived roughly three hours after the \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20230614a.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a pause on interest rate hikes following a 15-month-long campaign of rate increases to combat surging inflation.\par \par \uc2 While the market {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-rejects-cpi-boost-market-fed-rate-pause-odds-near-95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was almost unanimously expecting}}}\uc2  a rate pause, the Federal Open Markets Committee statement hinted at further rate hikes in the future, which typically blunts investor excitement for risk assets like cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 eToro\uc2  market analyst Josh Gilbert, Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  has made it quite clear that this is only a temporary pause, something that could spell further trouble for Bitcoin in the long term.\par \par \uc2 "Much of the positivity we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen from risk assets this year, including Bitcoin, is built on the expectation that inflation will fall and interest rates will peak, and then begin to be cut," Gilbert said.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is moving in the right direction but the comments from \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  signify that rates could stay higher for longer, which would put Bitcoin on the back foot."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-cpi-and-a-strong-rebound-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC, CPI and a \u8216\'20\'18strong rebound\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 5 things to know in Bitcoin this week}}}\par \par \uc2 The second largest cryptocurrency by market cap, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), also took a hit, falling more than 5% from $1,727 to $1,631 in the same time frame. Altcoins were not spared from the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment either, with many of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tokens labeled as securities}}}\uc2  in the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits stumbling another than 3%.\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is currently down 3.4% in the last 24 hours, while Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) fell 3.3% and 2.8% respectively.\par \par \uc2 According to Cointelegraph analyst Marcel Pechman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fed-pauses-interest-rates-but-bitcoin-options-data-still-points-to-btc-price-downside"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current options data for Bitcoin}}}\uc2  suggests a further slide to the downside, especially when considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/big-week-for-crypto-here-s-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the regulatory hostility}}}\uc2  towards the crypto industry on U.S. soil combined with the likelihood of further rate increases from the Fed in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/bitcoin-net-zero-2050-climate-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin is on a collision course with \u8216\'20\'18Net Zero\u8217\'20\'19 promises}}}\par \par \uc2 Update (June 15, 1:40am UTC): This article has been updated to include comments from \uc2 eToro\uc2  market analyst Josh Gilbert.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b3ef6494-52ca-40bd-85b6-fcf0357568e4.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230615ej6f00032\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin price\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin dips below $25K for the first time in 3 months\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Tom Mitchelhill \par \uc2 534 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The price of Bitcoin plummeted 4% in the hours following the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s move to pause interest rates. While the market expected a pause, the Fed hinted at more rate hikes in the near future.\par \par \uc2 The price of Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) has fallen below the $25,000 mark for the first time since March 17 following a hawkish Fed announcement amidanother turbulent week for the crypto industry.\par \par \uc2 Within the span of 30 minutes on June 15, the price of Bitcoin fell 4% from $25,867 to $24,819 according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.tradingview.com/symbols/BTCUSD/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from TradingView. At the time of publication Bitcoin has regained ground and is holding just above $25,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/13e9265d-9b18-4748-8eb5-418115f16bff.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price from June 12 to June 15. Source: TradingView.\par \par \uc2 Over the past week Bitcoin had been holding around the $26,000 region as the market came to grips with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/binance-coinbase-head-to-court-and-the-sec-labels-67-crypto-securities-hodlers-digest-june-4-10/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC\u8217\'20\'19s legal action against}}}\uc2  crypto exchange heavyweights \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and Binance as well as increasing macroeconomic uncertainty around interest rate signals from the \uc2 United States Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The sharp drop in price arrived roughly three hours after the \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20230614a.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced}}}\uc2  a pause on interest rate hikes, following a fifteen-month-long campaign of rate increases to combat surging inflation.\par \par \uc2 While the market {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-rejects-cpi-boost-market-fed-rate-pause-odds-near-95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was almost unanimously expecting}}}\uc2  a rate pause, the Federal Open Markets Committee statement hinted at further rate hikes in the future, which typically blunts investor excitement for risk assets like cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 eToro\uc2  Market Analyst Josh Gilbert, Federal Reserve chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  has made it quite clear that this is only a temporary pause, something that could spell further trouble for Bitcoin in the long-term.\par \par \uc2 "Much of the positivity we\u8217\'20\'19ve seen from risk assets this year, including Bitcoin, is built on the expectation that inflation will fall and interest rates will peak, and then begin to be cut," Gilbert said.\par \par \uc2 Inflation is moving in the right direction but the comments from \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  signify that rates could stay higher for longer, which would put Bitcoin on the back foot."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-cpi-and-a-strong-rebound-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC, CPI and a \u8216\'20\'18strong rebound\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 5 things to know in Bitcoin this week}}}\par \par \uc2 The second largest cryptocurrency by market cap, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), also took a hit, falling more than 5% from $1,727 to $1,631 in the same time frame. Altcoins were not spared from the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment either, with many of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tokens labeled as securities}}}\uc2  in the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuits stumbling another than 3%.\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is currently down 3.4% in the last 24 hours, while Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) fell 3.3% and 2.8% respectively.\par \par \uc2 According to Cointelegraph analyst Marcel Pechman, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fed-pauses-interest-rates-but-bitcoin-options-data-still-points-to-btc-price-downside"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 current options data for Bitcoin}}}\uc2  suggests a further slide to the downside, especially when considering {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/big-week-for-crypto-here-s-everything-you-need-to-know"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the regulatory hostility}}}\uc2  towards the crypto industry on U.S. soil combined with the likelihood of further rate increases from the Fed in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/bitcoin-net-zero-2050-climate-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin is on a collision course with \u8216\'20\'18Net Zero\u8217\'20\'19 promises}}}\par \par \uc2 Update (June 15, 1:40am UTC): This article has been updated to include comments from \uc2 eToro\uc2  market analyst Josh Gilbert.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b3ef6494-52ca-40bd-85b6-fcf0357568e4.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230615ej6f00009\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin\par \b \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s what happened in crypto today\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Kyle White \par \uc2 924 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto prices fail to immediately react to the Fed\u8217\'20\'19s decision to pause rate hikes. Cointelegraph explains why.\par \par \uc2 The crypto market remains volatile after the June 14 Federal Open Market Committee (FOMC) announcement and presser with Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  revealed that the central bank would pause rate hikes for June.\par \par \uc2 While this move aligned with investors\u8217\'20\'19 expectations, the crypto market has yet to show any \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum. Powell also mentioned that at least two more rate hikes would be needed in the future.\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) price started the day up, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-flat-26-k-ppl-data-markets-fed-powell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 trading}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-flat-26-k-ppl-data-markets-fed-powell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 above $26,000}}}\uc2 , but it has since retraced to a 24-hour low of $25,791 after the FOMC announcement. Some analysts are predicting that a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-bitcoin-resistance-to-retesting-25-k-support-is-futile"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 drop to $25,000}}}\uc2  is inevitable based on the current state of BTC derivatives data.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/2113de8e-773f-4a3f-9c73-323173391a8f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market performance, 1-day chart. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 The muted crypto price action and lack of a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  response to today\u8217\'20\'19s rate hike pause could be the lingering effect of the charges by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/coldie-snoop-dogg-piece-vitalik-buterin-john-mcafee/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \u8216\'20\'18Holy shit, I\u8217\'20\'19ve seen that!\u8217\'20\'19 \u8212\'20\'14 Coldie\u8217\'20\'19s Snoop Dogg, Vitalik and McAfee NFTs}}}\par \par \uc2 FOMC tanks crypto and some equities\par \par \uc2 The stock market dropped sharply on June 14 after the FOMC decision, with the Dow Jones dropping 200 points minutes after the announcement. Another major equity index, the S&P 500 Index, hit a 13-month high.\par \par \uc2 While Powell decided to pause interest rate hikes, the Fed reiterated its focus to bring down elevated inflation.\par \par \uc2 In the policy issuance, the \uc2 Federal Reserve{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/monetary20230614a.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stated}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CIn determining the extent of additional policy firming that may be appropriate to return inflation to 2 percent over time, the Committee will take into account the cumulative tightening of monetary policy, the lags with which monetary policy affects economic activity and inflation, and economic and financial developments.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The wording shows a potential return to interest rate hikes in the future. To date, crypto prices are still highly correlated with the Dow and S&P 500, and most major banks still expect the United States to experience a sharp recession at some point in 2023. This has not stopped major stock indexes from reaching yearly highs after the U.S. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/31k-was-not-the-end-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debt ceiling deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 According to a \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2  analysis, which incorporates more than 1,000 data points, \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the current state of the economy remains low.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d0c63524-07e7-43dd-8c7d-ae2d814ace85.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Global economic health. Source: \uc2 U.S. Bank\par \par \uc2 According to Robert Haworth, senior investment strategy director at \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2 :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1COverall, the U.S. economy is slowing, but not reaching recession.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The pausing of rate hikes is causing \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  across equities and cryptocurrencies.\par \par \uc2 Crypto sector \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  is still the main threat\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a constant in the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/5-key-highlights-sec-lawsuit-binance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 recent cryptocurrency news cycle}}}\uc2 . While the \uc2 European Union\uc2  unveiled a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/eu-s-new-crypto-law-how-mica-can-make-europe-a-digital-asset-hub"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22digital asset\b0 \highlight22  framework}}}\uc2  called the Markets in Crypto-Assets law, the U.S. seems intent to regulate through SEC enforcement.\par \par \uc2 On June 5 and June 6, the SEC filed civil lawsuits that increased the number of cryptocurrencies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the agency claims are securities to 61}}}\uc2 , representing $100 billion in value.\par \par \uc2 One of the 61 crypto tokens is Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), a token that, in 2019, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/video-of-sec-chair-praising-algorand-resurfaces-after-recently-deeming-it-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC Chair Gary Gensler called}}}\uc2  a \u8220\'20\'1Cgreat technology,\u8221\'20\'1D which seems to contradict this latest enforcement action.\par \par \uc2 Other top crypto tokens specifically mentioned as securities include \uc2 Binance\uc2  USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ) and COTI.\par \par \uc2 The recent SEC action adds to a long history of disputes, misconceptions and mistrust over the actual use case of digital assets. After the \uc2 FTX\uc2  implosion, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-poked-the-bear-and-the-bear-is-pissed-o-leary-on-the-crypto-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some feel U.S. lawmakers are angry}}}\uc2  with the crypto industry. The most recent battle is centered on how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/centralized-cryptocurrency-exchanges-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centralized exchanges (CEXs)}}}\uc2  can use customer funds.\par \par \uc2 Not all lawmakers are comfortable with Gensler\u8217\'20\'19s actions. Ohio Rep. Warren Davidson introduced the \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-us-lawmakers-file-sec-stabilization-act-to-fire-gary-gensler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC Stabilization Act}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D into the House of Representatives on June 12. The bill would remove Gensler as chair and redistribute power among a committee.\par \par \uc2 TVL and volume remain low\par \par \uc2 The attack on CEXs has also increased Bitcoin exchange inflows and outflows. Exchange inflows indicate increased sell-side pressure, while outflows typically are to self-custody assets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/a5bcd73f-f098-4c40-8a38-9546ecd3dcb7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin exchange net transfer volume. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 Despite the net flow movement to on-chain self-custody, decentralized finance (DeFi) has not witnessed growth. The total value locked (TVL) is a common metric used to examine the health and sentiment of the crypto market. According to DefiLlama, TVL across all protocols dropped 0.5% in the past 24 hours and has shed $120 billion since April 5, 2022.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e5cf6a5f-a6be-4c95-8acf-f3ae003bb96c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 All protocol ecosystems' total value locked. Source: DefiLlama\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/industry-will-focus-on-bitcoin-due-to-regulators-michael-saylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto industry \u8216\'20\'18destined\u8217\'20\'19 to be BTC-focused due to regulators: Michael Saylor}}}\par \par \uc2 With heavy macro headwinds, upcoming rate hikes and low volume, it is likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in crypto will remain for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/78d78761-3bd2-4569-96a7-62a97f0a1b0a.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230614ej6e000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/14: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, SOL, MATIC, LTC, DOT\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,820 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and most major altcoins are trading sideways, but today\u8217\'20\'19s Fed press conference could alter their trajectory.\par \par \uc2 The United States equities markets rose after the Consumer Price Index print on June 13 came in below expectations, but Bitcoin and the altcoins {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-rejects-cpi-boost-market-fed-rate-pause-odds-near-95"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 failed to recover}}}\uc2 . This suggests that cryptocurrency traders are focused on crypto-specific issues and are not buying on favorable macroeconomic news.\par \par \uc2 However, there is a ray of hope for the bulls because Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) is still holding above the $25,000 support. \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  co-founder \uc2 Michael Saylor\uc2  said in a \uc2 Bloomberg\uc2  interview on June 13 that the regulatory crackdown by the Securities and Exchange Commission may be \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  for Bitcoin. Saylor expects {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/industry-will-focus-on-bitcoin-due-to-regulators-michael-saylor"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s dominance to hit 80%}}}\uc2  in the future as \u8220\'20\'1Cmega institutional money\u8221\'20\'1D flows into crypto after the \u8220\'20\'1Cconfusion and anxiety\u8221\'20\'1D dies down.\par \par \uc2 Although Saylor\u8217\'20\'19s views may sound comforting to the Bitcoin bulls, traders should keep in mind that \uc2 MicroStrategy\uc2  has a large position in Bitcoin; hence, his views may be biased.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/355b0cab-327c-495e-8837-92a8c5338075.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Traders hate uncertainty and generally stay on the sidelines until clarity emerges. The same may happen with the cryptocurrency markets in the near term. A trending move is likely to begin only after investors sense some regulatory clarity. During uncertain phases, traders could consider reducing their position size to avoid getting whipsawed.\par \par \uc2 What are the levels that may act as resistance in Bitcoin and the major altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin climbed close to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $26,531 on June 13, but the long wick on the candlestick shows that the bears sold at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7efc283b-5ee9-41a1-b365-5b004ebe90b4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price has been stuck between the 20-day EMA and the crucial support at $25,250 for the past few days. This suggests that bulls are buying the dips, but the bears are not willing to let go of their advantage.\par \par \uc2 The downsloping moving averages indicate that bears have the upper hand, but the positive divergence on the relative strength index (RSI) indicates that the selling pressure may be reducing.\par \par \uc2 If buyers kick the price above the 20-day EMA, the BTC/USDT pair may rally to the resistance line of the descending channel. Buyers will have to overcome this roadblock to signal the start of a march to $31,000.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below $25,250, it will suggest that the bulls have given up. The pair may first slump to the support line of the channel and eventually to the psychologically important level of $20,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) shallow bounce off the strong support at $1,700 indicates a lack of demand at higher levels. A tight consolidation near a support level increases the risk of a breakdown.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/9472a9a0-36e9-49c0-b8cd-98f78619ef11.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Therefore, the buyers will have to quickly propel the price above the moving averages. If they manage to do that, the ETH/USDT pair could first rise to $1,928 and then make a dash toward the overhead resistance at $2,000.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down from the current level or the moving averages, it will indicate that bears are selling on every minor rally. That could sink the pair below $1,700. There is minor support at $1,600, but if that also fails to hold, the decline may extend to $1,352.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) once again bounced off the strong support at $220 on June 12, indicating that the bulls are aggressively protecting the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/aa783580-1fc2-4c2b-bcbd-2d4739e61aef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The BNB/USDT pair has started a recovery that is likely to face stiff resistance at the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement at $252 and again at the breakdown level of $265. If the price turns down from either level, it will suggest that the bears are viewing the relief rallies as a selling opportunity. The pair could then once again slide to $220.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls push and sustain the price above the breakdown level of $265, it may trap the aggressive bears. There is minor resistance at the 20-day EMA ($272), but it is likely to be crossed.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers shoved XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) above the overhead resistance at $0.56 on June 13, but they could not sustain the higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/c74ee48c-f992-4eda-b2c6-298800e914ee.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USDT pair turned down sharply, forming a long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The bears are trying to strengthen their position further by pulling the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.50). Below this level, the next important support to watch out for is the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) at $0.47.\par \par \uc2 If this level gives way, the selling pressure could increase and the pair may nosedive to the next major support level near $0.41. On the contrary, if the price bounces off the 50-day SMA, it will signal range-bound action for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) recovery halted near the breakdown level of $0.30, indicating that the bears are fiercely protecting the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/c3420760-5977-41e4-920e-4a8bba727888.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If bulls fail to kick the price above $0.30, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may turn down and slide to the support at $0.24. A strong rebound off this level may keep the pair range-bound between $0.24 and $0.30 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 If buyers push the price above $0.30, it will suggest that the decline may have ended in the near term. The pair could then rise to the 20-day EMA ($0.32) and subsequently to the 50-day SMA ($0.36).\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) has been sustaining above the $0.06 level since June 11, but a minor negative is that the bulls have failed to start a meaningful bounce.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/dc8cafaa-77e5-48b8-99f4-825108d6b7fa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The failure to rise above the 20-day EMA ($0.07) may give rise to another round of selling by the bears. If the $0.06 support gives way, the DOGE/USDT pair could plunge to the vital support at $0.05. Buyers are expected to defend this level with vigor.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 20-day EMA. That will increase the possibility of a relief rally to $0.08, where the bulls may again face strong resistance by the bears.\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been witnessing a tough battle between the bulls and the bears near the crucial support at $15.28.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/47df2ee3-cba4-48ee-a312-a77662535b5b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to sustain the price above $15.28, but they can take some minor solace in knowing that they have not allowed the SOL/USDT pair to remain below $15. The oversold levels on the RSI suggest that a relief rally is possible, but the bulls will have to overcome the barrier at $16.20. If they manage to do that, the pair may start an up move to the 20-day EMA ($18.16).\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down from the current level, it will suggest that the bears remain in control. If the price slips below $15, the pair could retest the intraday low of $12.80 made on June 10.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-flat-26-k-ppl-data-markets-fed-powell"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin stays flat at $26K after PPL data as markets await Fed\u8217\'20\'19s Powell}}}\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) nosedived below the support at $0.69 and hit the psychologically important level of $0.50 on June 10.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/5eaf02d2-8a2b-48bc-ae2a-87dc2de40900.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip and are trying to start a recovery, which is likely to face stiff resistance at the breakdown level of $0.69. If the price turns down from this level, it will suggest that the bears have flipped the level into resistance. That could result in a retest of the support at $0.50.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if bulls thrust the price above $0.69, the MATIC/USDT pair may reach the 20-day EMA ($0.76). A break above this level will indicate that the bears are losing their grip. The pair may then attempt a rally to $1.\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) turned down from the moving averages and plummeted below the support line of the symmetrical triangle pattern on June 10, indicating that the bears overpowered the bulls.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f272d8e2-b487-49ef-a312-c619a06a2571.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The LTC/USDT pair is attempting a bounce off the horizontal support at $75, but the failure of the bulls to push the price back into the triangle suggests that the bears are selling on minor rallies. That increases the likelihood of a further fall below $75. The next major support on the downside is $65.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level and reenters the triangle, it will suggest that the recent breakdown may have been a bear trap. The positive momentum may pick up after the bulls push the price above $91.50.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the strong support at $4.22 on June 10, indicating that the bulls are trying to arrest the decline.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/881dc3ed-6bdd-4eec-aaca-ec1dc1ff1702.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The relief rally could reach the 20-day EMA ($4.98), where the bears are likely to sell aggressively. If the price turns down from this level, the DOT/USDT pair may retest the support at $4.22. A break below this level could start a move to $4 and later to $3.50.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears may be losing their grip. The pair could first rise to $5.15 and then to $5.56. Until buyers clear this hurdle, the sellers will remain in control.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7a285cfa-9b82-4d4f-aabf-f962b8ac0efe.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230614ej6e000b7\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Bitcoin dominance\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin gets closer to '51% attack' on altcoin market\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Yashu Gola \par \uc2 593 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin dominance index has failed to sustain above 50% since April 2021. Is this time any different?\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) percentage share in the crypto market has risen to nearly 50% in the aftermath of the last week's altcoin market rout.\par \par \uc2 On June 13, the Bitcoin Dominance Index (BTC.D), which tracks BTC's weight against other cryptocurrencies, reached 49.29%, slightly down from its two-year highs of 49.66% seen earlier this week.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f73649b2-0200-447f-9acd-eb4876d69a95.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC.D daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 BTC not an "unregistered security"\par \par \uc2 The surge in Bitcoin dominance comes after the United States' \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 's (SEC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-coinbase-crypto-industry-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  against the crypto exchanges Binance and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 . In its court filings, the commission accused many leading altcoins, including Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), of being "unregistered securities."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-gary-gensler-in-2018-video-says-btc-eth-not-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC\u8217\'20\'19s Gensler says BTC, ETH \u8216\'20\'18not securities\u8217\'20\'19 in a newly surfaced video}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin's market share typically rises during high market stress, given that traders view it as the least volatile, non-stablecoin crypto asset than most cryptocurrencies. For instance, at the height of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-dominance-nears-50-as-research-hails-bullish-narrative-flip"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 banking crisis in March 2023}}}\uc2 , Bitcoin's dominance versus altcoins had also rebounded to 50%.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/0ea54629-b2d8-47a7-bff4-025da01b2437.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Altcoins' seven-day performance versus the U.S. dollar and Bitcoin. Source: Messari\par \par \uc2 There's also other cues suggesting Bitcoin's dominance could grow further to finally break 50%.\par \par \uc2 For instance, DWF Labs, a crypto market maker, has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/lookonchain/status/1668170561095364619"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly}}}\uc2  sent millions of dollars worth of non-Bitcoin tokens to exchanges, this potentially adding selling pressure for certain altcoins.\par \par \uc2 Independent market analyst Stack Hodler also {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/stackhodler/status/1667435638033981442?s=12&t=9Z7eZQ2MAn7cgruZycHUFw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suggests}}}\uc2  that most crypto hedge funds would first and foremost abandon their altcoin exposure.\par \par \uc2 But not everyone is \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  on BTC dominance. Fellow analyst Moustache, for example, argues the altcoin market may have bottomed once again as Bitcoin will be unable to break the 50% mark.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/Bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #Bitcoin}}}\par \par \uc2 Is the USDT-Dominance about to fall?\par \par \uc2 If so, we're in for a massive Altseason.\par \par \uc2 -Head and Shoulders pattern forming (W)?\par \par \uc2 -Stoch RSI heavily overbought.\par \par \uc2 In the last 3 years this has led to an Altseason 4 out of 5 times.\par \par \uc2 + Sentiment is in the basement for most = Good. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/odU5jg8srF"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/odU5jg8srF}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \u9431\'24\'D7 (@el_crypto_prof) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/el_crypto_prof/status/1668290670547677190?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin dominance risks pullback in June\par \par \uc2 Chart technicals suggest that Bitcoin's dominance can indeed drop in the coming weeks as altcoins rebound.\par \par \uc2 Related: \u8216\'20\'18 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/btc-prague-2023-samson-mow-interview"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no more exciting time than now\u8217\'20\'19 for Bitcoin: BTC Prague 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Most notably, BTC.D has failed to close decisively above the 50%-mark since April 2021, often reversing its gains due to an overbought weekly relative strength index (RSI).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/435825cd-09cc-4b32-bf3c-10092a47fae7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC.D weekly performance chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin now faces a similar scenario with a retest of the 50% level for the first time since last summer. Meanwhile, its RSI hangs just two points below its overbought level of 70.\par \par \uc2 Therefore, if history repeats, Bitcoin's dominance will decline toward 39% by late 2023 or early 2024.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a breakout here will be key for BTC \u8212\'20\'14 to reach levels not seen in over two years. For example, analyst Crypto Rover {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/rovercrc/status/1668273953637548032"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sees}}}\uc2  a classic \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuation setup with 52% being the next major hurdle if such a scenario pans out.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/140c6e95-f450-43ee-ace3-0336d3daad2e.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230613ej6d0008l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 eToro\par \b \uc2 eToro halts ALGO, MANA, MATIC and DASH purchases for US customers\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Brian Quarmby \par \uc2 460 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The firm also delisted XRP two years ago and doesn't offer exposure to other assets flagged by the SEC such as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \uc2 SOL\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Retail trading platform eToro has halted purchases of Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), and Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) for customers in the United States in response to the tokens being {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-binance-coinbase-terrible-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 labeled as securities in recent SEC lawsuits}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-binance-coinbase-terrible-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-binance-coinbase-terrible-defi}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The move comes just a few days after competitor {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/robinhood-will-end-support-for-3-tokens-named-in-sec-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Robinhood also halted support}}}\uc2  for MATIC along with Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), two other cryptocurrencies {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sol-is-not-a-security-says-the-solana-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 deemed as securities by the United States Securities and Exchange Commission.}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a June 12 \uc2 Twitter\uc2  thread, eToro US noted that it had reviewed its crypto listings \u8221\'20\'1Din light of the rapidly evolving regulatory landscape\u8221\'20\'1D and \u8220\'20\'1Crecent developments\u8221\'20\'1D with the SEC.\par \par \uc2 eToro has a framework in place which reviews the cryptoassets we offer in light of the rapidly evolving regulatory landscape. Due to recent developments, we will be making some changes to our crypto offering for US customers. (1/5)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 eToro US (@eToroUS) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/eToroUS/status/1668323755435622405?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The assets were officially delisted as of 6:00 am Eastern Time on July 12; however, eToro US users will still be able to hold and sell these assets.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe remain a supporter of crypto assets and believe in the importance of offering our users access to a diversified range of asset classes, which includes stocks, ETFs, and options. We are committed to working closely with regulators around the world to shape the future of the crypto industry and champion access for the ordinary investor,\u8220\'20\'1C the firm stated.\par \par \uc2 The firm has essentially opted to err on the side of caution, given that the SEC has now asserted in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-s-binance-suit-contains-heady-mix-of-predictable-charges-novel-revelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuits against Binance}}}\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  that major assets such as \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \uc2 SOL\uc2 , MATIC, MANA, ALGO, and several others are securities.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/breaking-us-lawmakers-file-sec-stabilization-act-to-fire-gary-gensler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Breaking: US lawmakers file \u8216\'20\'18SEC Stabilization Act\u8217\'20\'19 to fire Gary Gensler}}}\par \par \uc2 Members of the community have questioned why eToro US hasn\u8217\'20\'19t mentioned anything about \uc2 SOL\uc2 , which was also deemed as a security in the recent lawsuits. However, an eToro spokesperson has clarified that \uc2 SOL\uc2  is not part of eToro US's offerings.\par \par \uc2 interesting\par \par \uc2 eToro is removing Polygon and Algorand but not Solana {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/ZjigTmLmO0"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/ZjigTmLmO0}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 lightspeed mert | helius.dev (@0xMert_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/0xMert_/status/1668375373757796359?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 This isn\u8217\'20\'19t the first time eToro US has moved to halt access to certain assets in response to the litigation-friendly SEC. In December 2020, the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-exchanges-are-suspending-or-delisting-xrp-left-and-right"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 firm also delisted Ripple}}}\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) following the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against \uc2 Ripple Labs\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-regulation-sec-chair-gary-gensler-final-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22  \u8212\'20\'14 Does SEC Chair Gary Gensler have the final say?}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f026a359-a72c-4139-b274-e58ee3b66e1f.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230613ej6d00008\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 why crypto is down today\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Kyle White \par \uc2 841 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto markets are continuing to sell-off after the SEC crackdown against \uc2 Binance\uc2 , \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and the crypto market.\par \par \uc2 Price action across the crypto market remains tilted to the downside as investors and businesses digest the consequences of the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charges against Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-coinbase-crypto-industry-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase exchanges}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The lawsuits have also affected the decentralized financial (DeFi) markets by reducing total liquidity and most analysts believe that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-binance-coinbase-terrible-defi"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 more pain is}}}\uc2  on the way.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/2cb9df00-075e-4243-87b8-6a293f7d0362.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market performance, 30-day chart: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/bitcoin-net-zero-2050-climate-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin is on a collision course with \u8216\'20\'18Net Zero\u8217\'20\'19 promises}}}\par \par \uc2 SEC goes after centralized exchanges\par \par \uc2 On June 5 and June 6, the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  filed civil lawsuits against two of the largest centralized exchanges in crypto, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase}}}\uc2 . The SEC claims that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 61 different cryptocurrencies}}}\uc2 , representing $100 billion in value, are securities.\par \par \uc2 One of the 61 crypto tokens listed was Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), a token that in 2019, Gensler called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/video-of-sec-chair-praising-algorand-resurfaces-after-recently-deeming-it-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great technology}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D which seems to contradict this latest enforcement action.\par \par \uc2 Other top crypto tokens specifically mentioned as securities include \uc2 Binance\uc2  USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ) and COTI.\par \par \uc2 The enforcement actions have sent liquidity at Binance.US down by 78% since the lawsuit.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/pup2WYms9R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/pup2WYms9R}}}\uc2  market depth is down a whopping 78% since the SEC lawsuit\par \par \uc2 Market makers vacated instantly, leaving hardly any {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/liquidity?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #liquidity}}}\uc2 . {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/EvoO778mAy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/EvoO778mAy}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Kaiko (@KaikoData) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/KaikoData/status/1668206152377663488?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition to lowered liquidity, \uc2 Binance\uc2  exchange saw major balance decreases in stablecoins, BTC and Ether. Stablecoin balances are down over 20% since June 5.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/347e44e2-0d23-4757-b36a-ff798cca31a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  exchange reserves. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 The news has prompted \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  to delist three of the tokens the SEC listed as securities. \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  has given users until June 26 to withdraw assets or be forcefully liquidated. This means that over $1 billion can potentially be liquidated between the three coins within 2-weeks.\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  delisting Sol, MATIC and \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  something like ~$1B has to be sold or transferred off by users in the next 2 weeks {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/it4qSHwcGG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/it4qSHwcGG}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Tom Dunleavy (@dunleavy89) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/dunleavy89/status/1667610458759614467?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The recent SEC action adds to a long history of disputes, misconceptions or mistrust over the actual use case of digital assets. After the \uc2 FTX\uc2  implosion, some feel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-poked-the-bear-and-the-bear-is-pissed-o-leary-on-the-crypto-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. lawmakers}}}\uc2  are angry with the crypto industry. The most recent battle is centered on how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/centralized-cryptocurrency-exchanges-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centralized exchanges}}}\uc2  can use customer funds.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price falls behind equities\par \par \uc2 To date, crypto prices are still highly correlated with the Dow and S&P 500 and most major banks still expect the U.S. to experience a sharp recession at some point in 2023. This has not stopped major stock indices from reaching yearly highs after the United States {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/31k-was-not-the-end-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debt ceiling deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SEC crackdown is widening the gap between equities and Bitcoin. \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products have witnessed over $88 million in outflows since the complaint.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  investment products saw outflows totaling $88m, bringing this 8-week run of outflows to $417m. We believe that this is monetary policy related, with currently no clear end in sight to interest rate rises, leaving investors cautious. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/H1kwVxEM6B"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/H1kwVxEM6B}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 unfolded. (@cryptounfolded) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cryptounfolded/status/1668195218049609728?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 12, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2  analysis which incorporates more than 1,000 data points, \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the current state of the economy remains low.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7fcf107b-4011-477f-87a8-a0f487ef0314.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Global economic health. Source: \uc2 U.S. Bank\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Terry Sandven\uc2 , Portfolio Manager, Chief Equity Strategist at \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe improving performance of small- and mid-sized companies is notable. The small-cap Russell 2000 advanced 4.6% in the first two days of June, nearly twice that of the S&P 500 and NASDAQ Composite.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Despite the increase in equities, crypto price is not following suit.\par \par \uc2 TVL and volume remain low\par \par \uc2 The attack on centralized exchanges has also increased Bitcoin exchange inflow and outflow. Exchange inflows indicate increased sell-side pressure while outflows are typical to self-custody assets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/3370818d-d1c8-4acf-9a1a-4da1b40b1fa3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin exchange inflows and outflows. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 Despite the netflow movement to on-chain self-custody, \uc2 DeFi\uc2  has not witnessed growth. The total value locked metric (TVL) is a common way to examine the health and sentiment of the crypto markets. According to DeFiLlama, TVL across all protocols dropped 0.5% in the past 24-hours and shed $120 billion since April 5, 2022.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7a2c8437-4967-4a5d-9df7-5ce9edfea434.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 All protocol ecosystems total value locked. Source: DeFiLlama\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-and-select-altcoins-show-resilience-even-as-the-crypto-market-sell-off-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins show resilience even as the crypto market sell-off continues}}}\par \par \uc2 With heavy macro headwinds and low volume, it is likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in crypto will remain for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/8032812d-1d50-46ab-b965-a0cb6dd41a63.JPG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230612ej6c000e2\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 markets\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins show resilience even as the crypto market sell-off continues\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Marcel Pechman \par \uc2 897 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market continues to sell-off, but certain data points suggest that the sell pressure is beginning to taper off.\par \par \uc2 A \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend formation has been pressuring cryptocurrency prices for the past eight weeks, driving the total market capitalization to its lowest level in more than two months at $1.06 trillion, a 2.4% decline between June 4 and June 11.\par \par \uc2 This time, the move wasn\u8217\'20\'19t driven by Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), as the leading cryptocurrency gained 0.8% during the seven-day period. The negative pressure came from a handful of altcoins that plunged over 15%, including BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/dbe0cf91-16c9-481f-a9d4-718cbb9cc38d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total crypto market cap in USD, 1-day. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Notice that the downtrend initiated in mid-April has tested the support level in multiple instances, indicating that an eventual break to the upside would require extra effort from the bulls.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sol-is-not-a-security-says-the-solana-foundation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tagged multiple altcoins as securities}}}\uc2  in separate lawsuits filed last week against crypto exchanges \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Despite the worsening crypto regulatory environment, two derivatives metrics indicate that bulls are not yet throwing in the towel but will likely have a hard time breaking the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  price formation to the upside.\par \par \uc2 Crypto exchanges are under severe constraints in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Binance.US announced on June 9 the upcoming {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-us-suspends-usd-deposits-warns-withdrawal-pause-incoming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspension of U.S. dollar deposits and withdrawal}}}\uc2  channels, besides delisting USD trading pairs. The exchange added that it plans to transition to a crypto-only exchange but maintains a 1:1 ratio for customer assets. The SEC issued an emergency order on June 6 to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-us-user-funds-safe-amid-sec-injunction-freeze-assets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 freeze the assets of Binance.US}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also on June 9, the Crypto.com exchange announced it would {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-com-suspends-us-institutional-exchange-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 no longer service institutional clients in the United States.}}}\uc2  Although the Singapore-based company alleged a lack of client demand, the curious timing matching the recent actions against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2  has raised suspicions, as pictured by UtilizeWeb3 founder CryptoTea.\par \par \uc2 The SEC will likely sue Crypto .com\par \par \uc2 they sued \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2  for selling securities\par \par \uc2 specifically naming Solana, Cardano, Sandbox, Matic, CHZ, BNB, Mana, Algo and more\par \par \uc2 crypto .com also sells ALL of these cryptos\par \par \uc2 plus they launched their own CRO coin\par \par \uc2 plus they offer\u8230\'20\'26 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/2nuqd5ljVY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/2nuqd5ljVY}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Crypto Tea (@CryptoTea_) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/CryptoTea_/status/1666606658536058881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 8, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Despite being spared from the attacks coming from the SEC, the vice-leader Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) traded down 3.5% between June 4 and June 11 after co-founder \uc2 Vitalik Buterin\uc2  stated that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/vitalik-buterin-ethereum-fails-without-these-three-transitions"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethereum network would \u8220\'20\'1Cfail\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  if scaling doesn\u8217\'20\'19t go through. In a June 9 post via his personal blog, Buterin explained that the success of Ethereum depends on layer-2 scaling, wallet security and privacy-preserving features.\par \par \uc2 Derivatives markets show balanced leverage demand\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  contracts, also known as inverse swaps, have an embedded rate that is usually charged every eight hours.\par \par \uc2 A positive funding rate indicates that longs (buyers) demand more leverage. Still, the opposite situation occurs when shorts (sellers) require additional leverage, causing the funding rate to turn negative.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/6fb5fafa-102e-4b5c-af91-ce5cd0a75f3b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Perpetual\uc2  futures accumulated 7-day funding rate on June 11. Source: Coinglass\par \par \uc2 The seven-day funding rate for BTC and ETH was neutral, indicating balanced demand from leveraged longs (buyers) and shorts (sellers) using perpetual futures contracts. Curiously, BNB, \uc2 SOL\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  displayed no excessive short demand {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-litecoin-price-up-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 after}}}\uc2  a 15% or higher weekly price decline.\par \par \uc2 Tether demand in Asia shows modest resilience\par \par \uc2 The Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ) premium is a good gauge of China-based crypto retail trader demand. It measures the difference between China-based peer-to-peer trades and the United States dollar.\par \par \uc2 Excessive buying demand tends to pressure the indicator above fair value at 100%, and during \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, Tether\u8217\'20\'19s market offer is flooded, causing a 2% or higher discount.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8bafa6b6-38a1-419b-8880-99e439d285e8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether (USDT) peer-to-peer vs. USD/CNY. Source: OKX\par \par \uc2 Currently, the Tether premium on OKX stands at 99.8%, indicating a balanced demand from retail investors. Consequently, the indicator shows resilience considering the cryptocurrency markets dropped 17.7% over the last eight weeks to $1.06 trillion from $1.29 trillion.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/democrats-crypto-war-alienate-youth-voters-winklevoss"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Democrats\u8217\'20\'19 \u8216\'20\'18war on crypto\u8217\'20\'19 will lose its key voters, Winklevoss twins}}}\par \par \uc2 Given the balanced demand according to the funding rate and stablecoin markets, bulls should be more than satisfied, given that the recent regulatory FUD was unable to break the cryptocurrency market capitalization below $1 trillion.\par \par \uc2 It is unclear whether the market will be able to break from the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  trend. Moreover, there is no apparent rationale for bulls to jump the gun and place bets on a V-shaped recovery, given the uncertainty in the regulatory environment. Ultimately, bears are in a comfortable place despite the resilience in derivatives and stablecoin metrics.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/1d1e372b-e48c-49ee-bbef-29137c29ca05.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230612ej6c000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/12: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , MATIC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,757 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 This week hosts multiple macroeconomic reports. If the data shows inflation becoming less sticky, Bitcoin and some major altcoins could witness a pickup in \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the tough sell-off seen in the past week, the cryptocurrency markets will be looking for some support from the macroeconomic data this week. The all-important United States Consumer Price Index report on June 13 will be followed up by the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s policy decision on June 14.\par \par \uc2 Both these events could trigger a sharp response from equities and crypto traders. While a knee-jerk reaction is expected, it will be interesting to note if there is any follow-up to it. Traders may remain cautious as market \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to pick up over the next few days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/07b5fdbf-621f-4393-9005-37e77f95a45b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although the lawsuit by the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has weakened sentiment, Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) whales are using this opportunity to increase their holdings. Behavior analytics platform Santiment said in a recent report that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-cpi-and-a-strong-rebound-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin whales accumulated 57,578 Bitcoin}}}\uc2  since April 9, even as Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price fell by roughly 10% during the period.\par \par \uc2 What are the important support levels in Bitcoin and the major altcoins that need to hold for the recovery to start? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index (SPX) reached the overhead resistance at 4,325 on June 9, but the long wick on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick shows that the bears are trying to stall the up move at this level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d3cf7c05-a58c-4e11-9338-4e006044ae3c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The upsloping moving averages and the relative strength index (RSI) in the positive territory indicate that the path of least resistance is to the upside. If buyers thrust the price above 4,325, the index could start its march toward 4,500, where the bulls may encounter selling from the bears.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate in the near term if the price turns down and breaks below the moving averages. Such a move will suggest that the bulls are aggressively booking profits. The index could then tumble to the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Dollar Index (DXY) skidded back below the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of 103 on June 8, but the bears are struggling to sustain the lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/713f0b21-d288-42cb-92ec-6880ec8de50a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers are trying to propel the price back above the 20-day EMA, which could start a rally to 104.70 and subsequently to 106. This level is likely to act as a formidable resistance.\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI just above the midpoint suggest that the index may remain inside the large range between 100.82 and 106 for a while longer.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down and slips back below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears are selling on rallies. The index could then start a deeper correction to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of 102.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls have managed to sustain Bitcoin above the important support of $25,250 for the past few days, indicating strong buying at the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/909d2d66-e1bf-4fd5-adfd-e35ec4019110.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Although the downsloping moving averages indicate an advantage to bears, the positive divergence on the RSI suggests that the selling pressure could be reducing. The bulls will try to thrust the price above the 20-day EMA ($26,654), clearing the path for a potential rally to the resistance line of the descending channel.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears are maintaining their selling pressure. The BTC/USDT pair could then retest the support at $25,250. If this level breaks down, the pair may decline to the support line of the channel and eventually to $20,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) tried to start a recovery on June 11, but the shallow bounce suggests that the bears are selling on every minor rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/29d14829-9114-44fa-ac57-587c57593e9d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to strengthen their position further by dragging the price below the immediate support at $1,700. If that happens, it will suggest the start of a deeper correction. There is minor support at $1,600, but if this level gives way, the decline may extend to $1,352.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the ETH/USDT pair once again rebounds off $1,700, it will signal that the bulls are fiercely protecting the level. A rally above the resistance at $1,778 could clear the path for a potential up move to the moving averages.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) price fell from $305 on June 5 to $220 on June 12, a 27% fall within a few days. This indicates that the bears are in firm command.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/45ed2c98-a483-463f-b5e6-235739d5aad2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sharp decline has pulled the RSI into deeply oversold territory, suggesting that a relief rally is possible in the next few days. The BNB/USDT pair could first rise to $240 and thereafter attempt a rally to the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $252.50.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this level, it will suggest that the sentiment remains negative and traders continue to sell on rallies. The bears will then again try to tug the price below $220. If they pull it off, the pair could nosedive to $200 and then to $183.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been a relative outperformer in the past few days, as the bulls have managed to sustain the price above the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/407dcb37-4254-4353-98e1-82fe50e68c85.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The buyers will have to overcome the obstacle at $0.56 to start the next leg of the uptrend. The XRP/USDT pair could then rise to $0.65.\par \par \uc2 However, this may not be easy because bears are likely to protect the $0.56 level with vigor. If the price dips below the 20-day EMA ($0.50), it could signal that the bulls are losing their grip. The pair may then slump to the 50-day SMA ($0.47), which is an important level to keep an eye on.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this level, the pair may oscillate between the 50-day SMA and $0.56 for a few days.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) succumbed to intense selling pressure after breaking down from the ascending channel pattern on June 5.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/5a56e6f3-742d-4903-a0ff-e09fcbbd2840.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The downward move continued, and on June 10, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair plunged below the crucial support at $0.24. This drop sent the RSI deep into the oversold territory, indicating that the selling may have been overdone in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Strong buying at $0.22 started a recovery that may first reach $0.29 and then the 20-day EMA ($0.33). This zone is likely to witness intense battles between the bulls and the bears. If the price turns down from the zone, it will suggest that bears remain in the driver\u8217\'20\'19s seat.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-and-select-altcoins-show-resilience-even-as-the-crypto-market-sell-off-continues"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins show resilience even as the crypto market sell-off continues}}}\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bears pulled Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) below $0.06 on June 10, but the bulls purchased this drop and the price recovered to close above the support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f3ec0fdd-b67b-4767-b548-4f26f3d99ae4.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the bulls are struggling to start a meaningful pullback, indicating that demand dries up at higher levels. The bears will once again try to sink the price below the strong support at $0.06. If they do that, the DOGE/USDT pair could slump to the next major support near $0.05.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to guard the zone between $0.06 and $0.05 with all their might because a break below it may lead to panic selling. Buyers will have to kick the price back above $0.07 to gain strength.\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) slipped below the strong support of $15.28 on June 10, but the long tail on the candlestick shows aggressive buying at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/33c3eb6c-304d-433e-b403-d1b407cd8968.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers attempted to start a rebound, but the doji candlestick pattern on June 11 shows that the bears are not willing to let go of their advantage easily. They are again trying to pull the price below the support at $15.28. If they succeed, the price could decline to the next support at $12.69.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns up from the current level and rises above $16.18, it will signal the start of a stronger recovery. The \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair could then rise to the 20-day EMA ($18.85), where the bears may again mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) plummeted below the vital support of $0.69 on June 10, indicating that bears are in firm control.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/1027b99c-e447-44ae-bbf4-fae1184f8e92.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A minor solace for the buyers is that the price recovered sharply off the strong support near $0.50 as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick. The MATIC/USDT pair will attempt a bounce, which is likely to face strong selling at the breakdown level of $0.69.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from this level, it will suggest that the bears are trying to flip $0.69 into resistance. That could result in a retest of $0.50. If bulls want to start a sustained recovery, they will have to drive and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.79).\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/85611b57-16fd-4410-8084-1168ddacd54d.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230612ej6c000b6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
