age.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230610ej6a0005m\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 why crypto is down today\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Yashu Gola \par \uc2 808 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market is down today after \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  announced the delisting of "unregistered securities" tokens from its platform.\par \par \uc2 The cryptocurrency market fell 7% below $1 trillion on June 10, continuing its decline in the week that saw the industry's biggest exchanges, \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , facing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-coinbase-crypto-industry-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 regulatory actions}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC).\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ), the leading cryptocurrency by market capitalization, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-avoids-3-month-lows-as-crypto-dive-liquidates-390m"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 dropped 3.75% to around $25,500}}}\uc2 . Second-largest cryptocurrency Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) fell 6.9% to around $1,700, its worst level in two months.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e3a8fd5f-c582-4402-819b-6bf8882ffaf1.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USD and ETH/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Nonetheless, the tokens deemed "unregistered securities" in the SEC lawsuits were among the worst performers on June 10. Namely, Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), and Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), which fell 22%, 25%, and 30% on the day, respectively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/783b61c4-f450-4be7-8dd2-2354cc900b51.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USD, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USD, and \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 What crashed the crypto market?\par \par \uc2 The crypto market's decline on June 10 appeared a day after \uc2 Robinhood{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/robinhood-will-end-support-for-3-tokens-named-in-sec-lawsuits"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decided}}}\uc2  to delist \uc2 SOL\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and MATIC from its online trading platform beginning June 27, citing "a cloud of uncertainty around these assets" amid the SEC crackdown.\par \par \uc2 $1.3 billion worth of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/alts?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #alts}}}\uc2  (excluding {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/BTC?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #BTC}}}\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ETH?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ETH}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/DOGE?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #DOGE}}}\uc2  ) held at \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  could be dumped on the market over the next 2 weeks, and the market is dumping in anticipation of that.\par \par \uc2 The majority of them will be of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24SOL&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $SOL}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24MATIC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $MATIC}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24ADA&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $\b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 That's why the market is\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 BITCOIN EXPERT INDIA (@Btcexpertindia) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Btcexpertindia/status/1667429225618612225?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition, Crypto.com {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-com-suspends-us-institutional-exchange-service"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspended}}}\uc2  its institutional investment services in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Binance reportedly dumping $4.4 billion in crypto assets in recent weeks may have also contributed to downward price pressure with independent analyst {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/0xG00gly/status/1667420966488616960"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Googly}}}\uc2  noting a substantial drop in the exchange's "{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-are-proof-of-reserves-audits-and-how-do-they-work"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proof-of-reserves}}}\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  founder \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 , or "CZ," a co-accused in the SEC lawsuit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance/status/1667439122137358336?s=12&t=9Z7eZQ2MAn7cgruZycHUFw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 refuted}}}\uc2  the claims.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the Bitcoin \b \highlight22\uc2 price drop\b0 \highlight\uc2  caught \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  options traders by surprise liquidating long positions worth over $340 million in just 24 hours, according to Coinglass data.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/35e2146d-ae77-42da-b495-e9aadaf75d21.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Liquidations by crypto asset as of June 10. Source: Coinglass\par \par \uc2 Stablecoin supply data hints at buying ahead\par \par \uc2 The duration of the crypto market decline has coincided with an increase in the supply of Tether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/tether-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDT}}}\uc2  ), the largest stablecoin by market capitalization.\par \par \uc2 However, other top stablecoins, including USD Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ) and Binance USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), have decreased in market capitalization.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/25edc8c2-f5bb-4ce7-96ae-a34548523ea5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Stablecoin aggregate supplies. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 This is supported by considerable flows from cryptocurrencies to Tether addresses in general. Santiment data shows that most of these Tether addresses belong to rich investors, i.e., entities that hold more than 100,000 USDT.\par \par \uc2 Most notably, entities holding between $100,000 and $1 billion in USDT have increased in June. In contrast, addresses with a balance north of 1 billion USDT have witnessed a drop in supply; these entities could be crypto exchanges.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/93e1ab4a-4ff4-4b1c-98fe-eff2ed4605c9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Tether supply distribution among whales and sharks. Source: Santiment\par \par \uc2 "Stablecoin market caps may be declining a bit lately. But it doesn't look like sharks and whales are the ones making them sink," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://insights.santiment.net/read/stablecoins-staying-stable-as-their-market-caps-are-anything-but-7317"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 noted}}}\uc2  Brian Q, analyst at Santiment, adding:\par \par \uc2 "Therefore, we have encouraging signs that show that the key stakeholders with the most power in the markets are still ready to boost crypto whenever the time is optimal for them."\par \par \uc2 Big crypto market rebound possible?\par \par \uc2 Some analysts are certain that the current downtrend is nothing new for Bitcoin and the cryptocurrency market as a whole.\par \par \uc2 Yes remember very well, and also remember that many so called expert out from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/search?q=%24BTC&src=ctag&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 $BTC}}}\uc2  at $3000 and than {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/bitcoin?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #bitcoin}}}\uc2  jump $19500 in next 3 month. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/7GnBog9JEU"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/7GnBog9JEU}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Nilesh Rohilla | Crypto Analyst (@nilesh_rohilla) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/nilesh_rohilla/status/1667446062519574529?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 10, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 But from a technical perspective, the crypto market cap has broken below its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-traders-weigh-next-move-with-btc-price-at-crucial-200-week-trendline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 key long-term support}}}\uc2  of the 200-week exponential moving average (200-week EMA; the blue wave in the chart below), which raises its downside prospects in 2023.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-can-gain-60-if-textbook-chart-pattern-confirms-trader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price can gain 60% if \u8216\'20\'18textbook\u8217\'20\'19 chart pattern confirms \u8212\'20\'14 Trader}}}\par \par \uc2 A decline further below the 200-week EMA would likely see a market cap of $875 billion next, down 25% from current levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/deeb84e0-909b-4c0d-b6d3-9d199652b975.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market cap weekly performance. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, bulls will argue that the weekly chart has painted an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-can-gain-60-if-textbook-chart-pattern-confirms-trader"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 inverse-head-and-shoulders}}}\uc2  (IH&S) pattern, whose price target for 2023-2024 sits around $2.23 trillion, more than double the current worth.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/8032812d-1d50-46ab-b965-a0cb6dd41a63.JPG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230610ej6a0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Gary Gensler\par \b \uc2 SEC charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  are terrible for DeFi\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By    Guneet Kaur \par \uc2 1,307 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  could have far-reaching consequences for decentralized finance.\par \par \uc2 The allegations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  by the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  have substantial ramifications for the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/defi-a-comprehensive-guide-to-decentralized-finance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized finance (DeFi)}}}\uc2  ecosystem, and they are far from positive. \uc2 DeFi\uc2  has developed as a promising area within the crypto industry, aiming to disrupt established financial systems and deliver financial services in a decentralized manner.\par \par \uc2 However, the latest charges against these centralized exchanges raise doubts about the future of DeFi. By targeting {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance}}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase}}}\uc2  for suspected {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-us-cz-put-funds-at-risk"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 violations of securities laws}}}\uc2  and operating unregistered exchanges, the regulator seems to be imposing its authority on an industry that thrives on independence and autonomy.\par \par \uc2 Here\u8217\'20\'19s why such charges are terrible for DeFi.\par \par \uc2 Solana, Matic, Algorand and other tokens targeted\par \par \uc2 DeFi\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s strength comes from its decentralized protocols, smart contracts and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/what-are-dapps-everything-there-is-to-know-about-decentralized-applications"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decentralized applications}}}\uc2  that empower users and eliminate the need for intermediaries. Nonetheless, such a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-and-cz-sued-by-the-sec"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legal conflict against centralized exchanges}}}\uc2  challenges the essential concepts of DeFi. It appears like regulators are seeking to suppress innovation and reestablish control over a fast-expanding business.\par \par \uc2 Moreover, the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s accusations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  might have a chilling effect on DeFi projects, leading to uncertainty among developers and entrepreneurs about pursuing new and breakthrough concepts. This could hinder the potential expansion and evolution of DeFi, limiting its ability to disrupt and improve established financial institutions.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/kevin-oleary-binance-sec-charges"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kevin O'Leary won't rule out criminal charges in Binance ordeal }}}\par \par \uc2 In the Binance lawsuit, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the SEC argues}}}\uc2  that tokens such as Solana\u8217\'20\'19s SOL ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon\u8217\'20\'19s MATIC ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos\u8217\'20\'19 ATOM ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox\u8217\'20\'19s SAND ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland\u8217\'20\'19s MANA ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Algorand\u8217\'20\'19s ALGO ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity Shards ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ), and COTI (COTI) are securities. Another notable cryptocurrency deemed a security by the SEC is \uc2 Ripple\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ).\par \par \uc2 Such charges have significant ramifications for the DeFi ecosystem, considering the high market capitalization and prominent position these cryptocurrencies have. The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s allegations imply that they would need to conform to the legislation and registration procedures relevant to regular securities. This would introduce a huge barrier for the DeFi projects utilizing these coins and might potentially hinder their growth and innovation.\par \par \uc2 One immediate concern is the potential impact on liquidity and trading activity linked to these coins. If their categorization as securities limits market accessibility or results in a lessened price impact, it might drastically curtail the options accessible to DeFi customers. Moreover, this could impair the overall effectiveness and efficiency of decentralized protocols.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s BNB ecosystem would face a $200 million liquidation if its price were to fall below $220, according to DeFiLlama data.\par \par \uc2 Single largest liquidation in DeFi.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 whalechart (@WhaleChart) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WhaleChart/status/1667119816962977793?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Another concern arises from the compliance duties created by recognizing these coins as securities. \uc2 DeFi\uc2  projects would face higher expenses and administrative difficulties, deterring smaller initiatives or firms from entering the DeFi industry. This could result in a reduction in innovation and a restricted range of services offered to users.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, the ramifications of these allegations extend beyond the specific coins cited in the lawsuit. The uncertainty surrounding the regulatory status of various tokens within the DeFi ecosystem has the potential to exert a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/what-is-crypto-contagion-and-how-does-it-affect-the-market"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ripple effect}}}\uc2  on the sector as a whole. Market participants may display reluctance to participate with tokens that could potentially be classified as securities, weakening investor confidence and limiting overall market growth.\par \par \uc2 Unlevel playing field\par \par \uc2 The charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  by the SEC can be perceived as giving traditional banking institutions an unfair advantage over DeFi. The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-is-the-global-financial-crisis-and-its-impact-on-the-global-economy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 financial crisis of 2008}}}\uc2  uncovered several examples of fraudulent operations, risky behavior and bad management within the traditional banking sector. Despite their role in contributing to the crisis, many banks got government bailouts to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11127-009-9478-z.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prevent}}}\uc2  their collapse. This liberal approach allowed them to continue functioning without suffering significant consequences for their actions.\par \par \uc2 In contrast, the crypto exchanges, such as \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , are now being sued for alleged violations of securities laws and operating unregistered exchanges. This gap in treatment raises concerns about justice and equal opportunity. It seems that traditional financial institutions are offered second chances and support, but crypto exchanges are instantly subjected to legal action and regulatory crackdowns.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-wrong-monero-zcash-privacy-coins"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance was wrong to boot Monero, ZCash and other privacy coins}}}\par \par \uc2 Such a difference not only contradicts the concepts of fairness and accountability but also limits the growth and development of the growing crypto economy. Moreover, this biased approach risks producing an unlevel playing field. Traditional financial organizations are subject to well-established rules and have the capacity to negotiate difficult compliance obligations, while crypto exchanges may struggle to satisfy these stringent criteria.\par \par \uc2 This discrepancy in resources and regulatory load puts crypto exchanges at a disadvantage, hampering their capacity to compete and innovate. This mismatch in regulatory treatment may hamper the fair playing field for DeFi ventures, limiting their ability to compete and develop against established financial firms.\par \par \uc2 Brain drain and talent migration\par \par \uc2 The availability of resources and financing frequently drives talent mobility. Countries or locations that have a robust investor community, well-established fundraising networks, and access to finance tend to attract top talent. These tools provide the necessary support for entrepreneurs and innovators to bring their ideas to fruition. Lack of financing and resources in certain places can encourage talent to relocate to areas where they have better access to these critical aspects.\par \par \uc2 Heightened regulatory measures against DeFi exchanges can lead to a skill drain within the ecosystem. Skilled professionals and entrepreneurs may choose to quit the DeFi industry or relocate to jurisdictions with more favorable regulatory conditions. This brain drain can deprive the DeFi business of valuable experience and limit the development of creative solutions.\par \par \uc2 For example, China\u8217\'20\'19s crackdown on cryptocurrency and ICO-related activities in 2017 led to the movement of talent and crypto-related enterprises to more crypto-friendly jurisdictions like {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/an-overview-of-the-cryptocurrency-regulations-in-singapore-and-thailand"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Singapore}}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/an-overview-of-the-cryptocurrency-regulations-in-switzerland"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Switzerland}}}\uc2 , and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/5-countries-leading-the-blockchain-adoption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Malta}}}\uc2 . This move led to these countries attracting considerable blockchain and DeFi innovation.\par \par \uc2 Disincentive for institutional adoption\par \par \uc2 Regulatory measures against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  can create a deterrent for institutional investors to join the DeFi ecosystem. Institutions typically seek regulatory clarity and compliance while selecting investments. Uncertainty and regulatory scrutiny surrounding DeFi exchanges may dissuade institutional investors from entering the market, reducing the inflow of institutional money that can contribute to the growth and maturation of DeFi.\par \par \uc2 For example, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-rejects-vaneck-s-spot-bitcoin-etf-as-btc-price-falls-below-63k"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s reluctance}}}\uc2  to approve a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/learn/bitcoin-etfs-a-beginners-guide-to-exchange-traded-funds"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin exchange-traded fund}}}\uc2  in the United States due to worries over market manipulation and a lack of regulatory control has caused many institutional investors to be wary about entering the cryptosphere. Furthermore, the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s rejection was correlated with major declines in Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s price, demonstrating that negative regulatory developments can impact price \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  and thereby damage investor confidence.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the outcome of these allegations and regulatory measures will influence the destiny of DeFi. It is vital for regulators to assess the potential of disruptive technologies and ensure that their actions do not hinder their growth or deter innovation. Striking the right balance between \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and decentralization is important to unlock the full potential of DeFi and usher in a new era of financial inclusiveness and empowerment.\par \par \uc2 Guneet Kaur joined Cointelegraph as an editor in 2021. She holds a master of science in financial technology from the \uc2 University of Stirling\uc2  and an MBA from India\u8217\'20\'19s Guru Nanak Dev University.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/33b71981-a51f-4ec8-a38c-f8a351ca27ae.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230610ej6a00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 business\par \b \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  will end support for 3 tokens named in SEC lawsuits\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Turner Wright \par \uc2 530 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 On June 27, \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  will end support for Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Polygon (MATIC) and Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ) in response to the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s cases against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency and stock trading app \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  announced it will be ending support for Cardano, Polygon and Solana \u8212\'20\'14 all tokens labeled as unregistered securities by the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) in its recent legal actions against crypto exchanges Binance and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a June 9 update, \uc2 Robinhood{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://robinhood.com/us/en/support/articles/cardano-polygon-solana-update/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  it will end support for the three tokens starting on June 27 following a review. In a \uc2 Twitter\uc2  thread, the firm specifically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobinhoodApp/status/1667236704506327040"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cited}}}\uc2  the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s actions as reasons for the delisting, saying the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2  lawsuits \u8220\'20\'1Cintroduced a cloud of uncertainty\u8221\'20\'1D around the tokens \u8212\'20\'14 the only three in the cases that \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  supported.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWe believe in the future of crypto and will continue to advocate for regulatory clarity in the U.S. so that customers can participate in the marketplace with greater confidence,\u8221\'20\'1D said \uc2 Robinhood\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Earlier this week, the SEC sued crypto companies \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 . The SEC has alleged that a number of cryptocurrencies trading on those platforms are unregistered securities, including three that are currently supported on Robinhood Crypto. (1/4)\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  (@RobinhoodApp) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/RobinhoodApp/status/1667236704506327040?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 9, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 On June 5, the SEC {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a lawsuit}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Binance\uc2  for allegedly offering unregistered securities. The regulator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 followed with similar allegations}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 a U.S. crypto exchange \u8212\'20\'14 naming 13 tokens, including Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) and Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) as unregistered securities.\par \par \uc2 Former SEC commissioner and \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  chief legal compliance and corporate affairs officer \uc2 Dan Gallagher{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-robinhood-cftc-testify-congress-draft-crypto-bill"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified in a June 6 congressional hearing}}}\uc2  that the current approach to operating as a registered broker-dealer in the U.S. was like \u8220\'20\'1Ccrypto the hard way.\u8221\'20\'1D He added that the path laid out by the SEC for crypto firms was difficult to follow, even when \uc2 Robinhood\uc2  tried.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CWhen Chair [Gary] Gensler at the SEC in 2021 said, \u8216\'20\'18Come in and register,' we did," said Gallagher. \u8220\'20\'1CWe went through a 16-month process with the SEC staff trying to register a special purpose broker-dealer, and then we were pretty summarily told in March that that process was over and we would not see any fruits of that effort."\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC lawsuits: 67 cryptocurrencies are now seen as securities by the SEC}}}\par \par \uc2 The SEC cases have spurred outrage among many crypto users, who have pointed out inconsistencies in the regulator\u8217\'20\'19s approach to handling \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms. For example, the lawsuit against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  alleged the exchange has been operating as an unregistered security broker since 2019, while the firm also went public in April 2021.\par \par \uc2 Binance.US and \uc2 Binance\uc2  CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  were also named in the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s cases against the crypto exchanges for their alleged roles in unregistered offers and sales of tokens, including BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ). The U.S. entity announced on June 8 it would be {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-us-suspends-usd-deposits-warns-withdrawal-pause-incoming"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 suspending U.S. dollar deposits}}}\uc2  in response to the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s \u8220\'20\'1Cextremely aggressive and intimidating tactics.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-regulation-sec-chair-gary-gensler-final-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22 : Does SEC Chair Gary Gensler have the final say?}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/30488d97-3dff-425f-8809-41dd6998ca67.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230609ej69000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Changpeng Zhao\par \b \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary won't rule out criminal charges for \uc2 Binance\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Rudy Takala \par \uc2 1,829 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In an interview with Cointelegraph, Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t rule out the possibility of more serious charges for \uc2 Binance\uc2  or CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  levied some \u8220\'20\'1Cserious\u8221\'20\'1D allegations in the 136-page charging document the agency issued against \uc2 Binance\uc2  on June 5, telling Cointelegraph in an interview that he believes founder and CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  is in a \u8220\'20\'1Ctough\u8221\'20\'1D spot.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Leary, a venture capitalist and CNBC personality known more colorfully as \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Wonderful,\u8221\'20\'1D was an investor in crypto exchange \uc2 FTX{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/regulators-face-public-ire-after-ftx-collapse-experts-call-for-coordination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prior to its November collapse}}}\uc2 , and has been open about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/12/08/ftx-spokesman-kevin-oleary-says-he-lost-15-million-crypto-payday.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing}}}\uc2  $15 million from his gig as a paid spokesman for the company.\par \par \uc2 Some observers attribute \uc2 FTX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure to a string of events that followed an exchange on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  between its 31-year-old founder and CEO, \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , and Binance CEO Changpeng \u8220\'20\'1CCZ\u8221\'20\'1D Zhao \u8212\'20\'14 who briefly suggested, amid \uc2 FTX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s collapse, that he was open to bailing the company out. But he quickly ruled out the possibility of making an offer, to Bankman-Fried\u8217\'20\'19s chagrin \u8212\'20\'14 and, perhaps, to O\u8217\'20\'19Leary\u8217\'20\'19s bank account.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Leary nonetheless said he felt sympathy toward the 46-year-old CZ, whom the SEC has targeted with allegations that he mishandled customer funds by transferring them between entities he controlled \u8212\'20\'14 including north of $20 billion between \uc2 Binance\uc2  and a company called Merit Peak.\par \par \uc2 You won, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cz_binance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There's no need to lie, now, about the buyout.\par \par \uc2 We initiated conversations around buying you out, and we decided to do it because it was important for our business.\par \par \uc2 And while I was frustrated with your 'negotiation' tactics, I chose to still do it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SBF (@SBF_FTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBF_FTX/status/1601191234034274304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re going after CZ personally,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s tough. I mean, you have to have a little compassion for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph: What should investors make of this lawsuit? Is it going to cripple the market? Do regulators have a case?\par \par \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary: If you think about why the crypto market is \u8220\'20\'1Cstuck,\u8221\'20\'1D why it\u8217\'20\'19s not advancing, it\u8217\'20\'19s because there\u8217\'20\'19s no new money coming into it. There\u8217\'20\'19s no institutional capital. [\u8230\'20\'26] And so, when you see a constant flood of litigation against exchanges and charges by regulators \u8212\'20\'14 that just scares away institutional money.\par \par \uc2 I think everybody\u8217\'20\'19s figured that out, in addition to the regulators themselves \u8212\'20\'14 and the legislators and the lawmakers. They\u8217\'20\'19re tired of the rogue nature of this space. They\u8217\'20\'19re sick and tired of holding hearings when the next guy blows up with $6 billion. Their constituencies are mad. They\u8217\'20\'19re just tired of it.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no emotional support at all on the Hill [for crypto] anymore, because when it was a nascent industry, there was a lot of promise \u8212\'20\'14 but now it\u8217\'20\'19s just fraud, and now it\u8217\'20\'19s just opaqueness and lack of transparency and allegations of commingling customer accounts and all of this stuff. This is taking crypto \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Wonderful\u8221\'20\'1D three years, and so everybody\u8217\'20\'19s tired of it. They want to change the page. We\u8217\'20\'19re seeing this movie play out every few months now.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-are-a-tax-win-for-ftx-investors-who-lost-cash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The outcome of SBF\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution could determine how the IRS treats your FTX losses}}}\par \par \uc2 So, if finance is the last shoe to drop, so be it. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get it over with, and we can start afresh. I think there\u8217\'20\'19s a real tonality today within the institutional market about turning the page. If you have to sacrifice a few rogue operators, if these people are going to get charged and have to be litigated, so be it. I mean, we gotta move on.\par \par \uc2 CT: We\u8217\'20\'19re seeing a lot of allegations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  similar to those against \uc2 FTX\uc2  in terms of manufacturing trading volume, encouraging VIP customers to bypass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/aml-and-kyc-a-catalyst-for-mainstream-crypto-adoption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Know Your Customer requirements}}}\uc2  with VPNs, and transferring customer funds to the tune of $20 billion to another entity called Merit Peak. And its chief compliance officer even said at one point \u8212\'20\'14 according to the SEC \u8212\'20\'14 it was \u8220\'20\'1Coperating as a fking unlicensed securities exchange in the USA.\u8221\'20\'1D What do you think are the odds of criminal charges coming out of this?\par \par \uc2 KO: It\u8217\'20\'19s an unknown. But you\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this movie before. Just last November, you saw this movie \u8212\'20\'14 they called it \uc2 FTX\uc2  Day. This is FTX II. I mean, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Nobody knows. It\u8217\'20\'19s all speculation, but these are serious charges, and there are a lot of them. If any of these allegations are true, that\u8217\'20\'19s an extremely difficult place.\par \par \uc2 Plus, they\u8217\'20\'19re going after CZ personally. That\u8217\'20\'19s tough. I mean, you have to have a little compassion for him. He\u8217\'20\'19s the founder of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest exchange. But I think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to run out of oxygen in terms of just what jurisdictions are going to let him operate when the No. 1 regulator on Earth has made these allegations and filed these charges. This is not a good situation. There\u8217\'20\'19s no good news here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how anybody could make good news out of this.\par \par \uc2 CT: There are two components in the case. Obviously, one is the allegation of misconduct. The second is the more basic element required for the SEC to pursue a case \u8212\'20\'14 which is the idea that \uc2 Binance\uc2  is a broker-dealer and clearing agency for securities. To that end, it alleged that some big cryptocurrencies are securities, such as Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Solana\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SOL\uc2  and Algorand\u8217\'20\'19s ALGO. How do you feel about that and the future of anything other than Bitcoin and Ether? Would you invest in them at this point?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/opinion-barry-silbert-keeps-quiet-as-genesis-goes-down-in-flames"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barry Silbert keeps quiet as Genesis goes down in flames}}}\par \par \uc2 KO: Yes. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change my investment thesis about crypto. In fact, this encourages me that we\u8217\'20\'19ll get to an endpoint sooner in terms of getting \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and getting the infrastructure to integrate it with the world\u8217\'20\'19s financial services. I find this a very encouraging development because we\u8217\'20\'19ve really got to turn the page. I\u8217\'20\'19ve said it multiple times. But I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Polygon. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Mysten [Labs] and [its token] Sui. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Bitcoin and Ethereum and many others.\par \par \uc2 I think the promise of modifying financial services is very intriguing and has great potential. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Circle and a user of it. These are all good advancements. What\u8217\'20\'19s holding us back are the rogue operators and all of these allegations of lack of transparency. [\u8230\'20\'26] These charges, to be honest with you \u8212\'20\'14 this is getting boring. I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s just getting boring.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m tired of it. I think most institutional investors are tired of it. It\u8217\'20\'19s just boring, and I\u8217\'20\'19d like to see something else now. And so, if we have to sacrifice a few pioneers, who cares? I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s not like they didn\u8217\'20\'19t see this coming. I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s obvious what\u8217\'20\'19s happening here. And I think, at this point, let\u8217\'20\'19s move on.\par \par \uc2 CT: Do you see any daylight between the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s case against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and its case against \uc2 Binance\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 KO: The charges are different. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has a different situation. It\u8217\'20\'19s a public company. Its market cap was decimated [by the SEC suit], and the management there seems to want to keep taking on the SEC over and over and over again.\par \par \uc2 I would think at this point, if you\u8217\'20\'19re a shareholder in that company, you may want to make some changes. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think this is working as a strategy. [\u8230\'20\'26] I am not optimistic for the management team there.\par \par \uc2 I think the winds of change are gonna blow through that boardroom, and probably that\u8217\'20\'19s a good thing. I think investors are done with this. There comes a point where you just have to realize you\u8217\'20\'19re banging your head against a brick wall and you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to resolve your issues with your regulator. You can\u8217\'20\'19t keep doing this over and over and over again. The definition of madness is doing the same thing over and over and over again and expecting a different outcome. At this point, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s over for them too.\par \par \uc2 I think we should thank the founders of that company. They were pioneers, but they clearly don\u8217\'20\'19t have the maturity or skill set to operate in a regulated environment. [\u8230\'20\'26] I think at this point, they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have to work something out.\par \par \uc2 CT: Do you think there's room after this for \uc2 FTX\uc2  to make a return to polite society, or to come out lookin more 'normal'?\par \par \uc2 KO: Well, the narrative on \uc2 FTX\uc2  is that it\u8217\'20\'19s in the recovery phase. Allegedly, there's $7.2 billion of the $8 billion [that\u8217\'20\'19s] been found. That's very encouraging. And so I would think we would want to go through the process of distributing that to the shareholders and the account holders and everything else.\par \par \uc2 KO: I think, you know, the question of the allegations of that the comingling of the equity that was brought up in the Senate hearings \u8230\'20\'26 the speculation \u8212\'20\'14 and I'm one of the people that speculated it \u8212\'20\'14 did \uc2 Binance\uc2  intentionally bankrupt \uc2 FTX\uc2  by stripping their balance sheet of $2 billion in U.S. cash and 580 million in FTT tokens to put their competitor out of business so they could be the global monopoly? That's one scenario. Who knows if it's true? But I guess in impressing these charges and going into discovery, we're gonna learn a lot.\par \par \uc2 But again, it's the past. I mean, the, you gotta think about, OK, this is gonna go on and whatever happens, the finance happens, but it's not the future. That\u8217\'20\'19s not the future. The future has great promise. I'm gonna start investing in regulated exchanges all around the world because all of these accounts are gonna have to go somewhere and they're going to want to go to a place where they're allowed to exist without being constantly threatened by regulators.\par \par \uc2 I've already invested in WonderFi up in Canada, that\u8217\'20\'19s Bitbuy. I'm looking at a deal in Abu Dhabi. I\u8217\'20\'19m looking in London. There are lots of regulated exchanges that never had a chance to make money because they were being beaten up by global behemoths that had no rules and no \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no cost of compliance. That's now shifting. I think it's gonna be interesting. I think you're gonna see, in 24 months, the value of these exchanges start to go up.\par \par \uc2 This interview was condensed for length and clarity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/30d46acf-3b7d-424b-b302-2ac43a315a5c.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230609ej69000bb\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Changpeng Zhao\par \b \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary doesn\u8217\'20\'19t rule out criminal charges for \uc2 Binance\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Rudy Takala \par \uc2 1,829 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 In an interview with Cointelegraph, Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said he wouldn\u8217\'20\'19t rule out the possibility of more serious charges for \uc2 Binance\uc2  or CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  levied some \u8220\'20\'1Cserious\u8221\'20\'1D allegations in the 136-page charging document the agency issued against \uc2 Binance\uc2  on June 5, telling Cointelegraph in an interview that he believes founder and CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  is in a \u8220\'20\'1Ctough\u8221\'20\'1D spot.\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Leary, a venture capitalist and CNBC personality known more colorfully as \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Wonderful,\u8221\'20\'1D was an investor in crypto exchange \uc2 FTX{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/regulators-face-public-ire-after-ftx-collapse-experts-call-for-coordination"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 prior to its November collapse}}}\uc2 , and has been open about {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2022/12/08/ftx-spokesman-kevin-oleary-says-he-lost-15-million-crypto-payday.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 losing}}}\uc2  $15 million from his gig as a paid spokesman for the company.\par \par \uc2 Some observers attribute \uc2 FTX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s failure to a string of events that followed an exchange on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  between its 31-year-old founder and CEO, \uc2 Sam Bankman-Fried\uc2 , and Binance CEO Changpeng \u8220\'20\'1CCZ\u8221\'20\'1D Zhao \u8212\'20\'14 who briefly suggested, amid \uc2 FTX\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s collapse, that he was open to bailing the company out. But he quickly ruled out the possibility of making an offer, to Bankman-Fried\u8217\'20\'19s chagrin \u8212\'20\'14 and, perhaps, to O\u8217\'20\'19Leary\u8217\'20\'19s bank account.\par \par \uc2 You won, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 @cz_binance}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 There's no need to lie, now, about the buyout.\par \par \uc2 We initiated conversations around buying you out, and we decided to do it because it was important for our business.\par \par \uc2 And while I was frustrated with your 'negotiation' tactics, I chose to still do it.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 SBF (@SBF_FTX) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SBF_FTX/status/1601191234034274304?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 December 9, 2022}}}\par \par \uc2 O\u8217\'20\'19Leary nonetheless said he felt sympathy toward the 46-year-old CZ, whom the SEC has targeted with allegations that he mishandled customer funds by transferring them between entities he controlled \u8212\'20\'14 including north of $20 billion between \uc2 Binance\uc2  and a company called Merit Peak.\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThey\u8217\'20\'19re going after CZ personally,\u8221\'20\'1D O\u8217\'20\'19Leary said. \u8220\'20\'1CThat\u8217\'20\'19s tough. I mean, you have to have a little compassion for him.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Cointelegraph: What should investors make of this lawsuit? Is it going to cripple the market? Do regulators have a case?\par \par \uc2 Kevin O\u8217\'20\'19Leary: If you think about why the crypto market is \u8220\'20\'1Cstuck,\u8221\'20\'1D why it\u8217\'20\'19s not advancing, it\u8217\'20\'19s because there\u8217\'20\'19s no new money coming into it. There\u8217\'20\'19s no institutional capital. [\u8230\'20\'26] And so, when you see a constant flood of litigation against exchanges and charges by regulators \u8212\'20\'14 that just scares away institutional money.\par \par \uc2 I think everybody\u8217\'20\'19s figured that out, in addition to the regulators themselves \u8212\'20\'14 and the legislators and the lawmakers. They\u8217\'20\'19re tired of the rogue nature of this space. They\u8217\'20\'19re sick and tired of holding hearings when the next guy blows up with $6 billion. Their constituencies are mad. They\u8217\'20\'19re just tired of it.\par \par \uc2 There\u8217\'20\'19s no emotional support at all on the Hill [for crypto] anymore, because when it was a nascent industry, there was a lot of promise \u8212\'20\'14 but now it\u8217\'20\'19s just fraud, and now it\u8217\'20\'19s just opaqueness and lack of transparency and allegations of commingling customer accounts and all of this stuff. This is taking crypto \u8220\'20\'1CMr. Wonderful\u8221\'20\'1D three years, and so everybody\u8217\'20\'19s tired of it. They want to change the page. We\u8217\'20\'19re seeing this movie play out every few months now.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-are-a-tax-win-for-ftx-investors-who-lost-cash"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The outcome of SBF\u8217\'20\'19s prosecution could determine how the IRS treats your FTX losses}}}\par \par \uc2 So, if finance is the last shoe to drop, so be it. Let\u8217\'20\'19s get it over with, and we can start afresh. I think there\u8217\'20\'19s a real tonality today within the institutional market about turning the page. If you have to sacrifice a few rogue operators, if these people are going to get charged and have to be litigated, so be it. I mean, we gotta move on.\par \par \uc2 CT: We\u8217\'20\'19re seeing a lot of allegations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  similar to those against \uc2 FTX\uc2  in terms of manufacturing trading volume, encouraging VIP customers to bypass {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/aml-and-kyc-a-catalyst-for-mainstream-crypto-adoption"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Know Your Customer requirements}}}\uc2  with VPNs, and transferring customer funds to the tune of $20 billion to another entity called Merit Peak. And its chief compliance officer even said at one point \u8212\'20\'14 according to the SEC \u8212\'20\'14 it was \u8220\'20\'1Coperating as a fking unlicensed securities exchange in the USA.\u8221\'20\'1D What do you think are the odds of criminal charges coming out of this?\par \par \uc2 KO: It\u8217\'20\'19s an unknown. But you\u8217\'20\'19ve seen this movie before. Just last November, you saw this movie \u8212\'20\'14 they called it \uc2 FTX\uc2  Day. This is FTX II. I mean, I don\u8217\'20\'19t know. Nobody knows. It\u8217\'20\'19s all speculation, but these are serious charges, and there are a lot of them. If any of these allegations are true, that\u8217\'20\'19s an extremely difficult place.\par \par \uc2 Plus, they\u8217\'20\'19re going after CZ personally. That\u8217\'20\'19s tough. I mean, you have to have a little compassion for him. He\u8217\'20\'19s the founder of the world\u8217\'20\'19s largest exchange. But I think he\u8217\'20\'19s going to run out of oxygen in terms of just what jurisdictions are going to let him operate when the No. 1 regulator on Earth has made these allegations and filed these charges. This is not a good situation. There\u8217\'20\'19s no good news here. I don\u8217\'20\'19t know how anybody could make good news out of this.\par \par \uc2 CT: There are two components in the case. Obviously, one is the allegation of misconduct. The second is the more basic element required for the SEC to pursue a case \u8212\'20\'14 which is the idea that \uc2 Binance\uc2  is a broker-dealer and clearing agency for securities. To that end, it alleged that some big cryptocurrencies are securities, such as Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Solana\u8217\'20\'19s \uc2 SOL\uc2  and Algorand\u8217\'20\'19s ALGO. How do you feel about that and the future of anything other than Bitcoin and Ether? Would you invest in them at this point?\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/opinion-barry-silbert-keeps-quiet-as-genesis-goes-down-in-flames"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Barry Silbert keeps quiet as Genesis goes down in flames}}}\par \par \uc2 KO: Yes. It doesn\u8217\'20\'19t change my investment thesis about crypto. In fact, this encourages me that we\u8217\'20\'19ll get to an endpoint sooner in terms of getting \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and getting the infrastructure to integrate it with the world\u8217\'20\'19s financial services. I find this a very encouraging development because we\u8217\'20\'19ve really got to turn the page. I\u8217\'20\'19ve said it multiple times. But I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Polygon. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Mysten [Labs] and [its token] Sui. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Bitcoin and Ethereum and many others.\par \par \uc2 I think the promise of modifying financial services is very intriguing and has great potential. I\u8217\'20\'19m an investor in Circle and a user of it. These are all good advancements. What\u8217\'20\'19s holding us back are the rogue operators and all of these allegations of lack of transparency. [\u8230\'20\'26] These charges, to be honest with you \u8212\'20\'14 this is getting boring. I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s just getting boring.\par \par \uc2 I\u8217\'20\'19m tired of it. I think most institutional investors are tired of it. It\u8217\'20\'19s just boring, and I\u8217\'20\'19d like to see something else now. And so, if we have to sacrifice a few pioneers, who cares? I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s not like they didn\u8217\'20\'19t see this coming. I mean, it\u8217\'20\'19s obvious what\u8217\'20\'19s happening here. And I think, at this point, let\u8217\'20\'19s move on.\par \par \uc2 CT: Do you see any daylight between the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s case against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and its case against \uc2 Binance\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 KO: The charges are different. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has a different situation. It\u8217\'20\'19s a public company. Its market cap was decimated [by the SEC suit], and the management there seems to want to keep taking on the SEC over and over and over again.\par \par \uc2 I would think at this point, if you\u8217\'20\'19re a shareholder in that company, you may want to make some changes. I don\u8217\'20\'19t think this is working as a strategy. [\u8230\'20\'26] I am not optimistic for the management team there.\par \par \uc2 I think the winds of change are gonna blow through that boardroom, and probably that\u8217\'20\'19s a good thing. I think investors are done with this. There comes a point where you just have to realize you\u8217\'20\'19re banging your head against a brick wall and you\u8217\'20\'19ve got to resolve your issues with your regulator. You can\u8217\'20\'19t keep doing this over and over and over again. The definition of madness is doing the same thing over and over and over again and expecting a different outcome. At this point, I think it\u8217\'20\'19s over for them too.\par \par \uc2 I think we should thank the founders of that company. They were pioneers, but they clearly don\u8217\'20\'19t have the maturity or skill set to operate in a regulated environment. [\u8230\'20\'26] I think at this point, they\u8217\'20\'19re gonna have to work something out.\par \par \uc2 CT: Do you think there's room after this for \uc2 FTX\uc2  to make a return to polite society, or to come out lookin more 'normal'?\par \par \uc2 KO: Well, the narrative on \uc2 FTX\uc2  is that it\u8217\'20\'19s in the recovery phase. Allegedly, there's $7.2 billion of the $8 billion [that\u8217\'20\'19s] been found. That's very encouraging. And so I would think we would want to go through the process of distributing that to the shareholders and the account holders and everything else.\par \par \uc2 KO: I think, you know, the question of the allegations of that the comingling of the equity that was brought up in the Senate hearings \u8230\'20\'26 the speculation \u8212\'20\'14 and I'm one of the people that speculated it \u8212\'20\'14 did \uc2 Binance\uc2  intentionally bankrupt \uc2 FTX\uc2  by stripping their balance sheet of $2 billion in U.S. cash and 580 million in FTT tokens to put their competitor out of business so they could be the global monopoly? That's one scenario. Who knows if it's true? But I guess in impressing these charges and going into discovery, we're gonna learn a lot.\par \par \uc2 But again, it's the past. I mean, the, you gotta think about, OK, this is gonna go on and whatever happens, the finance happens, but it's not the future. That\u8217\'20\'19s not the future. The future has great promise. I'm gonna start investing in regulated exchanges all around the world because all of these accounts are gonna have to go somewhere and they're going to want to go to a place where they're allowed to exist without being constantly threatened by regulators.\par \par \uc2 I've already invested in \uc2 WonderFi\uc2  up in Canada, that\u8217\'20\'19s Bitbuy. I'm looking at a deal in Abu Dhabi. I\u8217\'20\'19m looking in London. There are lots of regulated exchanges that never had a chance to make money because they were being beaten up by global behemoths that had no rules and no \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  and no cost of compliance. That's now shifting. I think it's gonna be interesting. I think you're gonna see, in 24 months, the value of these exchanges start to go up.\par \par \uc2 This interview was condensed for length and clarity.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/30d46acf-3b7d-424b-b302-2ac43a315a5c.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230609ej690008e\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/7: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOT, LTC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,737 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Even after a strong price bounce on June 6, Bitcoin and altcoins are still clearly trading in range-bound patterns that favor \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins have been volatile in the past two days, as the cryptocurrency markets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 come to terms with the actions}}}\uc2  of the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) against {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-coinbase-crypto-exchange"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 two of the biggest crypto exchanges}}}\uc2 , \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the initial knee-jerk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-og-keeps-faith-in-bull-market-as-btc-price-bounces-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reaction to the news and the subsequent rebound}}}\uc2 , markets are likely to enter a range as traders reflect upon the uncertainty around the lawsuits. The initial response has been encouraging, as the markets have not collapsed, indicating the growing maturity of the crypto space.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/5ec1e477-062d-499d-915b-246568c31283.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Glassnode data shows a decline of 12,600 Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) from exchange balances on June 5 and 6, indicating that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/what-asset-freeze-binance-btc-outflows-muted-as-users-shun-panic-selling"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 traders kept their cool and did not panic}}}\uc2  as they had done during the \uc2 FTX\uc2  episode in November.\par \par \uc2 What are the critical support levels to watch for on the downside? Will lower levels attract buyers? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin snapped back from the vital support at $25,250 on June 6, indicating that the bulls are trying to fiercely guard the level. However, the recovery is facing selling near the moving averages.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/45bf7f98-6880-4464-a2f4-d5d99e88c7c6.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will make another attempt to tug the price to $25,250. This remains the key level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it may open the doors for a potential fall to $20,000. Such a deep fall may delay the start of the next leg of the up move.\par \par \uc2 The bulls are expected to aggressively purchase the dips to the zone between $25,250 and the support line of the channel. On the upside, buyers will have to thrust the price above the resistance line of the channel to signal the end of the corrective phase. The BTC/USDT pair may then rally to $31,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the resistance line of the falling wedge pattern on June 5, but the bears could not build upon the strength. This shows demand at lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8651e934-5e8f-4aec-b135-0feafffddb17.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls propelled the price back above the moving averages on June 6 but were met with heavy selling pressure from the bears. The sellers will again try to sink the price into the wedge. If they manage to do that, the ETH/USDT pair could extend the decline to the support line of the wedge.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price rebounds off the resistance line of the wedge, it will suggest that the bulls have flipped the line into support. Buyers will have to drive the price above $1,928 to start the northward march to $2,000 and subsequently to $2,200.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) plummeted sharply on June 5, which yanked the price below the strong support at $280. There was a meek attempt to start a recovery on June 6, but the bears did not allow the price to sustain above $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/53e94217-e0d9-408e-80e0-4a109826eab2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling resumed on June 7, and the bears have dragged the price below the crucial support at $265. This is a negative sign, as it suggests the start of a new downward move to $240 and then to the vital support at $220.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to make a comeback, they will have to push the price back above the breakdown level of $265. If they can pull it off, the BNB/USDT pair could pull back to $280 and later to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $299.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 In an up move, traders generally buy the dip to the 20-day EMA ($0.49), and they did just that in XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) on June 5 and 6 as seen from the long tail on the candlesticks.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b47bff18-7e00-4199-8d6d-dac8966faa8d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 However, the bears are not ready to give up easily. They continue to sell on rallies to the resistance zone between $0.56 and $0.59. If the price turns down sharply and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the bears want to keep the range between $0.30 and $0.56 intact.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, buyers are likely to have other plans. They will try to clear the overhead hurdle, and if they do that, it will indicate the start of a new uptrend. The XRP/USDT pair could rally to $0.60 and then to $0.80.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) tumbled below the uptrend line of the ascending triangle pattern on June 5, invalidating the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/243b6f2f-7245-43e2-b96b-f5655e321cc3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls purchased the dip on June 5 but could not kick the price back inside the channel. This suggests that bears are trying to flip the uptrend line into resistance. The selling continued on June 7, and the bears yanked the price below $0.33. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could descend to the strong support at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the first sign of strength will be a close inside the channel. Such a move will suggest that the break below the channel may have been a bear trap. The pair could attract strong buying above $0.39.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) broke below the immediate support at $0.07 on June 5 but rebounded sharply off the support near $0.06.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b686f713-d3ed-42e1-852d-8908bccfff4f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls tried to propel the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.07) on June 6, but the bears sold the rally. This indicates that the bears have not given up and they continue to sell near stiff resistance. The downsloping moving averages and the relative strength index in the negative territory indicate that bears have an edge. The bears will attempt to sink the price below $0.06.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to make a comeback, they will have to push the price back above the 20-day EMA. The DOGE/USDT pair could then attempt a rally to $0.08.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) slipped below the $0.82 support on June 6, but the bulls aggressively purchased the dip as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/3017ce41-d663-4db6-9a3d-8c9936d9fdcf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers tried to sustain the price above the breakdown level of $0.82, but the bears had other plans. They sold aggressively on June 7 and pulled the price below the June 6 low of $0.79. This suggests the resumption of the downtrend. The MATIC/USDT pair could next drop to the strong support at $0.69.\par \par \uc2 If bears want to prevent the decline, they will have to quickly push the price back above $0.82. That may trap the aggressive bears, resulting in a short squeeze, which could push the price back toward $0.94.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ark-invest-buys-coinbase-shares-the-same-day-sec-serves-lawsuit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ARK Invest buys Coinbase shares the same day SEC serves lawsuit}}}\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) rebounded off the strong support at $18.70 on June 5 and 6 as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlesticks, but the bulls could not clear the hurdle at the 20-day EMA ($20.50).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/104932ce-6d41-4859-87d6-46813a8fd96d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This indicates that the bears remain active at higher levels. If the price continues lower and breaks below the $18.70 support, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair may start a down move toward the next support at $15.28.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price rebounds off the current level or $15.28, it will indicate demand at lower levels. The bulls will then try to drive the price above $22.30. If they succeed, the pair may climb to $24 and later attempt a rally to $27.12.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) collapsed below the crucial support of $5.15 on June 5 but bounced back sharply on June 6 and rose above the breakdown level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/902c15cc-8c5b-447c-ad3a-d7110b56a921.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls could not continue the recovery on June 7, as the bears sold the minor rally. Sellers will try to strengthen their position further by pulling the price below $4.90. If they manage to do that, the DOT/USDT pair may nosedive to $4.22.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the first crucial resistance to watch out for is the 20-day EMA ($5.29). A rally above this level will be the first indication that the selling pressure may be reducing. The pair may pick up momentum above $5.56.\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) plunged below the moving averages on June 5 and recovered sharply on June 6, but the bulls could not sustain the price above the 20-day EMA ($90). This suggests that bears are selling on rallies.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/acbec6ef-60b2-4cfe-9e37-51cad9e83fa7.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to drag the price to the uptrend line. This is an important level for the bulls to defend because a break and close below it will signal the start of a potential downward move. The LTC/USDT pair could first fall to $75 and thereafter to $65.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns up from the current level or the uptrend line, it will suggest that the pair may remain stuck inside the triangle for a while longer. The bulls will have to catapult the price above the triangle to start the next leg of the up move.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/a43526a3-9066-496b-b0fd-f7e547ac518f.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230607ej67000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 markets\par \b \uc2 Security or not, Ether looks poised to hold the $1.8K level based on 3 key metrics\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Marcel Pechman \par \uc2 890 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The crypto market has had an extremely rough week, but ETH\u8217\'20\'19s price continues to show strength. Here is why.\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s price retested $1,780 after the news of the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) suing cryptocurrency exchanges \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , but it\u8217\'20\'19s not preposterous to suggest that Ether bulls should be more than happy that its price did not break below the 67-day support.\par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s actions are actually a double-edged sword for Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), and on Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , some analysts attributed the bounce in Ether to its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/why-is-ethereum-eth-price-up-today"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not being listed as a security}}}\uc2  in either of the cases brought against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 . For instance, the SEC explicitly mentioned BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), which are direct competitors to Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s smart contract-processing capabilities.\par \par \uc2 However, as noted by analyst Jevgenijs Kazanins, Ether\u8217\'20\'19s omission does not mean that it has the green light from the SEC.\par \par \uc2 SEC did not mention {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/hashtag/ETH?src=hash&ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 #ETH}}}\uc2  in the list of tokens that it considers to be securities when suing \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  and \uc2 Binance\uc2 . Could it be that the SEC is working on a separate lawsuit targeting \uc2 Ethereum Foundation\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Jevgenijs Kazanins (@jevgenijs) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/jevgenijs/status/1666066370793021440?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Kazanins raises the question of whether the SEC could be targeting the \uc2 Ethereum Foundation\uc2  in a separate lawsuit. For now, the idea is a mere unfounded speculation, but it certainly has merit given that SEC Chairman \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  refused {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-house-committee-chair-repeatedly-presses-sec-chair-is-ether-a-commodity-or-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to answer questions about Ether\u8217\'20\'19s status}}}\uc2  before the \uc2 U.S. House Financial Services Committee\uc2  in April 2023.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, what traders can focus on is Ether\u8217\'20\'19s price action, network data and other data that impacts \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  and price in the short term.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum DApps get a slight boost\par \par \uc2 Total value locked (TVL) measures the deposits locked in Ethereum\u8217\'20\'19s decentralized applications (DApps), which have been in a downtrend since mid-March. The indicator reached a 14.35 million ETH bottom on June 3 but bounced back to 14.6 million ETH by June 6, according to DefiLlama.\par \par \uc2 The number of active addresses interacting with DApps is also in a slump. Over the last 30 days, the top 12 DApps running on the Ethereum network saw a 4% increase in active addresses, even though the average transaction gas fee remained above $6.50.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/701c7fd3-3b05-45aa-ba37-f55a14c81299.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ethereum's 30-day DApp activity. Source: DappRadar\par \par \uc2 If investors fear that Ether has higher odds of breaking below the $1,800 support, it should be reflected in the ETH futures contract premium and increased costs for protective put options.\par \par \uc2 Ether derivatives metrics neutral as regulations ramped up\par \par \uc2 Ether {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/trading-for-beginners/crypto-derivatives"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 quarterly futures}}}\uc2  are popular among whales and arbitrage desks. However, these fixed-month contracts typically trade at a slight premium to spot markets, indicating that sellers are asking for more money to delay settlement.\par \par \uc2 As a result, ETH futures contracts in healthy markets should trade at a 4 to 8% annualized premium \u8212\'20\'14 a situation known as contango, which is not unique to crypto markets.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/bded5537-d581-47bd-90ae-1986f4872d75.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether 2-month futures annualized premium. Source: Laevitas\par \par \uc2 According to the futures premium, known as the basis indicator, professional traders have been avoiding leveraged longs (\b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  bets). Still, not even the retest of the $1,780 level on June 6 was enough to flip those whales and market makers into \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  sentiment.\par \par \uc2 To exclude externalities that might have solely impacted the Ether futures, one should analyze the ETH options markets. The 25% delta skew indicator compares similar call (buy) and put (sell) options and will turn positive when fear is prevalent because the protective put option premium is higher than the call options.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/af7a72fb-9656-47b0-b1bd-0f30a8cf0910.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether 30-day 25% skew. Source: Laevitas\par \par \uc2 The skew indicator will move above 8% if traders fear an Ether price crash. On the other hand, generalized excitement reflects a negative 8% skew. As displayed above, the 25% delta skew moved above the positive 8% threshold on June 5, indicating bearishness. However, the subsequent bounce to $1,880 on June 6 has moved the metric back to a neutral state.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-reminds-world-it-tried-to-embrace-regulation-as-sec-sues-for-violations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coinbase reminds world it tried to \u8216\'20\'18embrace \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22 \u8217\'20\'19 as SEC sues for violations}}}\par \par \uc2 Ether\u8217\'20\'19s price looks poised to hold above $1,800\par \par \uc2 In short, these three indicators signal resilience \u8212\'20\'14 namely, the TVL bounce to 14.6 million ETH, the 4% increase in DApps\u8217\'20\'19 active addresses and a meager impact on Ether derivatives markets, despite the retest of the $1,800 level.\par \par \uc2 Ethereum network usage data remains healthy, and the recent retest of the 67-day support was not enough to scare professional traders, according to derivatives metrics.\par \par \uc2 Consequently, bulls seem to have dodged a bullet, greatly reducing the risk of an imminent price crash.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b0c16b9b-63f7-47fa-bdea-9ada0a043e29.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230607ej67000b8\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 SEC\par \b \uc2 SEC sues \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for breaking US securities rules\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Prashant Jha \par \uc2 583 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  has filed a lawsuit against New York-based crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for breaking U.S. securities rules.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) has filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  against New York-based crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for offering unregistered securities.\par \par \uc2 The SEC lawsuit alleges that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has never registered as a broker, national securities exchange or clearing agency, evading the disclosure scheme for securities markets. The SEC alleges that several tokens offered by the crypto exchange, including Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow (FLOW), Internet Computer ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/internet-computer-icp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ICP}}}\uc2  ), Near ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/near-protocol-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEAR}}}\uc2  ), Voyager Token (VGX), Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) and Nexo ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/nexo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEXO}}}\uc2  ) qualify as securities.\par \par \uc2 Today we charged \uc2 Coinbase, Inc\uc2 . with operating its crypto asset trading platform as an unregistered national securities exchange, broker, and clearing agency and for failing to register the offer and sale of its crypto asset staking-as-a-service program. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XPG2gDkxtV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XPG2gDkxtV}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hCdVMw8B2v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hCdVMw8B2v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (@SECGov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov/status/1666059252442746881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit further alleges that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has operated as an unregistered security broker since 2019, almost two years before its initial public offering in April 2021.\par \par \uc2 The SEC claims that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staking program includes five stackable crypto assets, making the staking program an investment contract and, therefore, a security. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was already fighting a staking battle with the SEC, claiming its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-submits-petition-to-explain-to-sec-that-staking-isn-t-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staking products do not qualify as securities}}}\uc2  despite Kraken previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/kraken-reaches-30m-settlement-with-sec-over-staking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settling with the SEC}}}\uc2  and winding down its staking services in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the latest \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  lawsuit, SEC Chair \uc2 Gary Gensler{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GaryGensler/status/1666059466750541825?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the crypto exchange allegedly deprived its customers of critical protections that prevent fraud and manipulation, and avoided proper disclosure and safeguards against conflicts of interest. \uc2 Gurbir Grewal\uc2 , director of the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s Division of Enforcement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/press-release/2023-102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs alleged in our complaint, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was fully aware of the applicability of the federal securities laws to its business activities, but deliberately refused to follow them\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share price dropped 15% in pre-trading after the SEC announced its lawsuit on June 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/33e0b2c0-5264-4cc2-afa7-92d4677ec3bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  share price movement. Source: \uc2 Google\par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  comes just a day after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 securities regulator sued Binance}}}\uc2  for violating securities law and comingling customers\u8217\'20\'19 funds. While \uc2 Binance\uc2  was charged with 13 counts of violations under various securities laws, the allegations against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  have puzzled many in the crypto industry, primarily because \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is a publicly listed company.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  reacted to the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  lawsuit by taking a dig at the SEC.\par \par \uc2 If you have to pick a fight with everyone, maybe you are the one at fault. \u8205\'20\'0D\u9794\'26\'42\u65039\'FE\'0F\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CZ Binance (@cz_binance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance/status/1666067006213222403?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Paul Grewal\uc2 , chief legal officer at \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , told Cointelegraph that the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s reliance on an enforcement-only approach without clear rules for the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry is hurting America\u8217\'20\'19s economic competitiveness, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe solution is legislation that allows fair rules for the road to be developed transparently and applied equally, not litigation. In the meantime, we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to operate our business as usual\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many in the crypto community {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WolfOfPoloniex/status/1666061923778187265?t=rOzEtLrEvgLzuV_tQfZ6mQ&s=19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned}}}\uc2  how \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was allowed to go public in 2021 if it operated as an unregistered security broker. One member of Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , The Wolf, said the SEC suing \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  could cut some slack for \uc2 Binance\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d82adc90-cc68-4dee-9df6-3498d7ee00eb.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej66000bd\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Ethereum\par \b \uc2 Why is Ethereum (ETH) price up today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Yashu Gola \par \uc2 544 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Ethereum price flashed a hint of green on the charts after the SEC omits it from the list of cryptocurrencies it considers to be securities.\par \par \uc2 On June 6, Ethereum's native token, Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ), rose nearly 2.25% to around $1,825, compared to its June 5 low at $1,775.\par \par \uc2 The bounce appeared synchronously with a similar move elsewhere in the crypto market. Interestingly, the move accompanied the \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-labels-61-cryptocurrencies-securities-after-binance-suit"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 decision}}}\uc2  not to call Ethereum a "security" in its lawsuits against Binance and \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 10/ SEC alleges that the following assets are securities: BNB, BUSD, Solana, Cardano, Polygon, Filecoin, Cosmos, Sandbox, Decentraland, Algorand, and Axie Infinity. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/oMz98NB6gh"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/oMz98NB6gh}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Henri Arslanian (@HenriArslanian) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/HenriArslanian/status/1665946664706748417?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The SEC steers clear of Ethereum, for now\par \par \uc2 In September 2022, SEC Chairman \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2  said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ether-staking-could-trigger-securities-laws-gensler"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 proof-of-stake tokens}}}\uc2  like Ether fall under the category of securities per the "Howey Test." However, his opinion differs from his predecessor \uc2 William Hinman\uc2 , who said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/judge-allows-ripple-to-depose-sec-official-who-decided-eth-is-not-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ether is not a security}}}\uc2  in his 2018 speech.\par \par \uc2 Also, in April 2023, Gensler {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/us-house-committee-chair-repeatedly-presses-sec-chair-is-ether-a-commodity-or-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sidestepped}}}\uc2  questions about Ethereum's status before the \uc2 U.S. House Financial Services Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And now, the SEC's omission of Ether in the list of crypto assets it considers security \u8212\'20\'14 including the Binance-branded stablecoin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  and PoS assets Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) and Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) \u8212\'20\'14 has boosted its competitive advantage in the layer-one blockchain market.\par \par \uc2 That is visible in Ethereum's crypto market dominance (ETH.D) performance since the SEC lawsuit; it rose to 20.7% on June 6, the highest in nine months.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8e37ef2d-a212-4a05-a440-5cc7a95fd9e2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH.D daily performance chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Bitcoin's market share (BTC.D) has dropped to 47.23%, the lowest since April 2023.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-net-outflows-on-ethereum-blockchain-after-sec-lawsui-nansen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance net outflows hit $778M on Ethereum since SEC charges: Nansen}}}\par \par \uc2 Is an extended ETH price rebound ahead?\par \par \uc2 From a technical perspective, Ether's price bounce has occurred near a short term support level that constitutes a descending triangle pattern.\par \par \uc2 A descending triangle is considered a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  continuation pattern in an uptrend. It resolves after the price breaks above the falling trendline resistance with strong volumes and rises by as much as the triangle's maximum height.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b8c86d98-cd80-4a2d-b323-cc491e04df1d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USD daily price chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 As a result, ETH price could see a run-up toward the triangle's upper trendline near $1,900. But, it may extend the recovery trend toward $2,100 if the price breaks above the $1,900-resistance. In other words, a 20% rebound in June.\par \par \uc2 As a note of caution, descending triangles have often appeared at the end of an uptrend, leading to sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  reversals.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-01/62a9e911-43a2-4cc4-92a1-f4819d8f0db5.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej66000ba\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 SEC\par \b \uc2 SEC sues \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for breaking US securities rules\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Prashant Jha \par \uc2 583 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  has filed a lawsuit against New York-based crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for breaking U.S. securities rules.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) has filed a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908/gov.uscourts.nysd.599908.1.0.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lawsuit}}}\uc2  against New York-based crypto exchange \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  for offering unregistered securities.\par \par \uc2 The SEC lawsuit alleged that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has never registered as a broker, national securities exchange or clearing agency, evading the disclosure scheme for securities markets. The SEC alleges that several tokens offered by the crypto exchange, including Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ), Chiliz (CHZ), Flow (FLOW), Internet Computer ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/internet-computer-icp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ICP}}}\uc2  ), Near ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/near-protocol-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEAR}}}\uc2  ), Voyager Token (VGX), Dash ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/dash-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DASH}}}\uc2  ) and Nexo ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/nexo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 NEXO}}}\uc2  ) qualify as securities.\par \par \uc2 Today we charged \uc2 Coinbase, Inc\uc2 . with operating its crypto asset trading platform as an unregistered national securities exchange, broker, and clearing agency and for failing to register the offer and sale of its crypto asset staking-as-a-service program. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/XPG2gDkxtV"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/XPG2gDkxtV}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/hCdVMw8B2v"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/hCdVMw8B2v}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (@SECGov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov/status/1666059252442746881?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit further alleges that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  has operated as an unregistered security broker since 2019, almost two years before its initial public offering in April 2021.\par \par \uc2 The SEC claims that \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s staking program includes five stackable crypto assets, making the staking program an investment contract and, therefore, a security. \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was already fighting a staking battle with the SEC, claiming its {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/coinbase-submits-petition-to-explain-to-sec-that-staking-isn-t-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 staking products do not qualify as securities}}}\uc2  despite Kraken previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/kraken-reaches-30m-settlement-with-sec-over-staking"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 settling with the SEC}}}\uc2  and winding down its staking services in the United States.\par \par \uc2 Addressing the latest \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  lawsuit, SEC Chair \uc2 Gary Gensler{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/GaryGensler/status/1666059466750541825?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  the crypto exchange allegedly deprived its customers of critical protections that prevent fraud and manipulation, and avoided proper disclosure and safeguards against conflicts of interest. \uc2 Gurbir Grewal\uc2 , director of the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s Division of Enforcement, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/press-release/2023-102"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  :\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs alleged in our complaint, \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was fully aware of the applicability of the federal securities laws to its business activities, but deliberately refused to follow them\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s share price dropped 15% in pre-trading after the SEC announced its lawsuit on June 6.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/33e0b2c0-5264-4cc2-afa7-92d4677ec3bb.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  share price movement. Source: \uc2 Google\par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s lawsuit against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  comes just a day after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 securities regulator sued Binance}}}\uc2  for violating securities law and comingling customers\u8217\'20\'19 funds. While \uc2 Binance\uc2  was charged with 13 counts of violations under various securities laws, the allegations against \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  have puzzled many in the crypto industry, primarily because \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  is a publicly listed company.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  reacted to the \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  lawsuit by taking a dig at the SEC.\par \par \uc2 If you have to pick a fight with everyone, maybe you are the one at fault. \u8205\'20\'0D\u9794\'26\'42\u65039\'FE\'0F\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CZ Binance (@cz_binance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance/status/1666067006213222403?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 6, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Paul Grewal\uc2 , chief legal officer at \uc2 Coinbase\uc2 , told Cointelegraph that the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s reliance on an enforcement-only approach without clear rules for the \b \highlight22\uc2 digital asset\b0 \highlight\uc2  industry is hurting America\u8217\'20\'19s economic competitiveness, adding:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CThe solution is legislation that allows fair rules for the road to be developed transparently and applied equally, not litigation. In the meantime, we\u8217\'20\'19ll continue to operate our business as usual\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Many in the crypto community {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/WolfOfPoloniex/status/1666061923778187265?t=rOzEtLrEvgLzuV_tQfZ6mQ&s=19"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 questioned}}}\uc2  how \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  was allowed to go public in 2021 if it operated as an unregistered security broker. One member of Crypto \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , The Wolf, said the SEC suing \uc2 Coinbase\uc2  could cut some slack for \uc2 Binance\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d82adc90-cc68-4dee-9df6-3498d7ee00eb.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej660008j\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Crypto fear and greed\par \b \uc2 Crypto sentiment index dips back to March \u8216\'20\'18fear\u8217\'20\'19 levels amid Binance lawsuit\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Tom Mitchelhill \par \uc2 431 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto market sentiment has taken a turn for the worse as the Fear and Greed Index tipped majorly into \u8220\'20\'1Cfear\u8221\'20\'1D territory for the first time in months, following an SEC lawsuit against \uc2 Binance\uc2  that caused more than $280 million liquidations.\par \par \uc2 The Crypto Fear and Greed Index \u8212\'20\'14 a tool that measures broader market sentiment toward Bitcoin and the broader crypto market \u8212\'20\'14 has dipped to a level of \u8220\'20\'1Cfear\u8221\'20\'1D not witnessed since March 11, when Circle\u8217\'20\'19s USD coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/usdc-depegs-as-circle-confirms-3-3b-stuck-with-silicon-valley-bank"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly lost its dollar-peg}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The stumble in market sentiment on June 5 comes in the wake of the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filing a lawsuit against Binance}}}\uc2 , its U.S. arm of operations and its CEO, \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SEC pressed a total of 13 charges against the exchange and its affiliates for failing to register as a securities exchange and operating illegally in the United States.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7a1952f0-fc0e-4401-8879-3fb36f5eb0ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin Fear and Greed Index. Source: Alternative.me.\par \par \uc2 The index works by aggregating a mixture of indicators to gauge market sentiment. It combines metrics, including price \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , momentum, trading volume, with data from social media and \uc2 Google\uc2  trends to form an overall picture of investor\u8217\'20\'19s emotions toward Bitcoin and the wider crypto market.\par \par \uc2 Much of the negative sentiment owes to the immediate plunge in the value of cryptocurrencies following the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-s-binance-suit-contains-heady-mix-of-predictable-charges-novel-revelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest move against Binance}}}\uc2 . Blue-chip crypto assets such as Bitcoin and Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) are down 4.1% and 3.1%, respectively, in the last 24 hours, according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/price-indexes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from Cointelegraph Price Index.\par \par \uc2 The larger altcoins also took a beating. At the time of publication, Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) was down 6.4% in the past24 hours, while Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) had fallen 7.4%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-brian-brooks-resign-us-ceo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC complaint hints at why Brian Brooks resigned as Binance.US CEO}}}\par \par \uc2 Traders with open positions on crypto derivatives markets also suffered consequences, with more than $280 million worth of liquidations occurring since the announcement of the lawsuit.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f65e764b-939f-4ad2-8ee1-d5196584f14d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total liquidations in the past 12 hours. Source: Coinglass.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, traders with open \u8220\'20\'1Clong\u8221\'20\'1D positions \u8212\'20\'14 a leveraged bet on the price of crypto assets increasing \u8212\'20\'14 were the hardest hit, accounting for $261.75 million (92%) of the overall liquidations. Meanwhile, short traders experienced $20.7 million in liquidations. The top two digital assets were responsible for around 43% of these losses.\par \par \uc2 Asia Express: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/yuan-stablecoin-team-arrested-wechats-new-bitcoin-prices-hk-crypto-rules-asia-express/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Yuan stablecoin team arrested, WeChat\u8217\'20\'19s new Bitcoin prices, HK crypto rules}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/6c75f9b3-5d8f-4881-9d49-958d2a182036.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej660005s\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 sec\par \b \uc2 Binance\uc2  lawsuit: 61 cryptocurrencies are now seen as securities by the SEC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By   Jesse Coghlan \par \uc2 616 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Around 61 cryptocurrencies have been deemed to be securities by the \uc2 U.S. SEC\uc2  with the addition of 10 cryptocurrencies from its latest suit against \uc2 Binance\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The total number of cryptocurrencies the United States securities regulator has accused to be a \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity\u8221\'20\'1D has now reached an estimated 61, after adding a few more from its lawsuit against crypto exchange \uc2 Binance\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The 61 cryptocurrencies accused of being a \u8220\'20\'1Csecurity\u8221\'20\'1D comes from years of various litigation undertaken by the \uc2 Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2 , which has outlined what cryptocurrencies it deems securities.\par \par \uc2 In its most recent {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-s-binance-suit-contains-heady-mix-of-predictable-charges-novel-revelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 case against Binance}}}\uc2 , the SEC introduced 10 cryptocurrencies into the securities classification: BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Binance USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  )and COTI (COTI).\par \par \uc2 Today we charged \uc2 Binance Holdings Ltd\uc2 . (\uc2 Binance\uc2 ); U.S.-based affiliate, BAM Trading Services Inc., which, together with \uc2 Binance\uc2 , operates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/swcxioZKVP"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/swcxioZKVP}}}\uc2  ; and their founder, \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 , with a variety of securities law violations. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/H1wgGgR5ir"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/H1wgGgR5ir}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/IWTb7Et86H"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pic.twitter.com/IWTb7Et86H}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 \uc2 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (@SECGov) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/SECGov/status/1665779371108335618?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 Other notable cryptocurrencies the SEC has deemed securities are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ripple-vs-sec-could-newly-released-documents-tip-the-balance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ripple\u8217\'20\'19s XRP}}}\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ), LBRY\u8217\'20\'19s LBRY Credits (LBC) \u8212\'20\'14 although {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-settles-on-security-claim-in-lbry-case-community-calls-it-a-big-win-for-crypto"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 not for secondary sales}}}\uc2  \u8212\'20\'14 and Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), which it named alongside five others {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ctmain.slack.com/archives/C01BQQXS7UM/p1686023354972939?thread_ts=1686003602.178779&cid=C01BQQXS7UMhttps://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-charges-bittrex-with-unregistered-operations-calls-six-tokens-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 when it charged Bittrex in April}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s largest one-time lumping of cryptocurrencies came when it {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-do-kwon-and-terraform-labs-for-fraud"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 charged Terraform Labs}}}\uc2  with fraud in February. A total of 16 crypto assets were labeled securities, including Terra Luna Classic (LUNC), Terra Classic USD (USTC), Mirror Protocol (MIR) and an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://medium.com/mirror-protocol/mirror-user-guide-fb1cc4a28258"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 estimated}}}\uc2  13 Mirrored Assets (mAssets) that aimed to copy the price of stocks such as Apple and \uc2 Tesla\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/fines-and-regulation-the-ever-growing-landscape-of-crypto-compliance"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Fines and \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22 : The ever-growing landscape of crypto compliance}}}\par \par \uc2 The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s litigated remit of the crypto space means it now covers over $100 billion worth of the market, or around 10% of the $1.09 trillion total crypto market capitalization.\par \par \uc2 SEC Chair \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2 , however, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-lawyers-flame-gensler-over-claims-that-all-crypto-are-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-lawyers-flame-gensler-over-claims-that-all-crypto-are-securities}}}{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-lawyers-flame-gensler-over-claims-that-all-crypto-are-securities"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has claimed that \u8220\'20\'1Ceverything other than Bitcoin\u8221\'20\'1D}}}\uc2  is a security that falls under the agency\u8217\'20\'19s remit. Crypto data site CoinMarketCap {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coinmarketcap.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lists}}}\uc2  around 25,500 cryptocurrencies in existence.\par \par \uc2 SEC-deemed crypto \u8216\'20\'18securities'\par \par \uc2 The SEC has now declared that these 48 crypto tokens are securities: XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ), {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-insists-grams-are-securities-ton-launch-wont-change-this"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Telegram\u8217\'20\'19s Gram}}}\uc2  (TON), LBRY Credits (LBC), OmiseGo (OMG), DASH (DASH), Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Naga (NGC), Monolith (TKN), IHT Real Estate (IHT), Power Ledger (POWR), Kromatica (KROM), DFX Finance (DFX), \uc2 Amp\uc2  (\uc2 AMP\uc2 ), Rally (RLY), Rari Governance Token (RGT), DerivaDAO (DDX), XYO Network (XYO), Liechtenstein Cryptoasset Exchange (LCX), Kin (KIN) Salt {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/enforce/33-10865-s"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Lending}}}\uc2  (SALT), Beaxy Token (BXY), DragonChain (DRGN), Tron (TRX), \uc2 BitTorrent\uc2  (BTT), Terra USD (UST), Luna (LUNA), Mirror Protocol (MIR), Mango (MNGO), Ducat (DUCAT), Locke (LOCKE), EthereumMax (EMAX), Hydro (HYDRO), BitConnect (BCC), Meta 1 Coin (META1), Filecoin (FIL), BNB (BNB), Binance USD (BUSD), Solana (\uc2 SOL\uc2 ), Cardano (\b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), Polygon (MATIC), Cosmos (ATOM), The Sandbox (SAND), Decentraland (MANA), Axie Infinity (AXS), COTI (COTI), Paragon (PRG) and AirToken (AIR).\par \par \uc2 In addition, the SEC has deemed that these 13 Mirror Protocol mAssets are securities: Mirrored \uc2 Apple Inc\uc2 . (mAAPL), Mirrored \uc2 Amazon.com, Inc\uc2 . (mAMZN), Mirrored \uc2 Alibaba Group Holding Limited\uc2  (mBABA), Mirrored \uc2 Alphabet Inc\uc2 . (mGOOGL), Mirrored \uc2 Microsoft Corporation\uc2  (mMSFT), Mirrored \uc2 Netflix, Inc\uc2 . (mNFLX), Mirrored \uc2 Tesla, Inc\uc2 . (mTSLA), Mirrored \uc2 Twitter Inc\uc2 . (mTWTR), Mirrored \uc2 iShares Gold Trust\uc2  (mIAU), Mirrored Invesco QQQ Trust (mQQQ), Mirrored \uc2 iShares Silver Trust\uc2  (mSLV), Mirrored United States Oil Fund, LP (mUSO), Mirrored \uc2 ProShares VIX Short-Term Futures ETF\uc2  (mVIXY).\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/crypto-regulation-sec-chair-gary-gensler-final-say/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Crypto \b  \highlight22regulation\b0 \highlight22  \u8212\'20\'14 Does SEC Chair Gary Gensler have the final say?}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/112d034a-1452-4f93-8e88-c12beb0a850e.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej6600007\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Crypto fear and greed\par \b \uc2 Crypto sentiment index dips back to March \u8216\'20\'18fear\u8217\'20\'19 levels amid Binance lawsuit\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By Tom Mitchelhill \par \uc2 432 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto market sentiment has taken a turn for the worse as the Fear and Greed Index tipped majorly into \u8220\'20\'1Cfear\u8221\'20\'1D territory for the first time in months, following an SEC lawsuit against \uc2 Binance\uc2  that caused more than $280 million liquidations.\par \par \uc2 The Crypto Fear and Greed Index \u8212\'20\'14 a tool that measures broader market sentiment towards Bitcoin and the broader crypto market \u8212\'20\'14 has dipped to a level of \u8220\'20\'1Cfear\u8221\'20\'1D not witnessed since March 11 this year, when Circle\u8217\'20\'19s USD coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/usdc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 USDC}}}\uc2  ) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/usdc-depegs-as-circle-confirms-3-3b-stuck-with-silicon-valley-bank"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 briefly lost its dollar-peg}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The stumble in market sentiment comes in the wake of the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filing a lawsuit against Binance}}}\uc2 , its U.S. arm of operations and its CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The SEC pressed a total of 13 charges against the exchange and its affiliates for failing to register as a securities exchange and operating illegally in the United States.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7a1952f0-fc0e-4401-8879-3fb36f5eb0ef.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 The Bitcoin Fear and Greed Index. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://alternative.me/crypto/fear-and-greed-index/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Alternative.me}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The index works by aggregating a mixture of indicators to gauge market sentiment. It combines metrics including price \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2 , momentum, trading volume with data from social media and \uc2 Google\uc2  trends to form an overall picture of investor\u8217\'20\'19s emotions towards Bitcoin and the wider crypto market.\par \par \uc2 Much of the negative sentiment owes to the immediate plunge in the value of cryptocurrencies following the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-s-binance-suit-contains-heady-mix-of-predictable-charges-novel-revelations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 latest move against Binance}}}\uc2 . Blue-chip crypto assets such as Bitcoin and Ethereum ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) are down 4.1% and 3.1% respectively in the last 24 hours according to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/price-indexes"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 data}}}\uc2  from Cointelegraph Price Index.\par \par \uc2 The larger altcoins also took a beating. At the time of publication, Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) is down 6.4% in the last 24 hours while Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has fallen 7.4%.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-lawsuit-binance-brian-brooks-resign-us-ceo"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC complaint hints at why Brian Brooks resigned as Binance.US CEO}}}\par \par \uc2 Traders with open positions on crypto derivatives markets also suffered consequences, with more than $280 million worth of liquidations occurring since the announcement of the lawsuit.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f65e764b-939f-4ad2-8ee1-d5196584f14d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Total liquidations in the past 12 hours. Source: Coinglass.\par \par \uc2 Unsurprisingly, traders with open \u8220\'20\'1Clong\u8221\'20\'1D positions \u8212\'20\'14 a leveraged bet on the price of crypto assets increasing \u8212\'20\'14 were the hardest hit, accounting for $261.75 million (92%) of the overall liquidations. Meanwhile, short traders experienced $20.7 million in liquidations. The top two digital assets were responsible for around 43% of these losses.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/yuan-stablecoin-team-arrested-wechats-new-bitcoin-prices-hk-crypto-rules-asia-express/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Asia Express: Yuan stablecoin team arrested, WeChat\u8217\'20\'19s new Bitcoin prices, HK crypto rules}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/6c75f9b3-5d8f-4881-9d49-958d2a182036.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej6600005\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Binance\par \b \uc2 SEC sues \uc2 Binance\uc2  in US district court for unregistered securities operations\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By    Derek Andersen \par \uc2 680 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The lawsuit also named \uc2 Binance\uc2  CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  as a defendant.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) filed a suit against \uc2 Binance\uc2 , its U.S. platform and CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  (CZ) in the District Court for the District of Columbia on June 5.\par \par \uc2 4.\par \par \uc2 Our team is all standing by, ensuring systems are stable, including withdrawals, and deposits.\par \par \uc2 We will issue a response once we see the compliant. Haven't seen it yet. Media gets the info before we do.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CZ Binance (@cz_binance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance/status/1665740237979492353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The U.S. regulator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ecf.dcd.uscourts.gov/cgi-bin/show_temp.pl?file=8344309-0--15324.pdf&type=application/pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressed}}}\uc2  13 charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2 , including unregistered offers and sales of the BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) and Binance USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ) tokens, the Simple Earn and BNB Vault products, and its staking program. In addition, the SEC alleges in the suit that \uc2 Binance\uc2  failed to register its Binance.com platform as an exchange or a broker-dealer clearing agency. Further, it claims \uc2 Binance\uc2  and BAM Trading \u8212\'20\'14 Binance.US\u8217\'20\'19 legal entity \u8212\'20\'14 failed to register Binance.US as an exchange, broker and clearing agency. CZ was sued as a \u8220\'20\'1Ccontrolling person."\par \par \uc2 According to the suit:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants have enriched themselves by billions of U.S. dollars while placing investors\u8217\'20\'19 assets at significant risk. [\u8230\'20\'26] Defendants have engaged in multiple unregistered offers and sales of crypto asset securities and other investment schemes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It continued, \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants BAM Trading and BAM Management defrauded equity, retail, and institutional investors about purported surveillance and controls over manipulative trading on the Binance.US Platform, which were in fact virtually non-existent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the allegations behind the charges are claims that \uc2 Binance\uc2  failed to restrict U.S. investors from using Binance.com and that Binance.US engaged in wash trading through its \u8220\'20\'1Cprimary undisclosed \u8216\'20\'18market making\u8217\'20\'19 trading firm Sigma Chain,\u8221\'20\'1D which is owned by CZ.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-plans-new-round-of-layoffs-to-address-increased-regulatory-scrutiny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance plans new round of layoffs amid increased regulatory scrutiny}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition, the suit claims that funds from \uc2 Binance\uc2  and Binance.US were commingled in an account controlled by CZ-associated Merit Peak Limited. These charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-ceo-cz-rejects-allegations-of-market-manipulation-in-response-to-cftc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echo complaints filed}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  on March 27. CZ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.binance.com/en/blog/from-cz/czs-response-to-the-cftc-complaint-2408916493005890282"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  those charges in a detailed blog post.\par \par \uc2 SEC Chair \uc2 Gary Gensler{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/press-release/2023-101?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs alleged, Zhao and \uc2 Binance\uc2  misled investors about their risk controls and corrupted trading volumes while actively concealing who was operating the platform, the manipulative trading of its affiliated market maker, and even where and with whom investor funds and crypto assets were custodied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The SEC is demanding permanent enjoinment on \uc2 Binance\uc2  and CZ from further activities, disgorgement of ill-gotten gains with interest and financial penalties.\par \par \uc2 The suit claims that tokens traded on the \uc2 Binance\uc2  exchange were securities. Those tokens are BNB, BUSD, Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ), and COTI.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  and Binance.US responded separately to the suit. Binance.US stated in a tweet the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s claims are its \u8220\'20\'1Clatest example of \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by enforcement.\u8221\'20\'1D The suit \u8220\'20\'1Cis baseless and we intend to defend ourselves vigorously,\u8221\'20\'1D it continued.\par \par \uc2 In a blog post on Binance.com, the company wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the start, we have actively cooperated with the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s investigations and have worked hard to answer their questions and address their concerns. [\u8230\'20\'26] While we take the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s allegations seriously, they should not be the subject of an SEC enforcement action, let alone on an emergency basis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny allegations that user assets on the Binance.US platform have ever been at risk are simply wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Binance.com added. \u8220\'20\'1CThe SEC\u8217\'20\'19s actions here appear to be in service of an effort to rush to claim jurisdictional ground from other regulators \u8212\'20\'14 and investors do not appear to be the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s priority."\par \par \uc2 Allegations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  are not new. An SEC investigation of \uc2 Binance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bad-day-for-binance-with-sec-investigation-and-reuters-expose"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly began in June 2022}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Binance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-customer-fund-mismanagement-denial-against-mainstream-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has called reports}}}\uc2  of mismanagement of funds \u8220\'20\'1Cconspiracy theory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/us-and-china-try-to-crush-binance-sbfs-40m-bribe-claim-asia-express/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and China try to crush Binance, SBF\u8217\'20\'19s $40M bribe claim: Asia Express}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/01ce5dd1-6d58-4d23-b410-9415c6c68058.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230606ej650000c\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/5: SPX, DXY, BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, SOL, MATIC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,718 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins threaten to sweep new lows after the SEC launches a lawsuit against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and altcoins witnessed a sharp sell-off on the news that the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 filed a suit against Binance}}}\uc2  in U.S. district court for unregistered securities operations.\par \par \uc2 This lawsuit could delay the recovery in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and most major altcoins, as traders could prefer to remain on the sidelines for a few days until some clarity emerges. Another upcoming event that could keep the investors at bay is the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19s meeting on June 14.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/6f24bf26-3955-4cf1-9dcd-727f7e18e61f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Although the short-term picture is uncertain, Glassnode data shows that the largest cohort of Bitcoin whales, owning at least 10,000 Bitcoin, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/31k-was-not-the-end-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has been on an accumulation spree}}}\uc2  for the past few days. On the other hand, all the other major cohorts have been in a distribution phase.\par \par \uc2 What are the important support levels that could start a recovery in Bitcoin and the major altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts to find out.\par \par \uc2 S&P 500 Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The S&P 500 Index (SPX) broke and closed above the overhead resistance of 4,200 on May 26, completing the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  ascending triangle pattern.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b9d6ab87-42fd-4950-9351-0f8eee86b8dd.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SPX daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears tried to trap the aggressive bulls on May 30 and May 31, but the bulls aggressively purchased the dip to the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) at 4,183. The up move resumed on June 1, and the bulls built upon it on June 2.\par \par \uc2 There is minor resistance at 4,325, where the bears will try to stall the rally. On the way down, if bulls do not allow the price to slide below 4,200, it will enhance the prospects of an up move to the 4,500 to 4,600 zone.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down and breaks below the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) at 4,128, it will suggest that the recent breakout may have been a bull trap. The index may then dive to the uptrend line.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Dollar Index price analysis\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Dollar Index (DXY) rebounded off the 20-day EMA (103) on June 2, indicating that the sentiment has turned positive and bulls are buying the dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/74c645f3-9c77-4f59-b702-090c44fcb7ab.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DXY daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price above the immediate resistance at 104.70. If they succeed, the index could reach the overhead level of 106. This is an important level to watch for because a break above it could start a new up move.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from 106 and breaks below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that the index may extend its stay inside the range for a few more days. The bears will have to pull the price below 100.82 to complete the \b \highlight22\uc2 bearish\b0 \highlight\uc2  head-and-shoulders pattern.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been trading inside the descending channel pattern for the past several days. The bulls pushed Bitcoin above the 20-day EMA ($27,083) on June 4, but the long wick on the candlestick shows that the bears sold the rally.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7b084194-8903-42e7-8776-8e9aae714789.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price turned down on June 5 and plummeted below the immediate support at $26,500. The selling picked up momentum, and the BTC/USDT pair dropped into the crucial support zone between $25,800 and $25,250.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are expected to guard this zone with all their might because a break below it may result in long liquidation. The pair could then descend toward $20,000.\par \par \uc2 The first of strength will be a break and close above the descending channel. That could indicate the end of the corrective phase. The pair may then soar to $31,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) broke above the falling wedge pattern on May 28 and successfully held the retest on June 1, but the bulls failed to start a new up move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/d288a2e9-b096-4527-a90a-55a1c1af2efc.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This gave an opportunity to the bears to make a comeback. Sellers tugged the price below the moving averages on June 5, which accelerated the selling. The ETH/USDT pair tumbled below the resistance line of the wedge pattern. If this level fails to hold, the next stop could be $1,740 and then the support line.\par \par \uc2 This negative view will invalidate in the near term if the price turns up and breaks above $1,928. The pair could then surge to $2,000 and eventually to $2,200, where the bears may again mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) narrow range trading resolved to the downside on June 5. The sharp selling pulled the price below $300 and the next support at $280.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b06fad3b-965e-4760-bc7b-22f8061d1f2d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The BNB/USDT pair could drop to $265, which is an important level to keep an eye on. If the price turns up from $265 and rises above $280, it will indicate strong buying at lower levels. The pair may then rise to the 20-day EMA ($306), where the bulls are likely to encounter aggressive selling by the bears.\par \par \uc2 On the downside, a break and close below the $265 support could start a new downtrend. The pair may plunge to $240 and then to $220.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) has been oscillating inside a large range between $0.56 and $0.30 for the past several months. Generally, in such a well-defined range, traders buy at the support and sell close to the overhead resistance.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/4cdfec67-a8ef-4414-99ca-f147b8e0c584.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The XRP/USDT pair turned down from the overhead resistance on June 4, indicating profit-booking by the bulls and short positions by the aggressive bears.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns up from the 20-day EMA ($0.49), it will suggest that the sentiment has turned positive and traders are buying on dips. The bulls will then make one more attempt to clear the overhead hurdle.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price dips below the moving averages, it will suggest that the pair may remain stuck inside the range for a while longer.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 The long wick on Cardano\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) June 4 candlestick shows that the bears successfully halted the relief rally at the 50-day SMA ($0.38).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/f4cc80ea-f2c7-48dd-a0ea-ebbda6fb63a8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair turned down sharply on June 5 and plummeted below the uptrend line of the ascending channel pattern. This move invalidated the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  setup, and the pair may next descend toward the critical support at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 If bulls want to prevent the downward move, they will have to quickly push the price back into the channel. Such a move will suggest that the pair has rejected the lower levels. The upside momentum could pick up on a break above $0.39.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-will-get-another-test-of-200-week-trend-line-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin price will get 'another test' of 200-week trend line \u8212\'20\'14 analyst}}}\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls repeatedly failed to push Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.07) in the past few days, indicating that the bears are fiercely guarding the level.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/7136cc7e-2295-4d8d-867d-f19553e91432.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling picked up momentum on June 5, and the bears yanked the price below the immediate support at $0.07. That may have hit the stops of several traders, opening the gates for a further fall to $0.06. This level may attract strong buying by the bulls.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the $0.07 level may now act as a strong resistance during relief rallies. The bulls will have to propel and sustain the price above the breakdown level of $0.07 to signal the start of a potential recovery.\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) broke above the 50-day SMA ($21.54) on June 4, but the bulls could not sustain the positive momentum. This indicates that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/06299e3c-2089-4faa-a2d2-c7670b314c25.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears sensed an opportunity and pulled the price below the moving averages. That may have trapped the aggressive bulls, resulting in a sharp drop to the strong support at $18.70. This is an important level to keep an eye on because a break and close below it will open the doors for a potential drop to $15.28.\par \par \uc2 If the SOL/USDT pair rebounds off $18.70, the bulls will again try to clear the overhead hurdle at the moving averages. A break and close above $22.30 may tilt the advantage in favor of the bears.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls have been trying to push Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($0.89) for the past few days, but the bears held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/9e4fc6df-f3c5-41bf-bcd7-5d39ae5fcc7a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The selling intensified on June 5, and the bears pulled the price to the vital support at $0.82. Buyers are expected to defend this level aggressively. A strong bounce off this support will suggest that the pair may remain stuck between $0.82 and $0.94 for some more time.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the support at $0.82 crumbles, the MATIC/USDT pair could start a decline toward the next major support at $0.69. The bulls will have to push and sustain the price above the moving averages to signal the start of a sustained recovery.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/9b6d4e3d-eaca-4c84-a2d6-b6bad0a5210b.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230605ej65000e1\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Binance\par \b \uc2 SEC sues \uc2 Binance\uc2  in US District Court for unregistered securities operations\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By    Derek Andersen \par \uc2 662 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 The lawsuit also named \uc2 Binance\uc2  CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  as a defendant.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  (SEC) filed suit against \uc2 Binance\uc2 , its U.S. platform and CEO \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2  (CZ) in the District Court for the District of Columbia on June 5.\par \par \uc2 4.\par \par \uc2 Our team is all standing by, ensuring systems are stable, including withdrawals, and deposits.\par \par \uc2 We will issue a response once we see the compliant. Haven't seen it yet. Media gets the info before we do.\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 CZ Binance (@cz_binance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cz_binance/status/1665740237979492353?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The U.S. regulator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ecf.dcd.uscourts.gov/cgi-bin/show_temp.pl?file=8344309-0--15324.pdf&type=application/pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 pressed}}}\uc2  13 charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2 , including unregistered offers and sales of the BNB (BNB) and BUSD tokens, the Simple Earn and BNB Vault products and its staking program. In addition, the SEC alleges in the suit that \uc2 Binance\uc2  failed to register its Binance.com platform as an exchange or a broker-dealer clearing agency. Further, it claimed \uc2 Binance\uc2  and BAM Trading failed to register Binance.US as an exchange, broker and clearing agency. CZ was sued as a "controlling person."\par \par \uc2 According to the suit:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants have enriched themselves by billions of U.S. dollars while placing investors\u8217\'20\'19 assets at significant risk. [\u8230\'20\'26] Defendants have engaged in multiple unregistered offers and sales of crypto asset securities and other investment schemes.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 It continued, \u8220\'20\'1CDefendants BAM Trading and BAM Management defrauded equity, retail, and institutional investors about purported surveillance and controls over manipulative trading on the Binance.US Platform, which were in fact virtually non-existent.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Among the allegations behind the charges are claims that \uc2 Binance\uc2  failed to restrict U.S. investors from using Binance.com, And that Binance.US engaged in wash trading through its \u8220\'20\'1Cprimary undisclosed \u8216\'20\'18market making\u8217\'20\'19 trading firm Sigma Chain,\u8221\'20\'1D which is owned by CZ.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-plans-new-round-of-layoffs-to-address-increased-regulatory-scrutiny"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Binance plans new round of layoffs amid increased regulatory scrutiny}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition, the suit claims that funds from \uc2 Binance\uc2  and Binance.US were commingled in an account controlled by CZ-associated Merit Peak Limited. These charges {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-ceo-cz-rejects-allegations-of-market-manipulation-in-response-to-cftc"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 echo complaints filed}}}\uc2  by the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2  on March 27. CZ {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.binance.com/en/blog/from-cz/czs-response-to-the-cftc-complaint-2408916493005890282"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 denied}}}\uc2  those charges in a detailed blog post.\par \par \uc2 SEC chair \uc2 Gary Gensler{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/news/press-release/2023-101?utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said}}}\uc2  in a statement:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAs alleged, Zhao and \uc2 Binance\uc2  misled investors about their risk controls and corrupted trading volumes while actively concealing who was operating the platform, the manipulative trading of its affiliated market maker, and even where and with whom investor funds and crypto assets were custodied.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 The SEC is demanding permanent enjoinment on \uc2 Binance\uc2  and CZ from further activities, disgorgement of ill-gotten gains with interest and financial penalties.\par \par \uc2 The suit claimed that tokens traded on the \uc2 Binance\uc2  exchange were securities. Those tokens are BNB, BUSD, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , MATIC, FIL, ATOM, SAND, MANA, ALGO, AXS, and COTI.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  and Binance.US responded separately to the suit. Binance.US stated in a tweet the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s claims are its \u8220\'20\'1Clatest example of \b \highlight22\uc2 regulation\b0 \highlight\uc2  by enforcement.\u8221\'20\'1D The suit \u8220\'20\'1Cis baseless and we intend to defend ourselves vigorously,\u8221\'20\'1D it continued.\par \par \uc2 In a blog post on Binance.com, the company wrote:\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CFrom the start, we have actively cooperated with the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s investigations and have worked hard to answer their questions and address their concerns. [\u8230\'20\'26] While we take the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s allegations seriously, they should not be the subject of an SEC enforcement action, let alone on an emergency basis.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CAny allegations that user assets on the Binance.US platform have ever been at risk are simply wrong,\u8221\'20\'1D Binance.com added. "The SEC\u8217\'20\'19s actions here appear to be in service of an effort to rush to claim jurisdictional ground from other regulators\u8212\'20\'14and investors do not appear to be the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s priority."\par \par \uc2 Allegations against \uc2 Binance\uc2  are not new. An SEC investigation of \uc2 Binance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bad-day-for-binance-with-sec-investigation-and-reuters-expose"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly began in June 2022}}}\uc2 . \uc2 Binance{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/binance-customer-fund-mismanagement-denial-against-mainstream-reports"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has called reports}}}\uc2  of mismanagement of funds \u8220\'20\'1Cconspiracy theory.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 Magazine: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/us-and-china-try-to-crush-binance-sbfs-40m-bribe-claim-asia-express/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 US and China try to crush Binance, SBF\u8217\'20\'19s $40M bribe claim: Asia Express}}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/01ce5dd1-6d58-4d23-b410-9415c6c68058.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230605ej65000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 why crypto is down today\par \b \uc2 Why is the crypto market down today?\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Kyle White \par \uc2 722 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Crypto markets are selling-off sharply after the SEC launched a lawsuit against \uc2 Binance\uc2  and \uc2 Changpeng Zhao\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Right as analysts thought that Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) was on the cusp of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-chart-flashes-a-bullish-sign-that-could-lead-to-breakouts-in-ada-qnt-rndr-and-rpl"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 showing signs}}}\uc2  of a price breakout, the crypto market took a turn to the downside after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/sec-sues-binance-in-us-district-court-for-unregistered-securities-operations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SEC presented charges against Binance exchange}}}\uc2 . This has led some analysts to believe that the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-price-will-get-another-test-of-200-week-trend-line-analyst"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC price bottom}}}\uc2  is not yet in.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price hit a 60-day low on June 5 at $25,744 as traders worry that a larger price dip is possible, noting that Bitcoin price was already struggling with $26,600 resistance before the news of the SEC made headlines.\par \par \uc2 Similar worries exist for Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) which traded above the $2,100 level after the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-is-up-15-versus-bitcoin-since-shapella-more-eth-price-gains-ahead"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Shapella upgrade}}}\uc2  only to be followed by a 7-day low of $1,794 on May 24. The downturn comes as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ethereum-gas-fees-cool-down-after-may-memecoin-frenzy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ether gas fees}}}\uc2  have cooled after the May memecoin frenzy.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/45069c35-8939-48a8-a552-1df5bf7f7f03.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Cryptocurrency market performance, 1-day chart: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/magazine/bitcoin-net-zero-2050-climate-change/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin is on a collision course with \u8216\'20\'18Net Zero\u8217\'20\'19 promises}}}\par \par \uc2 Concerns over the debt ceiling weigh on risk assets\par \par \uc2 On June 5, the \uc2 United States Securities and Exchange Commission\uc2  led by Chairman \uc2 Gary Gensler\uc2 , filed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.sec.gov/files/litigation/complaints/2023/comp-pr2023-101.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 13 charges}}}\uc2  against \uc2 Binance\uc2  entities and Changpeng \u8220\'20\'1CCZ\u8221\'20\'1D Zhao. The lawsuit alleges \uc2 Binance\uc2  blatantly disregarded United States securities laws, enriching themselves to the tune of billions of dollars.\par \par \uc2 The lawsuit, which was filed in the District Court for the District of Columbia levied 13 charges against \uc2 Binance\uc2 . Further, in the lawsuit, 12 specific cryptocurrencies were listed as securities.\par \par \uc2 One of the 12 crypto tokens listed was Algorand ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/algorand-algo-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ALGO}}}\uc2  )., a token that in 2019, Gensler called a \u8220\'20\'1C {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/video-of-sec-chair-praising-algorand-resurfaces-after-recently-deeming-it-a-security"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 great technology}}}\uc2  \u8221\'20\'1D which seems to contradict this latest enforcement action.\par \par \uc2 Other crypto tokens specifically mentioned include \uc2 Binance\uc2  USD ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-usd-busd-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BUSD}}}\uc2  ), Binance Coin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ), Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ), Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ), Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ), Filecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/filecoin-fil-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FIL}}}\uc2  ), Cosmos ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/cosmos-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ATOM}}}\uc2  ), The Sandbox ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/the-sandbox-sand-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SAND}}}\uc2  ), Decentraland ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/decentraland-mana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MANA}}}\uc2  ), Axie Infinity ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/axie-infinity-axs-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 AXS}}}\uc2  ) and COTI.\par \par \uc2 Binance\uc2  posted an official response to the lawsuit on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 , shortly after the SEC\u8217\'20\'19s complaint went public.\par \par \uc2 Our response to the SEC's complaint. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://t.co/mgXxGTKr67"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://t.co/mgXxGTKr67}}}\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Binance (@binance) {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/binance/status/1665755879742767108?ref_src=twsrc%5Etfw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 June 5, 2023}}}\par \par \uc2 The recent SEC action adds to a long history of disputes, misconceptions or mistrust over the actual use case of digital assets. After the \uc2 FTX\uc2  implosion, some feel {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/ftx-poked-the-bear-and-the-bear-is-pissed-o-leary-on-the-crypto-crackdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. lawmakers}}}\uc2  are angry with the crypto industry. The most recent battle is centered on how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/explained/centralized-cryptocurrency-exchanges-explained"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 centralized exchanges}}}\uc2  can use customer funds.\par \par \uc2 Lido unlock adds pressure to the crypto market\par \par \uc2 To date, crypto prices are still highly correlated with the Dow and S&P 500 and most major banks still expect the U.S. to experience a sharp recession at some point in 2023. This has not stopped major stock indices from reaching yearly highs after the United States {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/31k-was-not-the-end-5-things-to-know-in-bitcoin-this-week"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 debt ceiling deal}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Binance\uc2  news is widening the gap between equities and Bitcoin.\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2  analysis which incorporates more than 1,000 data points, \b \highlight22\uc2 investor sentiment\b0 \highlight\uc2  about the current state of the economy remains low.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/93bda942-b038-4df8-a805-866511bff44f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Global economic health. Source: \uc2 U.S. Bank\par \par \uc2 According to \uc2 Terry Sandven\uc2 , Portfolio Manager, Chief Equity Strategist at \uc2 U.S. Bank\uc2 ,\par \par \uc2 \u8220\'20\'1CBetter-than-expected earnings results, particularly among growth-oriented sectors, have helped push equity prices higher.\u8221\'20\'1D\par \par \uc2 TVL and volume remain low\par \par \uc2 The total value locked metric (TVL) is a common way to examine the health and sentiment of the crypto markets. According to DeFiLlama, TVL across all protocols dropped 1% in the past 24-hours and shed $116 billion since April 5, 2022.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/58518b90-0d55-4d65-a42b-4e2d923127a3.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 All protocol ecosystems total value locked. Source: DeFiLlama\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/google-search-crypto-fall-btc-sentiment-neutral"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Google searches for \u8216\'20\'18crypto\u8217\'20\'19 fall to 2020 levels as BTC sentiment neutral}}}\par \par \uc2 In addition to tightening liquidity in the market, exchange inflows are pointing to increased sell-side pressure with an absence of buy-side pressure outside of stablecoins.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/86503750-625f-423c-955a-6c5a715101aa.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Buy-side vs sell-side exchange inflows. Source: Glassnode\par \par \uc2 With heavy macro headwinds and low volume, it is likely the \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  in crypto will remain for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2022-09/8032812d-1d50-46ab-b965-a0cb6dd41a63.JPG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230605ej65000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Bitcoin price chart flashes a  \highlight22\uc2 bullish \highlight\uc2  sign that could lead to breakouts in  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , QNT, RNDR and RPL\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,605 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Strong buying on dips suggests that Bitcoin, \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 , QNT, RNDR and RPL could be gearing up for a short-term rally.\par \par \uc2 The United States equities markets welcomed the debt ceiling deal and the May nonfarm payrolls data on June 2 with strong rallies. The S&P 500 rose 1.8% during the week while the tech-heavy Nasdaq was up 2%. This was the sixth successive week of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/06/02/tech-stocks-close-out-first-six-week-rally-since-january-2020.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gains}}}\uc2  for the Nasdaq, the first such occasion since January 2020.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the above, the expectation of the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  remaining in a pause mode during the next meeting may have acted as a catalyst for the rally. CME\u8217\'20\'19s FedWatch {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cmegroup.com/markets/interest-rates/cme-fedwatch-tool.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tool}}}\uc2  is showing a 75% probability of a pause, with the remaining 25% expecting a 25 basis points hike in the June 14 meeting.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8eae6dc4-9cde-4392-a823-5871492310a9.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Crypto market data daily view. Source: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://coin360.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Coin360}}}\par \par \uc2 Rallies in the equities markets failed to trigger a similar performance in Bitcoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) and the altcoins. However, a minor positive is that several major cryptocurrencies have stopped falling and are trying to start a recovery.\par \par \uc2 Could bulls maintain the momentum and surmount the respective overhead resistance levels? If they do, which are the top five cryptocurrencies that may lead the rally?\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been trading close to the 20-day exponential moving average ($27,233) for the past three days. This suggests that the bulls are buying the dip near $26,500.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/24a9935d-6ba7-40d4-932f-252ee41b919f.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA has flattened out and the relative strength index (RSI) is just below the midpoint, indicating a balance between supply and demand. This balance will tilt in favor of the buyers if they drive the price above the resistance line of the descending channel pattern. That may start a northward march toward $31,000.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the resistance line, it will suggest that the BTC/USDT pair may spend some more time inside the channel. The critical level to watch on the downside is $25,250. A break and close below this support may intensify selling and tug the price toward $20,000.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/62f17af4-2d46-409b-b547-7a3ed59bbe81.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bears are guarding the immediate resistance of $27,350. On the downside, the pair has been forming higher lows in the near term, indicating demand at lower levels. This enhances the prospects of a rally above the overhead resistance. If that happens, the pair may soar to the resistance line of the descending channel.\par \par \uc2 If bears want to gain the upper hand, they will have to quickly sink the price below the nearest support at $26,505. The next stop on the downside could be $26,360 and then $25,800.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) has been repeatedly finding support at the uptrend line but the bulls have failed to kick the price above the 50-day simple moving average ($0.38).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/0cb97c3a-9867-4532-9d38-046a14b14561.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 A breakout from this tight range trading is likely to happen within the next few days. If bulls shove and sustain the price above the 50-day SMA, it will clear the path for a possible rally to $0.42 and then to $0.44.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA and dips below the uptrend line, it will suggest the start of a deeper correction. The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair could then plunge to the strong support at $0.30.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/de942f2e-f8c9-463d-9867-a5d473befbbf.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the $0.38 level is behaving as a strong obstacle. However, the rising moving averages and the RSI in the positive zone indicate that the bulls have the upper hand. If buyers thrust the price above $0.38, the pair could climb to $0.40 and thereafter to $0.42.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down sharply from the current level and breaks below the 50-SMA, it will suggest that bears have seized control in the near term. The pair may then collapse to $0.36 and later to $0.35.\par \par \uc2 Quant price analysis\par \par \uc2 After staying below the downtrend line for several days, Quant ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/quant-qnt-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 QNT}}}\uc2  ) turned around and started a recovery on May 26. The bulls continued their purchase and pushed the price above the moving averages on May 29, indicating a potential trend change.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/857397a2-5ef6-484d-a785-be66764da255.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 QNT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating that the path of least resistance is to the upside. There is a barrier at $120 but if bulls overcome it, the QNT/USDT pair could rise to $128 and subsequently to $135.\par \par \uc2 Contrary to this assumption, if the price turns down sharply from $120, the bears will try to yank the price to the 20-day EMA ($110). This remains the key level to keep an eye on because a break below it will indicate that bears are back in control.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e7d74e2f-951c-4b40-82d2-90e06df9dd51.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 QNT/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the price is stuck inside a trading range between $114.50 and $120. The 20-EMA is flattish but the RSI is in the positive territory, indicating that the momentum remains \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If bulls clear the hurdle at $120, the pair is likely to start the next leg of the up-move.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price turns down and plummets below $114.50, it will suggest that bears have a slight edge. The pair may then slump to $110 and later to $102. The deeper the fall, the greater the time needed for the recovery to resume.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/cryptocurrency-markets-low-volatility-a-curse-or-an-opportunity"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Cryptocurrency markets\u8217\'20\'19 low \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22 : A curse or an opportunity?}}}\par \par \uc2 Render Token price analysis\par \par \uc2 While most major cryptocurrencies are struggling to start a recovery in a downtrend, Render Token (RNDR) has started a new upward move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8560db90-165c-4d40-89a0-d48d68352381.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 RNDR/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RNDR/USDT pair dipped to the 20-day EMA ($2.48) on May 31 but the bulls successfully defended the level. This shows a positive sentiment where traders are buying the dips to strong support levels. The pair could retest the 52-week high of $2.95. If this resistance is overcome, the pair may soar to $3.75.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of weakness will be a break and close below the 20-day EMA. Such a move will indicate aggressive profit-booking by the short-term bulls. That may open the doors for a possible drop to the 50-day SMA ($2.20).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/bb4014f1-e576-4e26-876d-a9c36d0dac50.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 RNDR/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The moving averages have completed a \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  crossover and the RSI is in positive territory, indicating that bulls have the upper hand. Buyers will try to push the price above the overhead resistance zone between $2.90 and $2.95. If they succeed, the pair may start a new uptrend.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from the current level or the overhead resistance and breaks below the moving averages, it will suggest that the bears are on a comeback. A break and close below $2.42 will indicate the start of a downward move toward $2.25.\par \par \uc2 Rocket Pool price analysis\par \par \uc2 Rocket Pool (RPL) has been trading inside an ascending channel pattern for the past several days. A positive sign in the short term is that the bulls have kept the price above the moving averages. This indicates a change in sentiment from selling on rallies to buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/c3bf96a2-5982-491d-b6e0-8519679e8a43.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 RPL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The RPL/USDT pair has been trading inside a tight range for the past few days. This suggests that a range expansion could be around the corner. If the price breaks and closes above $50.50, it will suggest the start of an up-move to the resistance line of the channel. The bears are expected to defend this level with all their might.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate in the near term if the price turns down from the current level and breaks below the moving averages. The pair could then plummet to the support line of the channel.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b546764f-91c0-4973-a3f1-9626099dfdda.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 RPL/USDT 4-hour chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 4-hour chart shows that the bulls are sustaining the price above the moving averages but they have failed to clear the overhead hurdle at $50.37. This suggests that bears continue to sell on minor rallies.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down and breaks below the 50-SMA, it will indicate that the bulls have given up. The pair may then plummet to the support line near $46.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if buyers propel and sustain the price above $50.50, the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum may pick up and the pair could rally to $53.50.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/cbe6ac38-eac4-4ddd-9b00-1a3e0988f869.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230604ej64000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 6/2: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, \uc2 SOL\uc2 , DOT, LTC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,785 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 June 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select coins are facing selling at higher levels and finding support on dips, pointing to a possible phase of short-term range-bound price action.\par \par \uc2 The United States equities markets {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/06/01/stock-market-today-live-updates.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 rallied}}}\uc2  sharply on June 2 even though nonfarm payrolls in May rose by 339,000, blowing past economists\u8217\'20\'19 expectations of a 190,000 increase. A few analysts pointed out that the market was possibly encouraged by the slower growth rate of hourly earnings, which was slightly below estimates, and an uptick in the unemployment rate.\par \par \uc2 The rally in the equities markets failed to act as a tailwind to the cryptocurrency markets, which remain stuck in a range. \uc2 Galaxy Digital\uc2  CEO \uc2 Mike Novogratz\uc2  said in an interview with CNBC that the lack of enthusiasm in the crypto markets was due to an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-markets-flat-as-institutional-buying-slows-mike-novogratz"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 absence of institutional buying}}}\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/036026c0-a447-42fd-85e6-c8271fd79ae5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) historical performance in June does not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. According to CoinGlass data, between 2013 and 2022, there have been an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/last-btc-price-dip-before-a-30k-breakout-bitcoin-wipes-weekend-gains"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 equal number of positive and negative monthly closes}}}\uc2  in June.\par \par \uc2 Will buyers defend the respective support levels and start a strong recovery in Bitcoin and select altcoins? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin has been trading inside a descending channel pattern for the past few days. The price closed below the 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $27,239 on May 31, but the bears are struggling to maintain the lower levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/e88aa009-63cd-45b8-9350-bb68f005080c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to push the price back above the 20-day EMA. If they do that, the BTC/USDT pair could reach the resistance line where the bears are expected to mount a strong defense.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the resistance line, it will signal that the pair may extend its stay inside the channel for some more time. The crucial support to watch on the downside is $25,250 because a break below it will indicate that bears are in control.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength on the upside will be a break and close above the channel. The pair could then start its journey toward $31,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls have successfully thwarted attempts by the bears to pull Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) back into the falling wedge pattern. This suggests that the bulls are trying to flip the resistance line into support.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/b064ed84-d96a-4254-97c3-e0276a996654.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The ETH/USDT pair has rebounded off the 20-day EMA ($1,855), indicating a change in sentiment from selling on rallies to buying on dips. The bulls will next try to propel the price above $1,927 and retest the stiff overhead resistance at $2,000.\par \par \uc2 This positive view will invalidate in the near term if the price turns down and re-enters the wedge. That could trap the aggressive bulls, resulting in a long liquidation. The pair may then slump toward the support line of the wedge.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) has been consolidating in a tight range between $300 and $317 for the past few days. This shows indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/8385ce8f-e2e6-45fb-89fc-746788be5779.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The gradually downsloping 20-day EMA ($310) and the relative strength index (RSI) below the midpoint give a slight advantage to the bears. If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will enhance the prospects of a break below $300. If that happens, the BNB/USDT pair could collapse to the next support at $280.\par \par \uc2 If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, the pair may reach the overhead resistance at $317. A break and close above this level will indicate the start of an up move to $334 and then $350.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 Buyers are trying to arrest XRP\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) pullback above the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.49. A shallow correction is a positive sign, as it shows that traders are keen to buy on minor dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/11320590-d35b-40ae-9754-7442db786c8c.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bulls will try to drive the price above the immediate resistance at $0.53. If they manage to do that, the XRP/USDT pair could attempt a rally to $0.56. This level is expected to act as a major hurdle, but if bulls overcome it, the pair may start a new uptrend toward $0.80.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns down from the current level and slips below $0.49, it will suggest that the bulls are booking profits. The pair could drop to the 20-day EMA ($0.48) and then to the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of $0.47.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Sellers tried to sink Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) below the uptrend line of the ascending triangle pattern on June 1, but the bulls held their ground.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/c218c920-0d24-486e-982c-55d2e03afe27.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair has risen above the 20-day EMA ($0.37), and the bulls will try to thrust the price above the 50-day SMA ($0.38). If they succeed, the pair could gradually climb to $0.42 and thereafter to the overhead resistance at $0.44.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price turns down from the current level or the 50-day SMA, it will indicate that bears are selling on rallies. That will increase the likelihood of a break below the uptrend line. The pair may then start its descent to the next support at $0.30.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls again managed to sustain Dogecoin ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) above the horizontal support at $0.07, but they are finding it difficult to push the price above the 20-day EMA ($0.07).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/c363ac40-b477-43ac-aff0-f8e85cb0e55d.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 This tight-range trading is ripe for a breakout. If buyers kick and sustain the price above the 20-day EMA, the DOGE/USDT pair could rally to $0.08. This level may again act as a strong barrier. If the price turns down from it, the pair may trade inside the range between $0.07 and $0.08 for some time.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down from the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are selling on every minor rally. The bears will then try to yank the price below $0.07 and extend the correction to $0.06.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) fell below the 20-day EMA ($0.90) on May 30, but the bears could not sustain the lower levels. This suggests buying on dips.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/2db05d6f-1b42-4de6-8787-02fa6a882946.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day EMA and the RSI near the midpoint signal a balance between supply and demand. If bulls push the price above the 20-day EMA, the MATIC/USDT pair will once again try to surmount the resistance at $0.94. If that happens, the pair could start its northward march toward the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 On the contrary, if the price turns down from $0.94 and dips back below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that bears are trying to flip the level into resistance. That could keep the pair stuck inside the $0.82 to $0.94 range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-wicks-down-to-26-5k-but-trader-eyes-chance-for-bullish-surprise"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin wicks down to $26.5K, but trader eyes chance for \u8216\'20\'18\b  \highlight22bullish\b0 \highlight22  surprise\u8217\'20\'19}}}\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been trading between the moving averages for the past few days. The bears tried to tug the price below the 20-day EMA ($20.58) on May 31 and June 1, but the bulls did not budge.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/482bf90a-3676-4b96-835b-0db1205b6935.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The tight-range trading is unlikely to continue for long. Buyers will try to thrust the price above the 50-day SMA ($21.50). If they can pull it off, the \uc2 SOL\uc2 /USDT pair may rally to $24 and subsequently to $27.12.\par \par \uc2 Instead, if the price turns down from the 50-day SMA and plummets below the 20-day EMA, it will suggest that supply exceeds demand. The pair could then drop to the vital support at $18.70. The bulls are likely to defend this level fiercely.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) has been consolidating in a tight range between $5.15 and $5.56 for the past several days.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/39bc76e8-a041-4463-8238-46a283c871a2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price rebounded off the $5.15 support on June 2, but the bulls are facing selling at the 20-day EMA ($5.37). This suggests that every relief rally is being sold into. If the price continues lower and plunges below $5.15, the DOT/USDT pair could start the next leg of the downtrend toward $4.22.\par \par \uc2 Buyers have a difficult task ahead of them. If they want to prevent a decline, they will have to shove the price above the 50-day SMA ($5.69). The pair could then attempt a recovery to $6 and eventually to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ) dipped below the moving averages on May 31, but the bulls purchased at lower levels as seen from the long tail on the day\u8217\'20\'19s candlestick.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/aab1c368-3427-4dd2-afde-0d81fbb72ae5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 Buyers propelled the price above the overhead obstacle at $95 on June 1, but they haven\u8217\'20\'19t achieved a close above it yet. If they do that, the LTC/USDT pair could rise to the resistance line of the symmetrical triangle pattern.\par \par \uc2 If the price turns down sharply from the resistance line, it will suggest that the pair may continue to oscillate inside the triangle for some more time.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, a break and close above the triangle will indicate the start of a new uptrend. The pair could first reach $115 and then start its march toward the pattern target of $142.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-06/80f0d4d4-fea6-4f63-a700-7c32f4f0b5e2.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230602ej62000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 Markets\par \b \uc2 Price analysis 5/31: BTC, ETH, BNB, XRP,  \highlight22\uc2 ADA \highlight\uc2 , DOGE, MATIC, SOL, DOT, LTC\b0\par\par\uc2 Cointelegraph By  Rakesh Upadhyay \par \uc2 1,736 \uc2 words\par \uc2 31 May 2023\par \uc2 The Cointelegraph\par \uc2 CONTEL\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Cointelegraph 2023. All rights reserved. \par \par \uc2 Bitcoin and select altcoins are close to their resistance levels, which could attract buyers in the short term.\par \par \uc2 After rising for four successive months, Bitcoin is on track to end May with losses of about 7%. Another noteworthy thing in May is that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/bitcoin-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BTC}}}\uc2  ) 30-day \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped to 1.52%, which is far below the yearly average of 4% and higher. Glassnode data shows that Bitcoin\u8217\'20\'19s low \b \highlight22\uc2 volatility\b0 \highlight\uc2  periods have only lasted for 19.3% of its total price history. Hence, there is an expectation for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-on-chain-and-options-data-hint-at-a-decisive-move-in-btc-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22volatility\b0 \highlight22  to pick up in June}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In an exclusive interview with Cointelegraph, Glassnode lead on-chain analyst James Check said that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-s-next-rally-may-be-imminent-on-chain-analyst-points-out"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin could rally to $32,000}}}\uc2 , which is its \u8220\'20\'1Ctrue cost basis.\u8221\'20\'1D Analysts at Glassnode arrived at this level after focusing on active Bitcoin investors and removing coins that are lost forever.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/4289d2bb-d4d6-44c9-ad79-3df551c0fff8.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Daily cryptocurrency market performance. Source: Coin360\par \par \uc2 In the near term, the outcome of the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cnbc.com/2023/05/30/stock-market-today-live-updates.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 vote}}}\uc2  on the debt ceiling in the \uc2 United States House of Representatives\uc2  could provide direction. If the vote succeeds, as is widely expected, it could lead to a knee-jerk reaction to the upside. But if the vote fails, then Bitcoin is likely to break below $25,000.\par \par \uc2 The short-term charts of Bitcoin and select major altcoins suggest that the bulls may be losing their grip. What are the important support levels that the bulls need to hold to avoid a collapse? Let\u8217\'20\'19s study the charts of the top 10 cryptocurrencies to find out.\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Bitcoin reversed direction from the downtrend line on May 29, indicating that the bears continue to sell near crucial resistance levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/b048a3c1-eb82-4518-98dd-815115e355e2.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The flattish 20-day exponential moving average (EMA) of $27,273 and the relative strength index (RSI) just below the midpoint do not give a clear advantage either to the bulls or the bears. If the price sustains below the 20-day EMA, the BTC/USDT pair could drop to the $25,250 support.\par \par \uc2 Buyers are expected to defend the zone between $24,000 and $25,250 with all their might because if it cracks, the pair may nosedive to $20,000.\par \par \uc2 On the upside, the bulls will have to surmount the downtrend line to signal the start of a new up move. The pair may first rise to $30,000 and later to $31,000.\par \par \uc2 Ether price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls are struggling to maintain Ether ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ethereum-price"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ETH}}}\uc2  ) above the 50-day simple moving average (SMA) of $1,883. This suggests a lack of demand at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/aec0728a-fe20-4f8a-8de3-aef2e4a67761.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 ETH/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to sink the price back into the falling wedge pattern and trap the aggressive bulls. If that happens, the ETH/USDT pair may fall to $1,762 and then to the support line of the wedge.\par \par \uc2 Conversely, if the price rebounds off the resistance line of the wedge, it will suggest that the bears have flipped the level into support. The pair may then rise to the psychological resistance at $2,000 and subsequently to $2,142.\par \par \uc2 BNB price analysis\par \par \uc2 BNB ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/binance-coin-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 BNB}}}\uc2  ) climbed and closed above the 20-day EMA ($311) on May 28, but the bulls could not continue the momentum and challenge the 50-day SMA ($319).\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/a84a25d5-ae12-426b-a329-ea35e109a12b.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 BNB/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears used the opportunity and pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA on May 31. Sellers will try to retest the psychological support at $300. If this level gives way, the BNB/USDT pair may descend to the support line.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price rebounds off $300, it will suggest that lower levels are attracting buyers. That may keep the pair inside the upper half of the channel for a few more days. A new up move could begin after bulls kick the price above the channel.\par \par \uc2 XRP price analysis\par \par \uc2 XRP\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/xrp-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 XRP}}}\uc2  ) rally is facing profit-booking near the overhead resistance of $0.54. The first support is at the 38.2% Fibonacci retracement level of $0.49 and then at the 50% retracement level of $0.48.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/b1c7e4ea-afc0-481f-bc1f-ad96ae670d57.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 XRP/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off this support zone, it will suggest that the sentiment has changed from selling on rallies to buying on dips. That will enhance the prospects of a rally above $0.54. The XRP/USDT pair may then rise to $0.58.\par \par \uc2 Contrarily, if the price breaks below $0.48, it will suggest that the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  momentum has weakened. That could tug the price to the moving averages and keep the price stuck inside the range for a few more days.\par \par \uc2 Cardano price analysis\par \par \uc2 Cardano ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ada-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22ADA\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  ) turned down from the 50-day SMA ($0.38) on May 29, indicating that the bears are protecting this level aggressively.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/7515f640-9712-407d-9e7d-4bf8f333eebe.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The sellers will try to pull the price below the uptrend line. This is an important level for the buyers to defend because a break below it will invalidate the \b \highlight22\uc2 bullish\b0 \highlight\uc2  ascending triangle pattern. That could then start a downswing to $0.30.\par \par \uc2 Alternatively, if the price turns up from the current level or the uptrend line, it will suggest that bulls are buying on dips. The bulls will then make one more attempt to thrust the price above the 50-day SMA. If they can pull it off, the \b \highlight22\uc2 ADA\b0 \highlight\uc2 /USDT pair may surge toward the $0.42 to $0.44 resistance zone.\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin price analysis\par \par \uc2 Dogecoin\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/doge-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOGE}}}\uc2  ) recovery stalled at the 20-day EMA ($0.07), indicating that the sentiment remains negative and relief rallies are being sold into.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/7a0e47f7-f936-4d87-bbb5-56762d28ea6a.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOGE/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears will try to strengthen their position by yanking the price below the immediate support at $0.07. If they manage to do that, the DOGE/USDT pair may start its journey toward the next support at $0.06.\par \par \uc2 Time is running out for the bulls. If they want to start a recovery, they will have to quickly drive the price above the 20-day EMA. The pair could then rally to the overhead resistance of $0.08. A break above this level will suggest that the bulls are on a comeback.\par \par \uc2 Polygon price analysis\par \par \uc2 Polygon\u8217\'20\'19s ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polygon-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 MATIC}}}\uc2  ) recovery fizzled out near the overhead resistance at $0.94, indicating that the bears are not willing to let go of their advantage.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/78a770e3-06f0-445f-a293-296d3bda9041.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 MATIC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears are trying to sustain the price below the 20-day EMA ($0.90). If they do that, the MATIC/USDT pair could drop to the vital support at $0.82. This remains the key level to watch out for on the downside because if it cracks, the selling may intensify and the pair is likely to plunge to $0.69.\par \par \uc2 The first sign of strength will be a break and close above the 50-day SMA ($0.96). Such a move will open the doors for a possible rally to the downtrend line.\par \par \uc2 Related: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/news/bitcoin-hodlers-exited-capitulation-above-20k-new-metric-hints"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bitcoin hodlers exited \u8216\'20\'18capitulation\u8217\'20\'19 above $20K, new metric hints}}}\par \par \uc2 Solana price analysis\par \par \uc2 Solana ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/solana-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 SOL}}}\uc2  ) has been stuck between the moving averages for the past four days. This suggests that the bulls are buying the dips to the 20-day EMA ($20.50) but the bears remain active at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/f833463f-e2a5-4fd4-90cd-5d65e2772243.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 SOL/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The 20-day EMA is flattish and the RSI is near the midpoint, indicating range-bound action in the near term. If the price dips below the 20-day EMA, the SOL/USDT pair could slide to the solid support at $18.70. A bounce off this level will suggest a consolidation between $18.70 and the 50-day SMA.\par \par \uc2 If the price bounces off the 20-day EMA, the bulls will again try to overcome the obstacle at the 50-day SMA. If they succeed, the pair could start a rally to $24 and then to $27.12.\par \par \uc2 Polkadot price analysis\par \par \uc2 The bulls pushed Polkadot ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/polkadot-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DOT}}}\uc2  ) above the 20-day EMA ($5.40) on May 28, but they could not build upon this breakout. This shows that demand dries up at higher levels.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/b824195b-8db1-40e9-b7c5-effc5cb001a5.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 DOT/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The bears have pulled the price back below the 20-day EMA. Sellers will next try to yank the price below the critical support at $5.15. If they manage to do that, the DOT/USDT pair could start a downward move toward $4.22.\par \par \uc2 If the price rebounds off $5.15, it will suggest that bulls continue to defend this level aggressively. The pair could then consolidate between $5.15 and $5.56 for a few more days. The bulls will gain the upper hand in the short term if they clear the 50-day SMA ($5.74).\par \par \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  price analysis\par \par \uc2 The price action of the past few weeks has formed a symmetrical triangle pattern in \uc2 Litecoin\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://cointelegraph.com/ltc-price-index"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 LTC}}}\uc2  ). This indicates indecision among the bulls and the bears about the next directional move.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/09c7810f-f0b9-4d66-bf2e-7d6112b84432.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 LTC/USDT daily chart. Source: TradingView\par \par \uc2 The price action inside a triangle is generally random and volatile. If the price sustains below the moving averages, the LTC/USDT pair could drop to the uptrend line. This line is likely to attract buying from the bulls.\par \par \uc2 Another possibility is that the price turns up from the moving averages. In that case, the pair will attempt to rise to the resistance line. A break and close above this level will indicate the start of a new up move. The pattern target of this setup is $142.\par \par \uc2 This article does not contain investment advice or recommendations. Every investment and trading move involves risk, and readers should conduct their own research when making a decision.\par \par \uc2 This article is for general information purposes and is not intended to be and should not be taken as legal or investment advice. The views, thoughts, and opinions expressed here are the author\u8217\'20\'19s alone and do not necessarily reflect or represent the views and opinions of Cointelegraph.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://images.cointelegraph.com/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,onerror=redirect,quality=90,width=840/https://s3.cointelegraph.com/uploads/2023-05/391b724f-4b3b-4d0b-b8b4-f8bf6c4be031.jpg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click to view image.}}}\par \par \uc2 Document CONTEL0020230531ej5v000e7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw40\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal600\pichgoal600
